E["item:andron-s-ledger"] = {t="item",n="Andron's Ledger",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Andron Gant's ledger draws the Deathstalkers' attention. They seek it as an operative gathers information for the Forsaken.",h="In the Undercity, Andron Gant's ledger draws the Deathstalkers' attention.",sec={{t="Uncovering the Syndicate",b="Andron Gant's bookshelf in the Undercity holds a ledger the Deathstalkers did not expect to find. Its pages reveal that the Syndicate, remnants of Alterac's fallen human nobility, is maneuvering in the region. Deathstalker Mennet Carkad sees the value at once: Alterac's ruined lords are scheming again. The ledger gives Forsaken leadership proof of Syndicate operations beyond what the Deathstalkers expected to find.",sp=1},{t="A Matter for the Dreadlord",b="Mennet Carkad sends the bearer straight to Varimathras in the Royal Quarter with the ledger, since it concerns threats to the Forsaken realm. Varimathras, Sylvanas Windrunner's dreadlord majordomo, oversees internal security and espionage through the Deathstalkers. He commends the ledger, recognizing the Deathstalker network's competence and the reliability of the operative who brought it to light.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Andron's Ledger?",a="Andron's Ledger is a record book from Andron Gant's bookshelf in the Undercity, with intelligence the Deathstalkers seek.",al={"androns ledger","what is this book","andron ledger"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Andron Gant?",a="Andron Gant is a Forsaken who keeps a shop near the Apothecarium in the Undercity. Lord Varimathras suspected he was secretly aiding an outside group, so the Deathstalkers sent an agent posing as Andron's expected messenger to obtain the ledger.",al={"who is andron","andron gant"},it="people"},{q="Why do the Deathstalkers want the ledger?",a="Mennet Carkad wants to examine Andron's information for intelligence useful to the Forsaken.",al={"why ledger matters","why deathstalkers want ledger"},it="ties"},{q="Who receives the ledger?",a="The ledger goes first to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter. After evaluating its contents, he directs the bearer to deliver it straight to Lord Varimathras in the Hall of the Dark Lady.",al={"who gets androns ledger","who do i bring the ledger to"},it="target"},{q="What does delivering the ledger achieve for a rogue?",a="Delivering the ledger earns the operative formal induction into the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken's secretive assassin guild.",al={"deathstalker induction","joining deathstalkers"},it="for_you"},{q="Where did Andron's Ledger come from?",a="The ledger belongs to Andron Gant, an informant residing in the Undercity who keeps detailed records of his covert dealings. It rests on a bookshelf in his quarters until retrieved by an operative on behalf of the Deathstalkers.",al={"who made androns ledger","androns ledger origin","where did the ledger come from"},it="origin",add="83ea0415"},{q="Why do the Deathstalkers want Andron's Ledger?",a="Mennet Carkad and the Deathstalkers seek the ledger for intelligence about threats to the Forsaken. Mennet examines its contents before sending it to Lord Varimathras.",al={"why is androns ledger wanted","who wants androns ledger","why does mennet carkad want the ledger"},sp=1,it="why_wanted",add="45ae6031"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, retrieving and deciphering Andron's Ledger proves your worth. Mennet Carkad formally inducts you into the Deathstalkers, and Varimathras acknowledges your work.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see how the Forsaken gather intelligence on threats around their new realm."},kw={"alterac","andron gant","andron's ledger","deathstalkers","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","syndicate","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1886","quest:1885","npc:varimathras","subzone:rogues-quarter","topic:syndicate","topic:alterac-kingdom","zone:undercity","topic:rogue"},src={"Andron's Ledger","The Deathstalkers (3)","The Deathstalkers (4)"}}
E["item:astor-s-letter-of-introduction"] = {t="item",n="Astor's Letter of Introduction",z="undercity",s="Astor Hadren carries a letter between Silverpine Forest and the Undercity. Deathstalkers use it to pose as the courier and investigate Andron Gant, a shopkeeper suspected of leaking Forsaken intelligence.",h="Astor Hadren carries a letter between Silverpine Forest and the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Courier's Credentials",b="Astor Hadren carries messages between Silverpine Forest and the Undercity. His letter of introduction gives its bearer credentials with illicit contacts in the city. Mennet Carkad, a Deathstalker handler, needs to investigate suspicious leaks in the Undercity, and Astor's travels make him a target. An operative can eliminate Astor and take his papers, then assume his identity and intercept the covert messages meant for him.",sp=0},{t="The Sting at the Apothecarium",b="Mennet Carkad uses the recovered letter to deceive Andron Gant, a shopkeeper near the Apothecarium. Lord Varimathras suspects Gant of leaking Forsaken intelligence to an unknown third party. An undercover operative presents the letter as the expected contact. Gant trusts the bearer, giving the operative a chance to learn who his conspirators are and find proof of his treason.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Astor's Letter of Introduction used for?",a="Mennet Carkad uses Astor's letter to fool the shopkeeper Andron Gant. The bearer poses as courier Astor Hadren to uncover Gant's secret dealings.",al={"purpose of the letter","what does the letter do","astors letter use"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who was Astor Hadren?",a="Astor Hadren was an emissary and messenger who carried private correspondence along the roads between Silverpine Forest and the Undercity. Deathstalker agents intercepted him.",al={"who is astor","astor hadren lore","who had the letter"},it="people"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad want this letter?",a="Mennet Carkad needs the letter to test recruits seeking to join the Deathstalkers and to run a sting against Andron Gant, whom Lord Varimathras suspects of treason.",al={"why does mennet need it","carkad's plan"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Does Andron Gant suspect the letter is stolen?",a="No. Mennet says Gant lacks the wit to suspect foul play, and Gant accepts the bearer as the regular messenger sent by his conspirators.",al={"does gant notice","does andron get tricked"},sp=1},{q="What is Astor's Letter of Introduction?",a="It is a credential carried by Astor Hadren, a traveling courier journeying between Silverpine Forest and the Undercity. The document identifies its bearer as an expected go-between to Andron Gant, an Undercity merchant suspected of collaborating with an unknown external faction.",al={"what is astor's letter","astor letter of introduction","what is this letter"},it="identity",add="da9b0b54"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Forsaken rogue, you can use Astor's letter in a field exercise for entry into the Deathstalkers. It tests assassination, theft, and impersonation.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you can see the Undercity's internal paranoia in this scheme. Lord Varimathras uses the Deathstalkers to root out subversion among the Forsaken."},kw={"andron gant","apothecarium","astor hadren","deathstalkers","mennet carkad","silverpine forest","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1886","npc:andron-gant","npc:varimathras","subzone:rogues-quarter","subzone:apothecarium","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity"},src={"Astor's Letter of Introduction","The Deathstalkers","The Deathstalkers (2)"}}
E["item:balnir-snapdragons"] = {t="item",n="Balnir Snapdragons",z="undercity",s="At Balnir Farmstead, vibrant snapdragons grow where the Scourge's corruption presses toward Tirisfal Glades. The Forsaken study their sensitivity to magic to watch for that corruption's spread.",h="At Balnir Farmstead, vibrant snapdragons grow where the Scourge's corruption presses toward Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Bloom in Ruin",b="Balnir Snapdragons still bloom in the garden of Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal Glades. The homestead lies in ruin after the fall of Lordaeron and the rise of the Scourge. The Plaguelands border Tirisfal to the east, and the garden sits where the Lich King's blight presses against the region. Its flowers give the Forsaken a place to watch for the spread of that corruption.",sp=0},{t="Magical Barometers",b="Balnir Snapdragons are unusually sensitive to atmospheric magic, making them living barometers for magical blights. Anastasia Hartwell and the Forsaken mages in the Undercity seek fresh flowers from the farmstead's window boxes. They send the plants to the Royal Apothecary Society for study, hoping to measure how far the Lich King's plague has seeped across the border into Tirisfal's soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Balnir Snapdragons be found?",a="Balnir Snapdragons grow in flower boxes and garden beds around the ruined Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal Glades, near the Western Plaguelands.",al={"balnir snapdragons location","where are the flowers","balnir flower location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell want these snapdragons?",a="Anastasia Hartwell wants fresh snapdragons sent to Undercity apothecaries. Their sensitivity to latent magical energies can help measure whether the Plaguelands' taint is spreading into Tirisfal Glades.",al={"why collect snapdragons","balnir farmstead quest goal","anastasia hartwell snapdragons"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who originally grew these flowers?",a="Balnir Snapdragons grow in the garden of Balnir Farmstead, the family homestead that gives them their name. The Scourge ruined the farm along with the rest of Lordaeron's countryside.",al={"who planted balnir snapdragons","balnir family snapdragons"},it="origin"},{q="Did the Scourge destroy the Balnir flowers?",a="No. Snapdragons still grow in the garden of Balnir Farmstead. Their growth so close to the Plaguelands lets Anastasia Hartwell's researchers study whether the plague has entered Tirisfal Glades.",al={"did plague kill snapdragons"},it="history"},{q="What are Balnir Snapdragons?",a="Balnir Snapdragons are a distinctive breed of flower grown in the garden boxes of the Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal Glades. Naturally sensitive and exceptionally receptive to magical energies, they absorb latent magical currents from their surroundings, making them prime indicators for detecting nearby environmental corruption.",al={"what is balnir snapdragons","balnir snapdragon flower","balnir snapdragons lore"},it="identity",add="ebe2752a"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Forsaken mage, you can study Balnir Snapdragons as conduits for magic. Their sensitivity helps measure how magical blights distort ambient leylines.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can use the flowers to watch your eastern border. Their readings can warn Undercity researchers if the Lich King's corruption is overtaking Tirisfal's soil."},kw={"anastasia hartwell","balnir farmstead","balnir snapdragons","mage quarter","plaguelands","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:balnir-farmstead","quest:1882","npc:anastasia-hartwell","zone:tirisfal","zone:undercity","subzone:mage-quarter","topic:forsaken","topic:lich-king"},src={"Balnir Snapdragons","The Balnir Farmstead"}}
E["item:berard-s-journal"] = {t="item",n="Berard's Journal",z="undercity",s="In Pyrewood Village, Berard's Journal holds research the Royal Apothecary Society needs. Berard studied an ancient plague that wiped out the aquatic life of Lake Lordamere.",h="In Pyrewood Village, Berard's Journal holds research the Royal Apothecary Society needs.",sec={{t="Lost Research of Lake Lordamere",b="Before Arugal's shadow magic spread across Silverpine Forest, Apothecary Berard was one of the Royal Apothecary Society's most promising minds. From Pyrewood Village, he studied an ancient blight that had wiped out all aquatic life in Lake Lordamere centuries earlier. When Arugal's curse gripped the settlement, Berard lost his mind and became a thrall. His detailed field notes remained on a bookshelf in his quarters at the Pyrewood Village Inn.",sp=0},{t="Fuel for the New Plague",b="Berard's research survived, though Berard himself was lost to the Society. At the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel recognizes its value and sends Forsaken agents into the hostile village to recover the journal. The notes on the ancient lake toxin give Master Apothecary Faranell and the Society in the Apothecarium groundwork for concocting the Forsaken's own new plague.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Apothecary Berard?",a="Apothecary Berard was a gifted member of the Royal Apothecary Society who lived in Pyrewood Village. He studied ancient toxins when Archmage Arugal cursed the region, breaking Berard's mind and enslaving him.",al={"who is berard","berard lore","apothecary berard"},it="people"},{q="Where is Berard's Journal found?",a="Berard's Journal rests on a bookshelf in his old study, on the upper floor of the inn in Pyrewood Village, deep in southern Silverpine Forest.",al={"find berards journal","journal location","where is the book"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What research is recorded in the journal?",a="The journal records Berard's findings on an ancient contagion that wiped out all aquatic life in Lake Lordamere. The Royal Apothecary Society hopes to adapt its toxic properties for their own chemical weapons.",al={"what is in the journal","berards research","journal contents"},it="power"},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel want the journal?",a="Apothecary Renferrel wants to recover useful research before it is destroyed or lost. Berard's findings on the Lake Lordamere contagion provide components Master Apothecary Faranell needs in Undercity to develop the Forsaken's new plague.",al={"why does renferrel want it","renferrel journal quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Berard's Journal?",a="Berard's Journal is a scientific research notebook compiled by Apothecary Berard, a former member of the Royal Apothecary Society. It contains his detailed findings regarding an ancient contagion that wiped out all aquatic life in Lake Lordamere long ago, which the Forsaken hope to study for their own alchemy.",al={"berard journal","what is berards journal","berards journal"},it="identity",add="b3a0b77c"},{q="Where does Berard's Journal come from, and who made it?",a="The journal was authored by Apothecary Berard prior to losing his mind to Archmage Arugal's shadow magic. He kept his study in the inn within Pyrewood Village, where the tome was left behind on a bookshelf after he became a mindless thrall.",al={"where is berards journal from","who wrote berard journal","berards journal origin"},it="origin",add="719e9fe0"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, every scrap of venomous lore helps the Royal Apothecary Society secure a weapon to defend the Forsaken against the Scourge and living enemies.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, reclaiming lost research in Pyrewood Village helps the Forsaken build a firm defensive stronghold across Silverpine Forest."},kw={"apothecary berard","apothecary renferrel","berard's journal","lake lordamere","master apothecary faranell","pyrewood village","royal apothecary society","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:447","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:pyrewood-village","topic:royal-apothecary-society","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:arugal","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher"},src={"Berard's Journal","A Recipe For Death (2)"}}
E["item:cantation-of-manifestation"] = {t="item",n="Cantation of Manifestation",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Anastasia Hartwell gives apprentices a scroll to reveal unseen magical beings in Algernon's shop.",h="In the Undercity, Anastasia Hartwell gives apprentices a scroll to reveal unseen magical beings in Algernon's...",sec={{t="Unveiling the Invisible",b="The Cantation of Manifestation reveals beings hidden by magic. Anastasia Hartwell keeps the scroll in the Magic Quarter and entrusts it to capable mages sent to contain rogue magical anomalies. Read aloud where arcane instability troubles the air, such as Algernon's alchemical workshop in the Apothecarium, its words force stray rift spawns into sight. The caster can then subdue them and trap them in containment coffers for further study.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the Cantation of Manifestation do?",a="The Cantation of Manifestation reveals invisible arcane anomalies. Recited where magical tears or disturbances trouble an area, it forces unseen creatures such as rift spawns into sight so you can fight and capture them.",al={"what is cantation of manifestation","cantation purpose","how does cantation work"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Where can I find the Cantation in Undercity?",a="You can find the Cantation on the floor directly behind Anastasia Hartwell, the mage trainer in the Undercity's Magic Quarter.",al={"cantation location undercity","where is cantation of manifestation","find cantation undercity"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell need this scroll used?",a="A strange magical disturbance broke out in Algernon's alchemical shop in the Apothecarium. Unseen beings made entirely of magic began wandering there, so Anastasia Hartwell needs you to read the scroll on site and reveal and capture them before the rift worsens.",al={"why use cantation","hartwell quest motive","anastasia disturbance"},it="motive"},{q="Do I get to keep the scroll after using it?",a="No. After you reveal the rift spawns and capture them in containment coffers, return the Cantation of Manifestation and the coffers to Anastasia Hartwell.",al={"keep cantation","do i lose cantation","return cantation"},gp=true},{q="What is the Cantation of Manifestation?",a="The Cantation of Manifestation is a specialized arcane scroll utilized by mages. When invoked, its incantation pierces magical concealment, forcing invisible entities woven purely of arcane energy to reveal themselves to the naked eye.",al={"what is cantation of manifestation","cantation of manifestation scroll","what does cantation do"},it="identity",add="1a839123"},{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell want the Cantation of Manifestation?",a="Invisible magical creatures have appeared around Algernon's shop in the Apothecarium, signaling a rift in the flow of magic. Mage trainers need the cantation read so an apprentice can reveal and capture the entities for study, allowing Undercity's magi to determine whether this disturbance is an accident or an active magical attack.",al={"why want cantation","why need cantation of manifestation","why does anastasia want cantation"},it="why_wanted",add="f236f2b5"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you use the Cantation of Manifestation in your early training to detect hidden arcane currents and contain volatile rift entities.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know Forsaken spellcasters in the Magic Quarter keep close watch over arcane fluctuations so magical rifts do not threaten the Undercity's stability."},kw={"algernon","anastasia hartwell","apothecarium","cantation of manifestation","containment coffer","magic quarter","rift spawn","undercity"},rel={"npc:anastasia-hartwell","quest:1960","subzone:magic-quarter","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","topic:mage","item:chest-of-containment-coffers","item:filled-containment-coffer"},src={"Cantation of Manifestation","Investigate the Alchemist Shop"}}
E["item:chest-of-containment-coffers"] = {t="item",n="Chest of Containment Coffers",z="undercity",s="Mages in the Undercity keep the Chest of Containment Coffers close at hand. Its enchanted vessels can secure unstable magical phenomena.",h="Mages in the Undercity keep the Chest of Containment Coffers close at hand.",sec={{t="Vessels for the Unseen",b="Invisible arcane creatures can emerge from experiments or sudden rifts between planes. Ordinary cages cannot hold beings made of magic. The Chest of Containment Coffers holds enchanted vessels that bind subdued creatures alive. Senior instructors keep the chest nearby, including Anastasia Hartwell in the Undercity and Jennea Cannon in Stormwind. They give initiates the coffers for surveying anomalies before those forces can unsettle their surroundings.",sp=0},{t="Arcane Containment Protocols",b="Invisible disturbances appeared in Algernon's shop in the Apothecarium, and Forsaken instructors sent mages with coffers to contain them. A mage first reveals a rift entity with a special scroll, then weakens it with spells and traps it in a coffer from the chest. Forsaken researchers can safely dissect and study the captured creatures, determining whether the disturbances were random tears in the Ley or deliberate arcane assaults.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside the Chest of Containment Coffers?",a="The chest holds empty, enchanted coffers. Mages use them to secure and trap subdued magical creatures, such as rift spawns, during dangerous field investigations.",al={"what does the chest give","containment coffers contents","chest contents"},it="item"},{q="Where can this chest be found?",a="In the Undercity, the chest sits behind Mage Trainer Anastasia Hartwell in the Magic Quarter. A matching chest is behind Jennea Cannon in the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind City.",al={"chest of containment coffers location","where is containment coffers chest","coffer chest location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do mages need these coffers instead of normal cages?",a="Rift spawns are made of intangible arcane energy, which ordinary materials cannot hold. Enchanted coffers can trap and stabilize these anomalies.",al={"why use coffers","what are coffers for","how do coffers work"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens to the coffers once they are filled?",a="Senior instructors receive filled coffers for study. Researchers analyze the captured creatures to determine whether a disturbance came from an accidental natural rift or an intentional attack by outside forces.",al={"what happens to captured rift spawns","filled containment coffer use","why capture creatures"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Chest of Containment Coffers?",a="It is a heavy supply chest kept by mage instructors to outfit practitioners investigating magical anomalies. Inside rests a set of enchanted containment coffers specially constructed to bind and hold erratic, non-physical beings composed purely of arcane energy.",al={"what is chest of containment coffers","chest of containment coffers","chest of coffers"},it="identity",add="fa57c13a"},{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell want you to take the Chest of Containment Coffers?",a="Anastasia Hartwell has detected invisible magical entities wandering Algernon's alchemist shop in the Apothecarium. Ordinary restraints cannot touch creatures woven entirely of raw magic, so she provides you with this chest of specially prepared coffers to capture the anomalies alive for study.",al={"why take the chest of containment coffers","why do i need containment coffers","why anastasia chest of coffers"},it="why_wanted",add="c9b5ba3b"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can use these field tools to manage volatile arcane manifestations and preserve living specimens for study.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can use these coffers to secure magical anomalies near the Apothecarium, keeping unvetted arcane forces from corrupting your work."},kw={"anastasia hartwell","apothecarium","arcane anomaly","containment coffer","magic quarter","rift spawn"},rel={"quest:1960","npc:anastasia-hartwell","item:filled-containment-coffer","item:cantation-of-manifestation","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","npc:jennea-cannon","topic:mage"},src={"Chest of Containment Coffers","Investigate the Alchemist Shop"}}
E["item:comar-s-heart"] = {t="item",n="Comar's Heart",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, warlocks seek Comar's Heart to draw a succubus into their service. The heart belonged to Comar Villard, a human searching the Wetlands for his lost wife.",h="In the Undercity, warlocks seek Comar's Heart to draw a succubus into their service.",sec={{t="A Beacon of Purity",b="Comar Villard keeps searching the Wetlands for his lost wife. Though turmoil has swept the Eastern Kingdoms, he refuses to abandon the search. Carendin Halgar's disciples in the Undercity judge his fidelity among the rarest and purest. To bind a succubus, a creature both capricious and predatory, warlocks need devotion like his as bait. Comar's steadfast love marks him for slaughter, and his heart becomes the lure for a demonic servant.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Seduction",b="Forsaken apprentices must travel south through contested lands, cross the Thandol Span, and enter marshes held by the Alliance to claim Comar's Heart. They carry it back to the Temple of the Damned with Dalin's Heart. The organ looks ordinary, though goodness once drove the man it belonged to. To the Nether, the virtue left in Comar's flesh is intoxicating bait. It can draw a succubus across the dimensional veil and into a warlock's thrall.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Comar Villard?",a="Comar Villard was a devoted human who searched the dangerous Wetlands for his missing wife. He would not give up hope, and his love marked him as a pure-hearted man.",al={"who is comar","comar villard lore","why kill comar"},it="identity"},{q="Why do warlocks need Comar's Heart?",a="Warlocks of the Undercity need Comar's Heart to lure and bind a succubus. His devotion makes the heart irresistible bait for the demon.",al={"why need comar heart","what is comars heart for","succubus heart lore"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Comar Villard found?",a="Comar Villard wanders the main road in the northern Wetlands, just south of the Thandol Span between Arathi Highlands and Khaz Modan.",al={"comar villard location","where is comar","how to find comar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who sends warlocks to collect the heart?",a="Warlock trainers in the Undercity direct apprentices to collect the heart. Carendin Halgar oversees them in the Temple of the Damned, where the apprentices learn to summon a succubus.",al={"who wants comar heart","who gives hearts of the pure","carendin halgar heart"},it="motive"},{q="What is Comar's Heart?",a="Comar's Heart is the literal heart carved from Comar Villard, a faithful human wanderer in the Wetlands. Warlocks prize it as a rare specimen of untainted virtue, steeped in fidelity and enduring love.",al={"what is comars heart","comar heart item","comar's heart lore"},it="item",add="7acb4df8"},{q="Where does Comar's Heart come from?",a="It is taken directly from the chest of Comar Villard, a man searching the treacherous marshes of the Wetlands for any trace of his lost wife. It is not an artifact forged by sorcery, but a mortal organ whose pure devotion makes it a potent ritual reagent.",al={"where does comars heart come from","who made comars heart","origin of comars heart"},it="origin",add="a49b76cf"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, taking Comar's Heart shows how demonology turns mortal virtue into bait for a succubus you mean to bind.",["race:Undead"]="As one of the Forsaken, harvesting the heart of a loyal human lover shows the emotional severance between the living and the undead in Lordaeron."},kw={"carendin halgar","comar villard","comar's heart","hearts of the pure","succubus","temple of the damned","undercity","wetlands"},rel={"quest:1476","item:dalin-s-heart","npc:carendin-halgar","zone:wetlands","subzone:thandol-span","zone:arathi"},src={"Comar's Heart","Hearts of the Pure"}}
E["item:daggerspine-scale"] = {t="item",n="Daggerspine Scale",z="undercity",s="Along Hillsbrad Foothills' southern shores, Daggerspine Scale comes from tough reptilian scales harvested from prowling Daggerspine naga. The Royal Apothecary Society seeks them to activate virulent brews in the Forsaken's ongoing plague experiments.",h="Along Hillsbrad Foothills' southern shores, Daggerspine Scale comes from tough reptilian scales harvested...",sec={{t="Apothecary Research",b="The Royal Apothecary Society seeks reagents for its toxins, plagues, and concoctions. While refining the experimental Elixir of Agony, its apothecaries found that scales from the local Daggerspine naga react in a useful way. Combined with troll regenerative elixirs and murloc organs, the scales chemically activate dormant contaminating agents suspended in raw mixtures. Gathering them means hunting along the rocky coastline east of Southshore, near both the vicious naga tribe and Alliance forces. The apothecaries need these scales for their research.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Daggerspine Scales used for?",a="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill gathers Daggerspine Scales for research into the Elixir of Agony. Combined with other reagents, they activate the contaminating properties of an alchemical mudsnout mixture.",al={"daggerspine scale use","why get daggerspine scales","what do daggerspine scales do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do these scales come from?",a="Daggerspine Scales come from Daggerspine naga along the Hillsbrad Foothills coastline directly east of Southshore. Their source includes shorestalkers, shorehunters, screamers, sirens, and their leader, Lady Zephris.",al={"where to find daggerspine scales","who drops daggerspine scales","daggerspine scale location"},it="origin"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society want naga scales?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society wants Daggerspine Scales because their resilient scales have the chemical properties needed to trigger specific infectious agents in experimental blight and disease concoctions.",al={"why naga scales","apothecary naga scales"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is a Daggerspine Scale?",a="A Daggerspine Scale is a tough, aquatic scale harvested from the Daggerspine naga prowling the coast of Hillsbrad Foothills. These serpent-like creatures possess unique biological properties that make their shed and harvested scales prized reagents for the sinister concoctions of the Royal Apothecary Society.",al={"what are daggerspine scales","daggerspine scale item","about daggerspine scale"},it="identity",add="8e2c4377"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, gathering these scales advances the Royal Apothecary Society's research into devastating new plagues against the Forsaken's enemies.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you must navigate carefully along the southern shore, where Daggerspine encampments lie dangerously close to the Alliance port of Southshore."},kw={"daggerspine","daggerspine scale","elixir of agony","hillsbrad","lydon","naga","royal apothecary society","undercity"},rel={"quest:509","topic:royal-apothecary-society","topic:naga","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","item:mudsnout-mixture","item:torn-fin-eye","npc:umpi"},src={"Daggerspine Scale","Elixir of Agony (3)"}}
E["item:dalaran-mana-gem"] = {t="item",n="Dalaran Mana Gem",z="undercity",s="Near Ambermill, Kirin Tor mages carry Dalaran Mana Gems to replenish their power. Forsaken tailors use the gems to weave enchanted robes.",h="Near Ambermill, Kirin Tor mages carry Dalaran Mana Gems to replenish their power.",sec={{t="Stolen Arcana",b="Kirin Tor mages, conjurors, and guards around Ambermill carry mana gems to focus and replenish their arcane power. In the Undercity’s Magic Quarter, Forsaken practitioners prize the gems as a ready supply of concentrated magic. Some undead mages share an academic heritage with Dalaran, but survival comes first. To the Forsaken, the Kirin Tor are rivals whose magical stores can be taken.",sp=0},{t="Weaving the Spellfire",b="Forsaken bring mana gems taken from fallen Kirin Tor operatives to tailors such as Josef Gregorian in the Undercity, along with simple linen. A tailor cannot channel arcane power directly, but can bind a gem into the cloth. The magic then strengthens the wearer’s connection to the arcane.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Dalaran Mana Gems come from?",a="Kirin Tor forces carry Dalaran Mana Gems in Silverpine Forest, especially around their encampments and outposts near Ambermill, southeast of the Sepulcher.",al={"where to farm mana gems","dalaran gem drop","who drops mana gems"},it="origin"},{q="What are these gems used for?",a="Forsaken mages bring the gems with linen to Josef Gregorian in the Undercity. He uses them to weave spellfire robes.",al={"mana gem purpose","why do i need dalaran mana gems"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the Kirin Tor in Silverpine carrying these gems?",a="Kirin Tor members carry mana gems as personal stores of arcane power. The gems sustain their spellcasting, defense wards, and conjurations in hostile Silverpine Forest.",al={"why do dalaran wizards have gems","kirin tor mana gems lore"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken target Dalaran mages for these gems?",a="Forsaken and Dalaran share an academic heritage, but the Forsaken see their living counterparts as rivals. Undercity mentors believe a mage who cannot defend their arcane wealth is too weak to survive, so they take the mage’s components.",al={"forsaken vs dalaran mages","why kill dalaran for robes"},it="motive"},{q="What is a Dalaran Mana Gem?",a="A Dalaran Mana Gem is a magically charged stone carried by the Kirin Tor operatives stationed in Silverpine Forest. Imbued with arcane energy, these crystals are essential components for crafting enchanted garments, such as the spellfire robes sewn by Forsaken tailors in the Undercity.",al={"what is dalaran mana gem","dalaran mana gem","mana gem silverpine"},it="identity",add="02094a76"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Forsaken mage, you are sent to take these gems as a rite of passage, proving your martial skill and mastery of harvested arcane power.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead traveler, you know the Forsaken set aside sentiment for former human colleagues in Dalaran to support their faction’s survival."},kw={"ambermill","dalaran mana gem","josef gregorian","kirin tor","linen","mana gem","silverpine forest","spellfire robes"},rel={"quest:1961","quest:1962","npc:josef-gregorian","subzone:ambermill","subzone:magic-quarter","subzone:dalaran","zone:silverpine","topic:mage"},src={"Dalaran Mana Gem","Gathering Materials (Horde)"}}
E["item:dalaran-status-report"] = {t="item",n="Dalaran Status Report",z="undercity",s="At Ambermill, the Kirin Tor watch Dalaran as the city is rebuilt in the open. Their report carries intelligence the Deathstalkers seek.",h="At Ambermill, the Kirin Tor watch Dalaran as the city is rebuilt in the open.",sec={{t="Eyes on the Rebuilding City",b="The Scourge sacked Dalaran, and Archimonde brought down its towering spires during the Third War. Early in the rebuilding, the surviving magi removed the city's protective shield and began their work in the open. The Kirin Tor also keeps enclaves such as Ambermill in southeastern Silverpine Forest. Its wizards compile the Dalaran Status Report, which holds intelligence about the city's condition and draws the Deathstalkers' attention.",sp=0},{t="A Deathstalker's Test",b="Lord Varimathras watches for remnants of the Alliance and Kirin Tor, guarding Forsaken control of Lordaeron with constant vigilance. After Forsaken interrogators forced admissions from a captured Kirin Tor mage, the dreadlord ordered the Deathstalkers to secure the report. The document lies in a locked strongbox deep inside Ambermill. For newly initiated rogues, retrieving it is also a rite of passage: a chance to master lockpicking under Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Dalaran Status Report?",a="The Dalaran Status Report is a set of confidential Kirin Tor documents about Dalaran's condition, recovery work, and current status. Mages at the Ambermill outpost compiled it.",al={"what is this report","dalaran report","ambermill documents"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the report kept?",a="The report is locked inside a strongbox in the Ambermill settlement in southeastern Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is the report","ambermill strongbox location","how to find the status report"},it="place"},{q="Why does the Undercity want this report?",a="Lord Varimathras and the Forsaken see the surviving Kirin Tor as an active threat on their doorstep. The report helps the Deathstalkers assess Dalaran's military strength and secret reconstruction work.",al={"why do forsaken want this","varimathras dalaran report","deathstalkers objective"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How did the Deathstalkers learn about the document?",a="The Deathstalkers learned of the document and its location from a captured Kirin Tor prisoner questioned in the Undercity.",al={"how did undercity find out","prisoner confession"},it="history"},{q="Where does the Dalaran Status Report come from, and who made it?",a="The report was drafted by the Kirin Tor wizards stationed at Ambermill in southern Silverpine Forest. Following the devastation of Dalaran during the Third War, the surviving mages maintain outposts throughout the surrounding regions to monitor their fallen city, document ongoing affairs, and coordinate their remaining forces.",al={"who wrote dalaran status report","dalaran status report origin","who made dalaran status report"},it="origin",add="f1fae308"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you prove your skill at lockpicking and infiltration under Mennet Carkad by retrieving the report from vigilant mages.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the Kirin Tor remnants at Ambermill trouble the Forsaken in Silverpine. Intelligence on their operations matters to Undercity's security."},kw={"ambermill","ambermill strongbox","dalaran status report","deathstalkers","kirin tor","mennet carkad","tools of the trade","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1999","subzone:ambermill","quest:1886","subzone:dalaran","npc:varimathras","zone:silverpine","subzone:rogues-quarter","topic:rogue"},src={"Dalaran Status Report","Tools of the Trade (Classic)"}}
E["item:dalin-s-heart"] = {t="item",n="Dalin's Heart",z="undercity",s="Near the Greymane Wall in Silverpine Forest, Dalin Forgewright patrols with an honorable heart.",h="Near the Greymane Wall in Silverpine Forest, Dalin Forgewright patrols with an honorable heart.",sec={{t="A Pure Heart for Dark Arts",b="Undercity warlocks seek hearts from truly virtuous mortals to call and bind a succubus to their service. Dalin Forgewright spends his days defending desperate Lordaeron refugees kept from safety by the sealed Greymane Wall. His selfless devotion marks him as a rare offering of unblemished purity, and his heart is carved for the rites held in the Temple of the Damned.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Dalin Forgewright?",a="Dalin Forgewright was an honorable human who protected Lordaeron refugees stranded outside the closed gates of the Greymane Wall in southern Silverpine Forest.",al={"dalin forgewright","who is dalin","dalin lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why do warlocks need Dalin's Heart?",a="Undercity warlocks use Dalin's Heart as a ritual lure to draw a succubus, then bind her to their service.",al={"why dalin heart","purpose of dalins heart","why do warlocks want dalin's heart"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who accepts Dalin's Heart?",a="Carendin Halgar, a warlock trainer in the Temple of the Damned within the Undercity, accepts Dalin's Heart.",al={"who takes the heart","dalin heart turn in","where to bring dalins heart"},it="target"},{q="What other component is needed alongside this heart?",a="Carendin Halgar requires Dalin's Heart and Comar's Heart. Comar Villard is a faithful husband wandering the Wetlands in search of his lost wife.",al={"hearts of the pure other heart","other heart needed","second heart"}},{q="What is Dalin's Heart?",a="It is the literal, physical heart cut from Dalin Forgewright, an honorable man tending to Lordaeron refugees near the Greymane Wall in Silverpine Forest. Though physically indistinguishable from any other human heart, it possesses the distinct spiritual purity of a selfless and virtuous soul.",al={"what is dalins heart","dalins heart description","dalin heart item"},it="item",add="5b5f5201"},{q="Where does Dalin's Heart come from?",a="The heart comes from Dalin Forgewright, a virtuous man who tends the Lordaeron refugees at the closed Greymane Wall in southern Silverpine Forest. A warlock must track him down and slay him to claim the organ directly from his corpse.",al={"where do you get dalins heart","dalins heart origin","who drops dalins heart"},it="origin",add="d7d2edf8"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Forsaken warlock, you undergo this rite of passage to learn to ensnare a succubus, harvesting untainted virtue for demonic mastery.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see the bitter reality of post-Scourge Lordaeron, where living human altruists outside the Greymane Wall become prey for the Forsaken."},kw={"carendin halgar","dalin forgewright","dalin's heart","greymane wall","hearts of the pure","silverpine forest","succubus","undercity"},rel={"quest:1476","item:comar-s-heart","npc:carendin-halgar","subzone:greymane-wall","zone:silverpine","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Dalin's Heart","Hearts of the Pure"}}
E["item:darthalia-s-sealed-commendation"] = {t="item",n="Darthalia's Sealed Commendation",z="undercity",s="At Tarren Mill, Darthalia sends word of victories against Hillsbrad's humans to Undercity's high command.",h="At Tarren Mill, Darthalia sends word of victories against Hillsbrad's humans to Undercity's high command.",sec={{t="Report to High Command",b="After the fighting across the Hillsbrad Foothills, High Executor Darthalia seals a dispatch recording victories against Hillsbrad's human defenders and the ruin of their positions. She addresses it to Varimathras, the dreadlord who advises Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. In the Royal Quarter, the report gives Forsaken leaders proof that Alliance enclaves south of Lordaeron can be broken, leaving northern garrisons free to face the Scourge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Darthalia's Sealed Commendation?",a="High Executor Darthalia of Tarren Mill writes a sealed commendation for a fighter's performance against the Alliance in the Battle of Hillsbrad. It is meant for Undercity's high command.",al={"sealed commendation","darthalia letter","hillsbrad report"},it="identity"},{q="Who receives this commendation?",a="The commendation is addressed to Varimathras, the dreadlord advisor to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner in Undercity's Royal Quarter.",al={"who do i bring this to","commendation turn in","who gets darthalia's commendation"},it="target"},{q="Why does Varimathras care about the fighting in Hillsbrad?",a="The Forsaken face the Lich King and his Scourge to the north, while humans in Hillsbrad disrupt their supply lines and southern border security. Varimathras values victories that remove that obstacle and let Undercity's forces focus on the greater war.",al={"why varimathras cares","hillsbrad dreadlord","forsaken strategy hillsbrad"},it="motive"},{q="Where does Darthalia's Sealed Commendation come from, and who made it?",a="This letter is written and sealed by Darthalia, a Forsaken commander coordinating Horde forces in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Recognizing your valor and relentless perseverance during the bitter campaign against the human settlements of Hillsbrad, she penned this official dispatch to personally praise your battlefield accomplishments to the high command.",al={"who wrote darthalia commendation","where did darthalia commendation come from","who gave sealed commendation"},it="origin",add="fd99e080"},{q="Why does Varimathras want Darthalia's Sealed Commendation?",a="Darthalia sends the document directly to Varimathras in the Undercity so the Forsaken leadership takes note of your deadly effectiveness. While the dreadlord views the Scourge to the north as the primary threat, Alliance humans in Hillsbrad disrupt their broader strategic plans. This commendation formally proves that decisive strikes against human settlements can succeed under capable field champions like you.",al={"why deliver sealed commendation","why does varimathras want commendation","purpose of darthalias commendation"},it="why_wanted",add="9dfe1fb6"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, the commendation records a strategic victory in Lordaeron and shows Undercity's leadership that Alliance strongholds in the southern foothills can be dismantled.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, earning Darthalia's praise and bringing the commendation to the throne room raises your standing in the Dark Lady's growing military hierarchy."},kw={"commendation","darthalia","hillsbrad","southshore","tarren mill","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"quest:527","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity","npc:varimathras","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:human","topic:lich-king"},src={"Darthalia's Sealed Commendation","Battle of Hillsbrad (7) (Classic)"}}
E["item:egalin-s-grimoire"] = {t="item",n="Egalin's Grimoire",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Egalin's Grimoire holds the rites for summoning and commanding a voidwalker. A master warlock wrote it as a teaching text for the Temple of the Damned.",h="In the Undercity, Egalin's Grimoire holds the rites for summoning and commanding a voidwalker.",sec={{t="A Master's Work",b="Egalin's Grimoire records how to call a being of chaos from the Nether. Egalin was a master summoner, renowned for his effortless command of voidwalkers. He passed that skill to his students, including Carendin Halgar. Without the formulas and channeling methods in the book, an unprepared summoner risks being torn apart by the being they call forth.",sp=0},{t="The Scarlet Theft",b="A Scarlet Crusade operative named Perrine stole the grimoire from the Forsaken warlocks and hid it in a chest in a tower in western Tirisfal Glades. The Crusade hated dark magic, yet Perrine seemed to know little of the book's true significance. The tome was treated as seized heretical salvage until Forsaken initiates seeking to master the void retrieved it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Egalin?",a="Egalin was a talented warlock who mentored Carendin Halgar. He was the first among them to summon a voidwalker and commanded chaotic entities with ease.",al={"who is egalin","egalin lore","who wrote the grimoire"},it="people"},{q="Why is Egalin's Grimoire so dangerous?",a="Egalin's Grimoire contains the incantations and channeling methods for summoning a voidwalker. A warlock who attempts the ritual without mastering these instructions risks being torn apart by the summoned void entity.",al={"what does the grimoire do","voidwalker tome danger","why dangerous"},it="danger"},{q="How did the Scarlet Crusade get the book?",a="A Scarlet Crusade agent named Perrine stole the tome from the Forsaken warlocks. He hid it in a chest at a Crusade watchtower in western Tirisfal Glades, seemingly unaware of its true magical worth.",al={"who stole the book","perrine grimoire","why do crusaders have it"},it="history"},{q="Who needs this grimoire returned?",a="Carendin Halgar, the warlock trainer in the Temple of the Damned beneath the Undercity, needs the grimoire to teach new initiates to summon and bind voidwalkers.",al={"who wants the grimoire","who turns in egalin grimoire","carendin halgar book"},it="target"},{q="What is Egalin's Grimoire?",a="Egalin's Grimoire is a musty, specialized spellbook containing the secrets of calling upon beings from the chaos beyond. Specifically, it details the intricate process and spell structure required to summon and bind a voidwalker—a creature capable of tearing an unprepared summoner apart.",al={"what is egalins grimoire","egalin book","what is the grimoire"},it="identity",add="cc7caae6"},{q="Where does Egalin's Grimoire come from, and who made it?",a="The tome was penned by Egalin, a master warlock celebrated among practitioners in the Undercity as the first to summon a voidwalker. Egalin taught other prominent warlocks, including Carendin Halgar, who revered his mentor's effortless command over summoned horrors.",al={"who wrote egalins grimoire","egalin book origin","who made egalins grimoire"},it="origin",add="29951967"},{q="Why is Egalin's Grimoire wanted?",a="The warlocks in the Temple of the Damned require the grimoire to instruct aspiring practitioners in summoning voidwalkers. After a Scarlet Crusade operative named Perrine stole it and hid it in a nearby tower, recovering the text became critical to keep its dangerous rituals out of enemy hands and return vital knowledge to the Forsaken.",al={"why do they want egalins grimoire","who wants the grimoire","why recover egalin book"},it="why_wanted",add="c5f2fef1"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can use Egalin's Grimoire to learn the techniques for summoning a voidwalker from the Nether and binding it to your will, a rite of passage for practitioners.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, recovering the book keeps the Scarlet Crusade from holding a powerful magical artifact stolen from the Undercity's practitioners."},kw={"carendin halgar","creature of the void","egalin","egalin's grimoire","perrine","temple of the damned","voidwalker"},rel={"quest:1473","npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1471","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:undercity","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Egalin's Grimoire","Creature of the Void (Undercity)"}}
E["item:fenwick-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Fenwick's Head",z="undercity",s="Forsaken rogues seek Fenwick Thatros along the shores of Lordamere Lake. His head is proof of his execution, claimed on orders passed down from Lord Varimathras.",h="Forsaken rogues seek Fenwick Thatros along the shores of Lordamere Lake.",sec={{t="A Contract from the Shadows",b="Mennet Carkad acts from the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity on urgent intelligence from dreadlord Varimathras. Fenwick Thatros, a hostile undead leader, has established a foothold near the decaying docks along Lordamere Lake in Silverpine Forest. To keep him from rallying hostile undead against the Forsaken, Carkad sends promising Deathstalkers to find and kill him, then bring back his head as proof.",sp=0},{t="A Rite of Passage",b="For Deathstalker operatives, bringing Fenwick's Head to Carkad is a trial beyond collecting a bounty. The severed head proves a rogue's skill in infiltration and assassination. Success opens the way to deeper, more specialized instruction in the shadow arts from Forsaken masters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Fenwick Thatros?",a="Lord Varimathras identified Fenwick Thatros as an undead leader entrenched in Silverpine Forest. Near the decrepit docks of Lordamere Lake, he posed an immediate danger to Forsaken interests in the region.",al={"who is fenwick","fenwick thatros lore","who was thatros"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants Fenwick's Head?",a="Mennet Carkad, a Deathstalker trainer in the Undercity's Rogues' Quarter, demands Fenwick's Head on an urgent order passed down from Lord Varimathras.",al={"who wants the head","who turned in to","mennet carkad"},it="target"},{q="Where is Fenwick Thatros located?",a="Deathstalker scouts place Fenwick Thatros by the decrepit docks on the shore of Lordamere Lake in Silverpine Forest.",al={"fenwick thatros location","where is fenwick","find fenwick"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why must his head be severed?",a="Mennet Carkad requires physical proof that the threat has been eliminated before advancing an operative to advanced shadow training.",al={"why take his head","why decapitate him"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does Fenwick's Head come from?",a="This severed head is taken from Fenwick Thatros, an undead leader encountered near the decaying docks along the shores of Lordamere Lake in Silverpine Forest. It is not an crafted object, but the grim remains of an enemy commander claimed in the field.",al={"fenwicks head origin","where do you get fenwicks head","who had fenwicks head"},it="origin",add="bc6d2652"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, claiming Fenwick's Head marks a rising Forsaken operative as a reliable Deathstalker and earns access to advanced training.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see the Forsaken ruthlessly suppress rival undead factions contesting control of Silverpine Forest and the shores of Lordamere Lake."},kw={"deathstalkers","fenwick","lordamere","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","silverpine","thatros","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1998","quest:1999","npc:varimathras","quest:1886","subzone:rogues-quarter","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity","topic:rogue"},src={"Fenwick's Head","Fenwick Thatros (quest)"}}
E["item:filled-containment-coffer"] = {t="item",n="Filled Containment Coffer",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Forsaken spellcasters use Filled Containment Coffers to capture erratic magical entities. A Cantation of Manifestation reveals and weakens rift spawn in the Apothecarium, so mages can seal them inside for examination.",h="In the Undercity, Forsaken spellcasters use Filled Containment Coffers to capture erratic magical entities.",sec={{t="Trapping the Unseen",b="Magical disturbances have appeared in Algernon's shop in the Apothecarium. The Forsaken mage Anastasia Hartwell has called on arcane practitioners to capture the entities behind them. Rift creatures are living magical energy and cannot be seen, so ordinary cages cannot hold them. Spellcasters reveal them with a Cantation of Manifestation, defeat them in combat, and snap prepared coffers shut around them. The sealed boxes protect their carriers from volatile magical backlashes and keep the creatures intact for magical dissection.",sp=0},{t="Arcane Forensics",b="Living mana creatures in the Undercity pose a serious threat. Once sealed inside containment coffers, the beasts are carried to Anastasia Hartwell and the city's scholars. Forsaken mages seek to learn whether the intrusions come from natural rifts in Azeroth's magical fabric or are preliminary probes in a calculated magical assault on the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside a Filled Containment Coffer?",a="Each coffer holds a captured rift spawn, an invisible creature of raw magical energy that appeared inside Algernon's alchemy shop in the Apothecarium.",al={"what is in the coffer","coffer contents","filled coffer monster"},it="item"},{q="How is a containment coffer filled?",a="A mage reads the Cantation of Manifestation to reveal the hidden creatures, defeats them in combat, then uses an empty coffer to trap the remaining energy before it dissipates.",al={"how to fill coffer","how do i capture the rift spawn","filling coffer"},gp=true},{q="Who wants these filled coffers in Undercity?",a="Anastasia Hartwell, a prominent mage trainer in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, asks for the sealed coffers to investigate the disturbance threatening the city.",al={"who takes the coffers","coffer quest giver","anastasia hartwell coffer"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are the Forsaken studying these creatures?",a="Undercity's scholars need to learn whether the anomaly came from a random tear in the local flow of magic or a deliberate, coordinated attack by a hostile magical force.",al={"why study rift spawn","undercity rift reason"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is a Filled Containment Coffer?",a="A Filled Containment Coffer is an enchanted container used by mages to trap and hold volatile beings made purely of magical energy, such as rift spawns. Once the creature is forced into visibility and subdued, the coffer secures it safely for transportation and study without letting its magical essence disperse.",al={"what is filled containment coffer","filled containment coffer","containment coffer item"},it="identity",add="d6cc8dac"},{q="Where does a Filled Containment Coffer come from, and who made it?",a="The empty coffers are specialized arcane devices provided by mage instructors such as Anastasia Hartwell in the Undercity. They become filled when an adept mage tracks down invisible magical entities—such as those lurking around Algernon's shop in the Apothecarium—forces them to manifest, weakens them, and seals them inside.",al={"who made containment coffer","origin of containment coffer","where do containment coffers come from"},it="origin",add="1e3ef013"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Forsaken apprentice, you handle containment coffers as a practical lesson in abjuration. You learn to reveal hidden magical entities and bind unstable arcane energy into physical wards.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know the Apothecarium's safety matters greatly to the Forsaken. Investigating and containing a mysterious magical breach is an urgent concern at home."},kw={"algernon","anastasia hartwell","apothecarium","arcane disturbance","cantation of manifestation","containment coffer","filled containment coffer","rift spawn"},rel={"quest:1960","npc:anastasia-hartwell","item:cantation-of-manifestation","item:chest-of-containment-coffers","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","topic:mage"},src={"Filled Containment Coffer","Investigate the Alchemist Shop"}}
E["item:gordon-s-crate"] = {t="item",n="Gordon's Crate",z="undercity",s="Weapons are bound for the Forsaken forces in Silverpine Forest, packed in Gordon's Crate in the Undercity. The shipment is meant for the remote garrison at the Sepulcher.",h="Weapons are bound for the Forsaken forces in Silverpine Forest, packed in Gordon's Crate in the Undercity.",sec={{t="Supplies for Silverpine",b="The Forsaken keep a steady flow of supplies from the Undercity to hold Silverpine Forest. Gordon's Crate carries weapons for Deathguard Podrig's defenders at the Sepulcher. The outpost sentries face worgen, wild beasts, and human remnants in the woods.",sp=0},{t="The Bat Handler's Route",b="Overland roads from the capital are dangerous and slow, so valuable shipments travel with the Undercity's bat handlers. Gordon's Crate is handed to Michael Garrett, the bat master above the city's trade quarter. He arranges passage on a trained flying bat to Karos Razok's roost back at the Sepulcher.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Gordon's Crate?",a="Gordon's Crate holds weapons and vital combat supplies requisitioned from the Undercity to reinforce Deathguard sentries in Silverpine Forest.",al={"contents of gordons crate","what does crate contain"},it="item"},{q="Who is supposed to receive Gordon's Crate?",a="Deathguard Podrig at the Sepulcher is meant to receive Gordon's Crate. Michael Garrett, an Undercity bat handler, arranges its flight.",al={"who gets gordons crate","where does crate go"},it="target"},{q="Why is the crate transported by bat instead of a courier on foot?",a="Silverpine Forest remains contested and hazardous. Trained bats overseen by Michael Garrett and Karos Razok carry shipments swiftly through the air, away from threats along the ground routes.",al={"why fly the crate","bat travel crate"}},{q="Why does Michael Garrett require you to visit the Sepulcher first?",a="Forsaken bats instinctively return to the capital. Before they can safely fly to an outlying base like the Sepulcher, you must first establish a connection with its local handler, Karos Razok.",al={"why need flight path","bat flight requirement"}},{q="What is Gordon's Crate?",a="Gordon's Crate is a shipment of vital weapons and military supplies packed in the Undercity. It is prepared specifically to be flown via bat handler to the remote Forsaken outpost at the Sepulcher.",al={"gordon's crate","what is this crate","gordons crate"},it="identity",add="df26763c"},{q="Where does Gordon's Crate come from, and who made it?",a="The crate originates in the Undercity, where Gordon packed the garrison supplies into it before arranging for its delivery to the bat handlers.",al={"where did gordons crate come from","who packed gordons crate","who made gordons crate"},it="origin",add="e23fc119"},{q="Why does anyone want Gordon's Crate?",a="Deathguard Podrig and the soldiers stationed at the Sepulcher desperately need the shipment. The crate contains weapons necessary to ensure the local Deathguards defending Silverpine Forest are well-armed and not caught unprepared against their enemies.",al={"why is gordons crate needed","why bring gordons crate to the sepulcher","who needs gordons crate"},it="why_wanted",add="a5301c7a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know every shipment of blades and gear from the capital helps hold Lady Sylvanas's tenuous frontier borders in Silverpine Forest.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see the Forsaken's flight routes bringing supplies and couriers swiftly across contested Lordaeron."},kw={"bat handler","deathguard podrig","gordon's crate","gordons crate","karos razok","michael garrett","silverpine supplies","the sepulcher","undercity"},rel={"quest:6322","quest:6324","zone:undercity","subzone:sepulcher","npc:karos-razok"},src={"Gordon's Crate","Michael Garrett (Classic)","Return to Podrig"}}
E["item:grizzled-bear-heart"] = {t="item",n="Grizzled Bear Heart",z="undercity",s="In Silverpine Forest, sturdy bears yield hearts for the Royal Apothecary Society's research into the New Plague.",h="In Silverpine Forest, sturdy bears yield hearts for the Royal Apothecary Society's research into the New...",sec={{t="A Reagent for the New Plague",b="The Royal Apothecary Society works without pause to create an engineered blight that can exterminate both the Scourge and living humanity. In Silverpine Forest's woodlands, Apothecary Renferrel found that toxins from a grizzled bear's heart make a remarkably lethal concoction when joined with arachnid ichor. Couriers and Forsaken loyalists hunt ferocious grizzled bears, giant grizzled bears, and the roaming beast Old Vicejaw. They carve out the hearts and carry them to Master Apothecary Faranell, deep within the Undercity's Apothecarium.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Grizzled Bear Heart used for?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society uses Grizzled Bear Hearts as experimental biological reagents. Apothecary Renferrel discovered that toxins from these hearts can be distilled into a lethal elixir for the Forsaken effort to brew the New Plague.",al={"what does bear heart do","bear heart quest","recipe for death reagents"},it="purpose"},{q="Who wants these bear hearts?",a="Apothecary Renferrel in Silverpine Forest directs travelers to gather the hearts alongside Skittering Blood and deliver them to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity's Apothecarium.",al={"who needs bear heart","faranell bear heart","who do i give bear heart to"},it="item"},{q="Where do Grizzled Bear Hearts come from?",a="Grizzled Bear Hearts come from the bears roaming Silverpine Forest, including ferocious grizzled bears, giant grizzled bears, and the roaming beast Old Vicejaw.",al={"where do i find bear hearts","which bears drop heart","bear heart location"},it="origin"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society need natural animal toxins?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society seeks biological agents that can contaminate and destroy living flesh and undead physiology. The unique chemical properties in the heart tissues of Silverpine's hearty bears provide an ideal reactive base when blended with virulent spider blood.",al={"why do apothecaries use bear venom","why animal hearts for plague"},it="motive"},{q="What is a Grizzled Bear Heart?",a="It is the fresh organ harvested from the ferocious grizzled bears that prowl Silverpine Forest. While a mundane organ at first glance, the heart contains a natural, resilient biological toxin that makes it an alluring reagent for alchemical experiments.",al={"what is grizzled bear heart","bear heart info","grizzled bear heart lore"},it="identity",add="9ca08a87"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, harvesting these organs directly aids Master Apothecary Faranell in engineering a weapon against both Arthas's Scourge and the living mortals threatening Lordaeron.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking Silverpine's massive bears, including Old Vicejaw, tests your patience and field-dressing skill as you seek biological samples."},kw={"a recipe for death","apothecary renferrel","grizzled bear heart","master apothecary faranell","new plague","old vicejaw","royal apothecary society","silverpine forest","skittering blood"},rel={"quest:447","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:royal-apothecary-society","item:skittering-blood","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity"},src={"Grizzled Bear Heart","A Recipe For Death"}}
E["item:hardened-tumor"] = {t="item",n="Hardened Tumor",z="undercity",s="Forsaken researchers seek a Hardened Tumor for their work on the New Plague. Apothecary Berard first studied the growth before Arugal's curse made him a mindless servant.",h="Forsaken researchers seek a Hardened Tumor for their work on the New Plague.",sec={{t="A Rare Biological Anomaly",b="Along Lake Lordamere, Vile Fin murlocs sometimes develop a rare, calcified growth. Apothecary Berard recorded the abnormality while studying wildlife along Silverpine Forest's eastern borders. The growth appears only in mature specimens along the shoreline and the Dawning Isles. Its cause remains uncertain, but the Royal Apothecary Society took notice of the dense tissue.",sp=0},{t="Fuel for the New Plague",b="After Arugal's curse left Berard a mindless servant, his journal was recovered from Pyrewood Village and taken to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher. Renferrel saw promise in Berard's work and sent Forsaken agents to retrieve a Hardened Tumor and native aquatic mosses. Master Apothecary Faranell oversees the Apothecarium in the Undercity, where he seeks reagents that can resist decay or alter biological matter. He added the growth to the Society's ongoing work on the New Plague.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Hardened Tumor?",a="A Hardened Tumor is a rare, abnormal calcified mass that forms inside Vile Fin murlocs around Lake Lordamere. Apothecary Berard discovered it, and it resists ordinary physical decay and has unusual biological properties.",al={"what is this tumor","tumor lore","hardened tumor drop"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society want it?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society gathers unusual toxic and biological specimens to make the New Plague. Master Apothecary Faranell considers the tumor's resilience and cellular makeup a candidate for blight experiments.",al={"why apothecary want tumor","recipe for death tumor use","faranell tumor"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these tumors found?",a="Vile Fin murlocs in Silverpine Forest carry these tumors, including those near the Dawning Isles in eastern Lake Lordamere and along the village shores northeast of Ambermill.",al={"where to find hardened tumor","which murlocs drop tumor","tumor location"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who was Apothecary Berard?",a="Apothecary Berard was a Royal Apothecary Society apothecary stationed in Silverpine Forest. Arugal's curse made him a mindless servant in Pyrewood Village. Berard researched local flora, fauna, and murloc mutations, and uncovered the utility of the Dawning Isles' mosses and hardened tumors.",al={"who is berard","berard lore","berard journal"}},{q="Where does a Hardened Tumor come from?",a="Hardened tumors are abnormal biological growths found on the Vile Fin murlocs dwelling around Lake Lordamere in Silverpine Forest. They are not crafted by mortal hands, but rather harvested from the flesh of these tainted amphibious creatures. Apothecary Berard first documented their existence in his field research, noting that finding a murloc bearing such an unusually dense, calcified growth is remarkably rare.",al={"hardened tumor origin","where do hardened tumors come from","who made hardened tumor"},it="origin",add="9aa7efc6"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you help advance Master Apothecary Faranell's research into the New Plague, serving Lady Sylvanas and the Forsaken's struggle against living and undead adversaries."},kw={"apothecary faranell","apothecary renferrel","berard","dawning isles","hardened tumor","lake lordamere","murloc","new plague","vile fin"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","item:berard-s-journal","quest:447","topic:royal-apothecary-society","topic:murloc","subzone:dawning-isles","zone:silverpine"},src={"Hardened Tumor","A Recipe For Death (3)"}}
E["item:lake-creeper-moss"] = {t="item",n="Lake Creeper Moss",z="undercity",s="Around Lake Lordamere’s southern Dawning Isles, Lake Creeper Moss grows on aquatic beasts. The Royal Apothecary Society seeks the organic compound as a vital reagent for engineering a lethal new plague.",h="Around Lake Lordamere’s southern Dawning Isles, Lake Creeper Moss grows on aquatic beasts.",sec={{t="Alchemical Harvest",b="Lake Creeper Moss grows on the hides of freshwater beasts in the waters by the southern Dawning Isles. Lordaeron’s blighted waters shape its unusual properties. Before Arugal’s curse claimed his mind, Apothecary Berard recorded the moss in his journal. He noted its resemblance to traces found on fossils of creatures killed by an ancient plague in the lake. Forsaken agents send recovered samples to the Apothecarium in the Undercity, where Master Apothecary Faranell uses them in his research.",sp=0},{t="Fueling the New Plague",b="Lake Creeper Moss is a critical stage in developing the Forsaken’s signature weapon. Along with moss gathered from Lake Skulkers and diseased tumors taken from local Vile Fin murlocs, it provides the organic foundation for refining a strain meant to exterminate living tissue and the Scourge alike. Though the apothecary who discovered its use is lost, the Royal Apothecary Society continues to brew his recipe in service of the Dark Lady.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Lake Creeper Moss used for?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell and the Royal Apothecary Society use Lake Creeper Moss as an alchemical reagent to brew and refine their New Plague in the Undercity.",al={"creeper moss purpose","why collect lake creeper moss","lake creeper moss use"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does this moss come from?",a="Lake Creeper Moss grows on Lake Creepers and Elder Lake Creepers in the waters around the southern Dawning Isles in eastern Lake Lordamere.",al={"where to get creeper moss","creeper moss location","lake creeper location"},it="origin"},{q="Who discovered the moss's alchemical value?",a="Before Arugal’s curse left Apothecary Berard a mindless servant in Pyrewood Village, he documented the moss’s alchemical properties in his field journal. Apothecary Renferrel later recovered his notes.",al={"who found the moss","berard moss","who wrote about creeper moss"}},{q="Who receives the harvested moss?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell receives the moss at the Apothecarium in the Undercity. He combines it with Lake Skulker Moss and a hardened tumor in his research.",al={"who wants creeper moss","turn in creeper moss","faranell moss"}},{q="What is Lake Creeper Moss?",a="Lake Creeper Moss is an organic growth harvested directly from the bodies of the aquatic creepers inhabiting Lake Lordamere. While outwardly ordinary swamp flora, the Royal Apothecary Society values it as a vital reagent in their dark experiments.",al={"what is creeper moss","lake creeper moss lore","creeper moss explained"},it="identity",add="70aadfdf"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Each sample brought to the Apothecarium brings the Forsaken closer to perfecting the New Plague and securing vengeance against the Scourge and the living.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Though it grows on water beasts rather than in soil, the moss belongs to Lordaeron’s darker, experimental flora, gathered for apothecary research."},kw={"berard","dawning isles","elder lake creeper","faranell","lake creeper","lake creeper moss","lake lordamere","new plague","royal apothecary society"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","item:lake-skulker-moss","item:hardened-tumor","item:berard-s-journal","quest:447","subzone:dawning-isles","topic:royal-apothecary-society"},src={"Lake Creeper Moss","A Recipe For Death (3)"}}
E["item:lake-skulker-moss"] = {t="item",n="Lake Skulker Moss",z="undercity",s="In northern Lake Lordamere, Lake Skulker Moss draws the Royal Apothecary Society's attention. Apothecary Berard identified it as an organic part of research into brewing a New Plague before Arugal's curse claimed his mind.",h="In northern Lake Lordamere, Lake Skulker Moss draws the Royal Apothecary Society's attention.",sec={{t="A Plague Reagent",b="Lake Skulker Moss is gathered from Lake Skulkers and Elder Lake Skulkers on the Dawning Isles. Before Arugal's curse claimed his mind, Apothecary Berard cataloged the plants and creatures of eastern Silverpine Forest. In his journal, he wrote that Lake Skulker and Lake Creeper mosses could stabilize or react with other ingredients. After Berard became Arugal's mindless servant, his journal was recovered from Pyrewood Village for Apothecary Renferrel. Renferrel sent Forsaken champions to gather moss and a rare tumor from local Vile Fin murlocs, then deliver both to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Lake Skulker Moss used for?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity uses Lake Skulker Moss as an organic base for brewing the New Plague, in pursuit of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's goals for the Forsaken.",al={"moss use","why collect skulker moss","what does skulker moss do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this moss come from?",a="Lake Skulker Moss is scraped from Lake Skulkers and Elder Lake Skulkers in the waters around the Dawning Isles, in northeastern Lake Lordamere off Silverpine Forest.",al={"where to get skulker moss","skulker moss location","who drops lake skulker moss"},it="origin"},{q="Who discovered the moss's usefulness?",a="Apothecary Berard identified the moss's potential while studying Silverpine Forest. After Arugal's curse made him a mindless servant, his journal helped Apothecary Renferrel and Master Apothecary Faranell continue the experiments.",al={"who found the moss","berard moss","apothecary berard research"},it="history"},{q="Who requires this reagent?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell, leader of the Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity's Apothecarium, needs the moss for his biological warfare projects.",al={"who wants skulker moss","faranell skulker moss"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Lake Skulker Moss?",a="Lake Skulker Moss is a natural growth harvested from the backs of lake skulkers, amphibious beasts lurking around the Dawning Isles of Lake Lordamere. While unremarkable to fishermen and travelers, this organic matter possesses specific properties that drew the attention of Forsaken alchemists studying local flora and fauna.",al={"what is lake skulker moss","lake skulker moss info","skulker moss explained"},it="identity",add="18c0a856"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you bring the Royal Apothecary Society closer to perfecting the New Plague, a weapon the Forsaken intend to use against the Scourge and the living."},kw={"berard","dawning isles","faranell","lake lordamere","lake skulker","lake skulker moss","new plague","renferrel"},rel={"quest:447","item:lake-creeper-moss","item:berard-s-journal","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:dawning-isles","item:hardened-tumor"},src={"Lake Skulker Moss","A Recipe For Death (3)"}}
E["item:mudsnout-composite"] = {t="item",n="Mudsnout Composite",z="undercity",s="At Tarren Mill, Mudsnout Composite is prepared for the Royal Apothecary Society's research into a new plague. Apothecary Lydon makes it from Mudsnout Blossoms gathered in the Hillsbrad Foothills and sends it to the Undercity.",h="At Tarren Mill, Mudsnout Composite is prepared for the Royal Apothecary Society's research into a new plague.",sec={{t="A Base for Decay",b="Apothecary Lydon makes Mudsnout Composite from Mudsnout Blossoms gathered in the Hillsbrad Foothills. The paste is noxious on its own, but Master Apothecary Faranell must bind it with a colloid of decay to bring out its deadlier qualities. Together, the ingredients form a key chemical component in the Dark Lady's Elixir of Agony.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Correspondence",b="The Royal Apothecary Society receives Mudsnout Composite in the Undercity's Apothecarium after its journey from Tarren Mill. Field researchers gather reagents in different regions and send samples to the capital's masters for refinement. Lady Sylvanas demands swift results against living humans and the Scourge, and Faranell praises the composite as ingenious groundwork toward their goal.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Mudsnout Composite used for?",a="Mudsnout Composite is a paste made from Mudsnout Blossoms. Master Apothecary Faranell treats it with a colloid of decay in the Undercity to help formulate the Elixir of Agony.",al={"mudsnout composite purpose","what does mudsnout composite do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who created the composite?",a="Apothecary Lydon created the composite at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, crushing fresh blossoms into a paste before sending it north.",al={"who made mudsnout composite","mudsnout composite creator"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Master Apothecary Faranell need it?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell needs the composite for the Royal Apothecary Society's work on a new plague. Lydon's paste provides the herbal base for their research into lethal toxins.",al={"why bring it to faranell","faranell mudsnout"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Mudsnout Composite?",a="Mudsnout Composite is a refined mixture concocted by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill. Crafted by grinding down rare Mudsnout Blossoms found in the Hillsbrad Foothills, this potent substance serves as an essential alchemical base in the Royal Apothecary Society's research to engineer a devastating new plague for the Forsaken.",al={"mudsnout composite","what is mudsnout composite","mudsnout mixture"},it="identity",add="432a2438"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, each shipment of Mudsnout Composite serves the Dark Lady's mandate: to secure the Forsaken's future by developing a plague against the living and the Scourge.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you can see how Mudsnout Blossoms can be crushed and weaponized by an apothecary."},kw={"apothecarium","apothecary lydon","elixir of agony","master apothecary faranell","mudsnout blossom","mudsnout composite","royal apothecary society"},rel={"quest:509","item:mudsnout-blossom","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","subzone:apothecarium","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity","quest:367"},src={"Mudsnout Composite","Elixir of Agony (2)"}}
E["item:mudsnout-mixture"] = {t="item",n="Mudsnout Mixture",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Master Apothecary Faranell prepares a base for a deadly Forsaken poison. Mudsnout Mixture begins with mushrooms sent north from Tarren Mill.",h="In the Undercity, Master Apothecary Faranell prepares a base for a deadly Forsaken poison.",sec={{t="A Colloid of Decay",b="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill seeks to craft a virulent new biological weapon. He sends a composite made from Mudsnout Blossoms north to the Undercity. The toxic mushrooms grow at Nethander Stead, held by gnolls. Master Apothecary Faranell sees promise in the composite and adds his own colloid of decay. The resulting Mudsnout Mixture is volatile. It steadies the mushroom compound and prepares its virulent properties for further catalytic refinement in the foothills.",sp=0},{t="Catalyzing the Agony",b="Mudsnout Mixture needs key catalysts before its contaminating agents can take effect. Faranell sends couriers back to Tarren Mill with the vial, a Strong Troll's Blood Elixir, venomous Daggerspine naga scales, and Torn Fin murloc eyes. Apothecary Lydon catalyzes the mixture with these ingredients to make the lethal Elixir of Agony, a signature poison meant to spread ruin among the Forsaken's living enemies.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Mudsnout Mixture used for?",a="Mudsnout Mixture provides the chemical base for the Elixir of Agony, an experimental poison Apothecary Lydon is perfecting in Tarren Mill to kill the Forsaken's enemies.",al={"mudsnout mixture purpose","what does mudsnout mixture do","mudsnout mixture use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who creates the Mudsnout Mixture?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell creates Mudsnout Mixture in the Undercity by adding his colloid of decay to a raw mudsnout composite.",al={"who makes mudsnout mixture","mudsnout mixture creator"},it="origin"},{q="Why does it require gnoll components?",a="Mudsnout Mixture needs no gnoll parts. The composite comes from Mudsnout Blossoms, toxic mushrooms growing at Nethander Stead among the Mudsnout gnolls. Apothecary Lydon blends them into a composite before Faranell adds his colloid of decay.",al={"why mudsnout","gnoll poison lore"}},{q="How is the mixture activated?",a="Apothecary Lydon activates the dormant contaminating agents with a Strong Troll's Blood Elixir, Daggerspine naga scales, and Torn Fin murloc eyes gathered along the Hillsbrad coast.",al={"activate mudsnout mixture","elixir of agony reagents"}},{q="What is Mudsnout Mixture?",a="It is an experimental alchemical concoction formulated by the Royal Apothecary Society. Built around a composite of Mudsnout Blossoms, toxic mushrooms from Nethander Stead, the mixture incorporates Master Apothecary Faranell's own colloid of decay to serve as a volatile base for the apothecaries' plague research.",al={"what is mudsnout mixture","mudsnout mixture","mudsnout composite"},it="identity",add="f656f7cb"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want Mudsnout Mixture?",a="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill requires it to synthesize the Elixir of Agony, an experimental concoction aimed at spreading disease and death to the enemies of the Forsaken. By activating its contaminating agents with troll's blood and coastal reagents, he intends to advance the Royal Apothecary Society's plague research.",al={"why is mudsnout mixture needed","why does lydon want mudsnout mixture","what is mudsnout mixture for"},it="why_wanted",add="ac01c76e"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you can see the Royal Apothecary Society's ruthless ingenuity at work: wilderness ingredients refined into chemical weapons meant to kill the living.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer in Tarren Mill, you carry toxic concoctions across Lordaeron as a courier and field agent, helping secure the Forsaken foothold in Hillsbrad."},kw={"apothecary","colloid of decay","elixir of agony","faranell","hillsbrad","lydon","mudsnout mixture","undercity"},rel={"quest:509","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","topic:royal-apothecary-society","item:mudsnout-composite","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:undercity","item:daggerspine-scale","item:torn-fin-eye"},src={"Mudsnout Mixture","Elixir of Agony (3)"}}
E["item:nether-gem"] = {t="item",n="Nether Gem",z="undercity",s="Across Tirisfal Glades, the Nether Gem carries the image of a mysterious figure from Brightwater Lake to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity. What binds the two is yours to uncover.",h="Across Tirisfal Glades, the Nether Gem carries the image of a mysterious figure from Brightwater Lake to...",sec={{t="A Conduit of Arcane Communion",b="Gunther Arcanus forged or enchanted the Nether Gem on his solitary island in Brightwater Lake. He had broken free from the Lich King's control by his own will, yet suspicion kept him apart from the young Forsaken nation. After his lost spellbook is returned, Gunther gives the gem to an emissary as a gesture of goodwill. Atop the Magic Quarter in the Undercity, Bethor Iceshard channels magic through the stone. Gunther's magical visage appears before the Mage Guild leader, letting the two mages speak across Tirisfal Glades. Their meeting opens a path for Gunther to align with Lady Sylvanas and the Forsaken.",sp=1,bt={"q358.4"}}},faq={{q="What does the Nether Gem do?",a="The Nether Gem lets Gunther Arcanus communicate over a long distance with Bethor Iceshard. When Bethor channels magic into it in the Undercity, Gunther's ethereal visage appears so the two mages can speak directly.",al={"nether gem purpose","what is nether gem","what does nether gem do"},it="power"},{q="Who crafted the Nether Gem?",a="Gunther Arcanus provides the Nether Gem. He lives on an island in Brightwater Lake and gives it to an emissary for his old comrade Bethor after his lost spellbook is returned.",al={"who made nether gem","where does nether gem come from","gunther gem"},sp=1,it="origin",bt={"q358.4"}},{q="Why is the Nether Gem significant to the Forsaken?",a="The Nether Gem helps bring Gunther Arcanus into the Forsaken. He mistrusted other undead, fearing they remained thralls of the Scourge, but the gem lets him reconnect with Bethor Iceshard and pledge allegiance to Lady Sylvanas.",al={"why is nether gem important","gunther forsaken","forsaken nether gem"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Nether Gem?",a="The Nether Gem is a magical focus entrusted to you by Gunther Arcanus, a powerful undead mage residing on an island in Brightwater Lake. Charged with mystical arcane energies, it acts as a magical conduit that allows Gunther to communicate across great distances and project his visage directly to his old ally Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.",al={"what is nether gem","nether gem lore","nether gem item"},it="identity",add="aa73e2cb"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you see how arcane masters can bridge vast distances with magical scrying and projected visages instead of risking the journey.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the stone's delivery marks a diplomatic triumph for the Forsaken, securing Gunther Arcanus as a powerful ally against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brightwater lake","gunther arcanus","nether gem","prodigal lich","undercity"},rel={"quest:411","quest:405","npc:bethor-iceshard","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},src={"Nether Gem","The Prodigal Lich Returns"}}
E["item:pure-hearts"] = {t="item",n="Pure Hearts",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Pure Hearts draw a succubus from the Twisting Nether. Carendin Halgar gives these ritual reagents to Forsaken warlocks, who use them to manifest the demon and attempt to defeat and bind her.",h="In the Undercity, Pure Hearts draw a succubus from the Twisting Nether.",sec={{t="Bait for the Nether",b="Carendin Halgar gives Pure Hearts to warlocks who summon a succubus in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. Set on the summoning circle, these untainted spiritual essences lure the demon across the Twisting Nether and into the mortal realm. Once she appears, the warlock must resist her enthralling mind-charms and strike her down. Defeating the succubus asserts mystical dominance and sends her back to the Twisting Nether. Carendin then teaches the warlock the spell to summon her at will.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Pure Hearts used for?",a="Pure Hearts lure a succubus across the Twisting Nether and manifest her in the mortal realm, at the summoning circle in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, where a warlock can fight and bind her.",al={"pure hearts use","why pure hearts","what do pure hearts do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides the Pure Hearts?",a="Carendin Halgar, a Forsaken warlock trainer in the Undercity, gives Pure Hearts to warlocks preparing to summon a succubus.",al={"who gives pure hearts","pure hearts quest giver"},it="origin"},{q="Why does a succubus respond to Pure Hearts?",a="Succubi thrive on corruption and seduction, and the radiance of unblemished hearts is an irresistible lure across the Twisting Nether, drawing them to a warlock's summoning circle.",al={"why succubus wants pure hearts","lore behind pure hearts"},it="power"},{q="Do you get to keep the Pure Hearts after the ritual?",a="No. After the succubus is summoned and subdued, the Pure Hearts' remnants go back to Carendin Halgar as proof that the binding trial is complete.",al={"do i keep pure hearts","what happens to pure hearts"},gp=true},{q="What are the Pure Hearts?",a="The Pure Hearts are potent ritual components used by Forsaken warlocks in the Undercity. When cast upon a summoning circle, their untainted essence acts as a lure across the Twisting Nether, opening a rift specifically designed to entice and summon a dangerous succubus into your presence.",al={"what are pure hearts","pure hearts item","pure hearts warlock"},it="identity",add="105bfa16"},{q="Why would anyone want the Pure Hearts?",a="An aspiring warlock requires the Pure Hearts to complete the dangerous binding ritual for a succubus. Without offering such untainted bait to bridge the void, you cannot draw the demon through into the mortal realm to subdue her and master the art of summoning her to your command.",al={"why want pure hearts","pure hearts purpose","why are pure hearts sought"},it="why_wanted",add="3abadf0f"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, using Pure Hearts marks a turning point in demonology and proves your mental strength against the Twisting Nether's seductive lures.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you use untainted hearts to manipulate demonic appetites. This cold, pragmatic sorcery exemplifies Forsaken practice."},kw={"carendin halgar","magic quarter","pure hearts","succubus","summoning","the binding","undercity"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1471","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity"},src={"Pure Hearts","The Binding (Succubus, Undercity)"}}
E["item:runes-of-summoning"] = {t="item",n="Runes of Summoning",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Carendin Halgar gives warlocks runes for summoning a voidwalker. The ritual draws an unbound voidwalker into a circle, where an aspiring warlock can bend it to their will.",h="In the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Carendin Halgar gives warlocks runes for summoning a voidwalker.",sec={{t="Subjugation in the Magic Quarter",b="Carendin Halgar gives the Runes of Summoning to warlocks ready to command a voidwalker. In the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, Forsaken practitioners study how to manipulate the Nether. A warlock casts the runes in the active summoning circle below Halgar's station. The ritual tears through the Void and draws forth a creature to be overpowered and bound into servitude.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Runes of Summoning used for?",a="A warlock uses the runes in the summoning circle in the Undercity's Magic Quarter to draw an unbound voidwalker from the Nether into the physical world. The warlock can then defeat it and bend it to their will.",al={"runes of summoning purpose","what do runes of summoning do","how to use runes of summoning"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides the Runes of Summoning?",a="Carendin Halgar, the Forsaken warlock trainer in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, provides the runes during the final stage of training to bind a voidwalker.",al={"who gives runes of summoning","runes of summoning trainer","carendin halgar runes"},it="origin"},{q="Where must the runes be activated?",a="Bring the runes to the purple summoning circle directly below Carendin Halgar's platform in the Magic Quarter.",al={"where do i use runes of summoning","runes of summoning location","summoning circle undercity"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after the entity is summoned?",a="The voidwalker attacks as soon as it is summoned. The warlock must subdue it with magic and arms. Once defeated, the entity is indentured, and Carendin Halgar teaches the permanent spell to summon it.",al={"what happens after using runes","voidwalker subdued","after summoning voidwalker"},it="next_step"},{q="What are the Runes of Summoning?",a="The Runes of Summoning are a specialized ritual catalyst given to aspiring Forsaken warlocks in the Undercity. When brought to the circle of summoning in the Magic Quarter, the runes focus magical energies to tear open a passage and draw forth an unbound voidwalker from the Nether.",al={"what are runes of summoning","runes of summoning","runes of summoning item"},it="identity",add="1ce5479a"},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar want the Runes of Summoning returned?",a="Carendin Halgar provides the runes specifically as a trial of mastery. Once you activate them and subdue the summoned voidwalker in combat, returning the runes proves to him that you have dominated the creature, allowing him to properly teach you the permanent spell to summon and command voidwalkers.",al={"why return runes of summoning","why does carendin want the runes","return runes of summoning"},it="why_wanted",add="0508549c"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you use the runes to prove your dominion over the Void, turning a chaotic shadow into an enduring, loyal minion.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you follow Forsaken practitioners into the Undercity's depths, where they bind void entities beneath the ruins of Lordaeron despite ancient taboos."},kw={"carendin halgar","magic quarter","runes of summoning","the binding","undercity","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"quest:1471","npc:carendin-halgar","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:1473","quest:1478","topic:warlock"},src={"Runes of Summoning","The Binding (Voidwalker, Undercity)"}}
E["item:sample-ichor"] = {t="item",n="Sample Ichor",z="undercity",s="In Silverpine Forest, Sample Ichor carries traces of necromancy and warlock sorcery. Apothecary Renferrel refined it from the fluid that sustains the Rot Hide gnolls.",h="In Silverpine Forest, Sample Ichor carries traces of necromancy and warlock sorcery.",sec={{t="Unraveling the Rot Hides",b="Apothecary Renferrel sent Sample Ichor to the Undercity for closer study. He recovered samples from the Rot Hide gnolls and their lingering remnants, then reduced the foul liquid to its base components. His analysis showed that the ichor was made through necromantic rites woven with warlock magic. Since its craft reaches beyond simple alchemy, Renferrel sent the sample to Bethor Iceshard for divination.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sample Ichor?",a="Sample Ichor is a refined extract Apothecary Renferrel prepared from the bodily fluids of the Rot Hide gnolls. He separated it into its base components to learn how magic was used to create the walking dead beasts.",al={"sample ichor","what is this ichor","what is sample ichor"},it="identity"},{q="Who needs to see this sample?",a="Bethor Iceshard needs to examine the sample. He is an undead mage stationed in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, where his skill in divination and magical traditions can reveal traces ordinary alchemy cannot discern.",al={"who do i bring the ichor to","sample ichor turn in","bethor iceshard ichor"},it="purpose"},{q="What kind of magic is inside the ichor?",a="The ichor contains warlock and necromantic magic bound into the fluid. Bethor Iceshard notes that the vial is laced with powerful, ancient enchantments, requiring deeper divination to uncover fully.",al={"what magic is in the ichor","ichor magic type","rot hide magic"},it="power"},{q="Why didn't the apothecaries finish analyzing it themselves?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society excels in alchemy, toxins, and bodily blights, while complex arcane weaves call for a dedicated sorcerer. Bethor Iceshard can identify magical schools and unravel esoteric spells beyond an apothecary's usual tools.",al={"why apothecary sent to bethor","why not renounce rot hide ichor"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this Sample Ichor come from, and who made it?",a="Apothecary Renferrel prepared this vial by breaking down crude ichor gathered from the rot hide gnolls in Silverpine Forest. His initial analysis revealed that whoever created the original substance infused it with both necromancy and warlock magic, though the true mastermind behind its creation remains to be unraveled.",al={"sample ichor origin","where did sample ichor come from","who made sample ichor"},it="origin",add="f4e4cc11"},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard want the Sample Ichor?",a="Apothecary Renferrel hit the limits of alchemical science trying to determine what created the rot hides. He sent this refined sample to Bethor Iceshard in Undercity's Magic Quarter because Bethor possesses deep knowledge of arcane and dark arts, allowing him to use divination magic to identify the obscure spells woven into the fluid.",al={"why does bethor want sample ichor","why is sample ichor wanted","sample ichor purpose bethor"},it="why_wanted",add="045e6062"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may recognize the warlock arts Apothecary Renferrel detected interwoven with necromancy in the ichor, hinting that fel practices helped bind these undead beasts.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know the value of classical arcane analysis against dark sorcery. Bethor Iceshard uses specialized divination spells to read the residue in the sample."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","bethor iceshard","magic quarter","rot hide","rot hide origins","sample ichor","silverpine","undercity"},rel={"quest:444","npc:apothecary-renferrel","npc:bethor-iceshard","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","topic:warlock"},src={"Sample Ichor","Rot Hide Origins"}}
E["item:sevren-s-orders"] = {t="item",n="Sevren's Orders",z="undercity",s="In Brill, Magistrate Sevren sends a proven Forsaken agent to the Undercity. The orders direct the agent to Bethor Iceshard in the Magic Quarter.",h="In Brill, Magistrate Sevren sends a proven Forsaken agent to the Undercity.",sec={{t="Summons to the Capital",b="Skilled Forsaken agents who prove themselves against the Scourge in Tirisfal Glades are summoned south as their people strengthen their hold on Lordaeron. Magistrate Sevren writes the orders as an introduction and credentials for Bethor Iceshard, one of the Dark Lady's foremost arcane practitioners in the Magic Quarter. Sevren knows only that the assignment concerns reaching out to an errant lich. The Undercity's high mages give the summons their full authority.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wrote these orders?",a="Magistrate Sevren, who oversees Forsaken affairs in Brill, wrote the orders.",al={"author of sevren's orders","who is sevren","who gives sevrens orders"},it="origin"},{q="Who is intended to receive these orders?",a="The orders are addressed to Bethor Iceshard, a high-ranking Forsaken mage in the Undercity's Magic Quarter.",al={"who gets the orders","where do i bring sevren's orders","who is bethor iceshard"},it="target"},{q="What is the mission mentioned in the orders?",a="The orders call for recruiting a wayward lich to aid the Forsaken. The dangerous task falls to an agent already proven against the Scourge.",al={"what is the lich mission","what does bethor want","prodigal lich mission"},it="purpose"},{q="Why was I chosen to deliver them?",a="Bethor requested an operative proven against the Scourge. Magistrate Sevren judged your efforts in Tirisfal Glades enough to meet Bethor's dangerous request.",al={"why me","why did sevren pick me"},it="why_me"},{q="What is Sevren's Orders?",a="Sevren's Orders is an official dispatch written by Magistrate Sevren of Brill. It acts as formal credentials, identifying you as an agent of proven worth who has fought effectively against the Scourge and is ready to undertake a sensitive assignment.",al={"what are sevrens orders","sevren orders item","what is this document"},it="identity",add="59d8f724"},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard want Sevren's Orders?",a="Bethor Iceshard, a prominent mage in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, demanded that Sevren provide an agent capable of handling a perilous task involving a rogue lich. Presenting these orders proves that you are Sevren's chosen operative and that your interruption of the powerful wizard is warranted.",al={"why deliver sevren orders","why does bethor want orders","who needs sevren's orders"},it="why_wanted",add="680dc8a1"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, carrying Sevren's seal takes you from local service in Tirisfal to work for the Undercity's arcane elite.",["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, delivering the orders brings you before Bethor Iceshard, one of the foremost spellcasters in the Forsaken kingdom."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brill","magic quarter","magistrate sevren","prodigal lich","sevren's orders","undercity"},rel={"quest:405","npc:magistrate-sevren","npc:bethor-iceshard","zone:undercity","subzone:magic-quarter","topic:scourge","topic:mage"},src={"Sevren's Orders","The Prodigal Lich"}}
E["item:skittering-blood"] = {t="item",n="Skittering Blood",z="undercity",s="Skittering Blood feeds the Royal Apothecary Society's work on a New Plague. The reagent comes from arachnids in the Skittering Dark of Silverpine Forest, where Forsaken alchemists seek a weapon against the Scourge and humanity.",h="Skittering Blood feeds the Royal Apothecary Society's work on a New Plague.",sec={{t="A Toxic Distillate",b="Skitterweb lurkers, strikers, and their broodmother Krethis the Shadowspinner yield a venomous blood. Apothecary Renferrel found that, refined with toxins from grizzled bear hearts, it forms the base of an exceptionally lethal elixir. Its contaminating agents make it useful in the Apothecarium's chemical experiments.",sp=0},{t="Fueling the New Plague",b="In the Undercity, Master Apothecary Faranell directs the Royal Apothecary Society's search for a New Plague. The Forsaken face Scourge hordes and hostile human remnants, and turn to biological warfare to even the odds. Faranell studies the blood's toxic strength as he works toward a contagion that can destroy unlife and living flesh alike.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Skittering Blood used for?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society uses Skittering Blood in its work on the Forsaken's New Plague. Blended with toxins from bear hearts, it makes a volatile mixture that Master Apothecary Faranell studies for use against the Scourge and living humans.",al={"skittering blood use","why gather spider blood","what does faranell do with skittering blood"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Skittering Blood found?",a="Skittering Blood comes from Skitterweb lurkers, strikers, and Krethis the Shadowspinner in and around the Skittering Dark, a gloomy, web-choked wood in northwestern Silverpine Forest.",al={"where to get skittering blood","skittering blood location","who drops skittering blood"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who requests these samples?",a="Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest asks for the blood. The gathered fluid is delivered to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity's Apothecarium.",al={"who wants skittering blood","quest giver for skittering blood"},it="people"},{q="Why do the Forsaken need venom from local beasts?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society draws natural toxins from Lordaeron's corrupted fauna. Venom from Silverpine's giant arachnids provides raw biological pathogens that can be concentrated and weaponized into synthetic plagues.",al={"why spider venom","apothecary beast research"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Skittering Blood?",a="Skittering Blood is the virulent ichor harvested from the massive spiders dwelling in the Skittering Dark of Silverpine Forest. It possesses natural venomous and contaminable properties that make it an invaluable biological reagent for alchemical experiments.",al={"what is skittering blood","skittering blood item","about skittering blood"},it="identity",add="8eea8a63"},{q="Where does Skittering Blood come from, and who made it?",a="It is not manufactured, but naturally drawn from the predatory arachnids inhabiting northwestern Silverpine Forest, including Skitterweb Lurkers, Skitterweb Strikers, and the broodmother Krethis the Shadowspinner. The blood is extracted directly from their carcasses by hunters gathering materials for the Forsaken.",al={"where does skittering blood come from","who made skittering blood","skittering blood origin"},it="origin",add="f7d32240"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, your contribution of Skittering Blood aids Queen Sylvanas and the Royal Apothecary Society as they develop a biological weapon against Arthas and living humanity.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help Forsaken apothecaries secure Lordaeron with weapons of their own making in their war against the Scourge."},kw={"faranell","new plague","renferrel","royal apothecary society","silverpine forest","skittering blood","skittering dark","skitterweb"},rel={"quest:447","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:royal-apothecary-society","item:grizzled-bear-heart","subzone:skittering-dark","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity"},src={"Skittering Blood","A Recipe For Death"}}
E["item:sturdy-dragonmaw-shinbone"] = {t="item",n="Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbone",z="undercity",s="At the Angerfang Encampment, renegade Dragonmaw orcs provide sturdy shinbones for armor. In the Undercity, Velora Nitely needs them to frame leg guards for warriors.",h="At the Angerfang Encampment, renegade Dragonmaw orcs provide sturdy shinbones for armor.",sec={{t="Bones for the Frame",b="Velora Nitely needs bones that can bear the strain of brutal leg guards. The renegade Dragonmaw orcs at the Angerfang Encampment in the central Wetlands have thick, sturdy frames, and their shinbones can brace the armor. Each bone must be tested by hand. Warriors discard any that snap under pressure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes these shinbones sturdy compared to normal ones?",a="Dragonmaw orcs have thick skeletal frames, but fractures can make a bone too brittle for armor. A warrior bends each shinbone by hand and keeps only those that resist breaking.",al={"why sturdy shinbones","dragonmaw bone strength","testing shinbones"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbones?",a="Velora Nitely, an armorer in the Undercity, wants Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbones. She uses them as framing struts for brutal leg guards made for promising Horde warriors.",al={"who needs shinbones","velora nitely bones","turn in dragonmaw shinbones"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these bones gathered?",a="The bones come from renegade Dragonmaw orcs in the Wetlands, south of the Arathi Highlands. They are found especially at the Angerfang Encampment in the hills southwest of the Thandol Span.",al={"where to find dragonmaw shinbones","dragonmaw shinbone location","angerfang bones"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Velora Nitely use orc bones for armor?",a="Forsaken smiths use bone, sinew, and metal to make durable wargear. The Dragonmaw clan is hostile to Thrall's Horde, so Forsaken smiths use their remains as resilient crafting material.",al={"why orc bones","forsaken bone armor","velora bone crafting"},it="motive"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you test dense orc bones by hand and gather pieces to frame custom armor. This shows your physical might.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you can see Forsaken pragmatism in Velora Nitely's use of enemy bones for equipment for the Dark Lady's champions."},kw={"angerfang encampment","dragonmaw shinbone","leg guards","sturdy dragonmaw shinbone","undercity","velora nitely","wetlands"},rel={"quest:1846","npc:velora-nitely","subzone:angerfang-encampment","zone:wetlands","subzone:thandol-span","zone:undercity"},src={"Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbone","Dragonmaw Shinbones"}}
E["item:the-lich-s-spellbook"] = {t="item",n="The Lich's Spellbook",z="undercity",s="On Brightwater Lake's island, a spellbook draws Bethor Iceshard's attention. He hopes its pages will reveal the lich's skill and who he was in life.",h="On Brightwater Lake's island, a spellbook draws Bethor Iceshard's attention.",sec={{t="A Reclusive Master's Tomes",b="A free-willed lich guards an island in Brightwater Lake with skeletal minions. He distrusts the outside world and mistakes other undead for Scourge thralls, ordering his guardians to kill anyone who approaches. Bethor Iceshard seeks skilled necromancers for the Forsaken beneath Queen Sylvanas Windrunner. He sends an emissary into the island camp to take the lich's spellbook. Bethor hopes its pages will reveal the master's power and identity before death took Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="Unmasking Gunther Arcanus",b="The recovered spellbook reveals that the reclusive lich is Gunther Arcanus, Bethor Iceshard's old friend and comrade-in-arms from before the Third War. Gunther was a necromantic prodigy in life, and his writings show that his power grew greater in undeath. Bethor knows Gunther could be a valued master of the dark arts for the Forsaken. Someone must first convince the suspicious lich that the Forsaken are free of the Lich King's grip.",sp=1,bt={"q358.4"}}},faq={{q="Where is the Lich's Spellbook found?",a="The spellbook lies in a container named Gunther's Books, in the encampment on Brightwater Lake's central island in northern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is the book","spellbook location","gunther's books"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who owns this spellbook?",a="The book belongs to a free-willed, reclusive lich on Brightwater Lake's island. Bethor Iceshard hopes its pages will reveal the lich's identity and skill.",al={"whose book is this","lich identity","who wrote the spellbook"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard want the book?",a="Bethor Iceshard wants to learn the lich's identity and measure his necromantic skill, hoping to recruit him for Lady Sylvanas and the Forsaken.",al={"why get the book","bethor quest reason","why does undercity want this"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does the lich attack visitors to his island?",a="The lich believes other undead nearby remain mind-controlled Scourge slaves. He orders his minions to attack anyone who approaches his island refuge.",al={"why is gunther hostile","why do minions attack","brightwater lake hostile"},it="hostile"},{q="What does Bethor hope to learn about the author?",a="Bethor hopes to learn who the isolated lich was in life and whether his necromantic knowledge could aid the Forsaken.",al={"what will bethor learn","lich author study","bethor spellbook study"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Where does The Lich's Spellbook come from, and who made it?",a="The spellbook belongs to the reclusive, free-willed lich who dwells on the island in Brightwater Lake. He penned and maintained the tome himself, filling its glowing pages with his necromantic arts both in life and after his transformation into a lich. Bethor Iceshard wants it to learn who the lich was.",al={"who made the lich spellbook","origin of the lich's spellbook","where did the lich spellbook come from"},sp=1,it="origin",add="44ee6981"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know that some who escaped the Lich King's control did not join the Forsaken at once. Rogue undead survivors across Tirisfal still distrust one another.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how the spellbook joins Dalaran wizardry with dark necromancy. Its author greatly expanded his craft after becoming undead."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brightwater lake","gunther arcanus","lich","necromancy","spellbook","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"quest:357","npc:gunther-arcanus","npc:bethor-iceshard","subzone:brightwater-lake","zone:tirisfal","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"The Lich's Spellbook","The Lich's Identity"}}
E["item:torn-fin-eye"] = {t="item",n="Torn Fin Eye",z="undercity",s="Along Hillsbrad's coast, Torn Fin Eyes draw the Royal Apothecary Society's attention. The Forsaken seek them for alchemical work on new plagues.",h="Along Hillsbrad's coast, Torn Fin Eyes draw the Royal Apothecary Society's attention.",sec={{t="A Reagent for Ruin",b="The Royal Apothecary Society puts rare biological components to use in its work on the Forsaken's New Plague. Torn Fin Eyes come from murlocs along the Western Strand of Hillsbrad Foothills. Their organic properties help activate volatile alchemical compounds. Mixed with Daggerspine naga scales, restorative troll elixirs, and gnoll-derived sludge, the eyes help stabilize and trigger toxic mixtures meant to spread death through enemy lands.",sp=0},{t="Brewing Agony",b="In the Undercity's Apothecarium, master alchemists found that decaying colloids added to Mudsnout composites need catalysts from Hillsbrad's coast. Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill uses the harvested eyes to catalyze his Elixir of Agony. The brew is part of the Forsaken's continuing effort to make devastating bio-weapons near human settlements.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Torn Fin Eye used for?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society seeks Torn Fin Eyes as an alchemical catalyst. In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon combines them with Daggerspine Scales and a Strong Troll's Blood Elixir to activate contaminants in a volatile Mudsnout Mixture and advance his work on deadly plagues.",al={"torn fin eye use","why get torn fin eyes","torn fin eye purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do you find Torn Fin Eyes?",a="You can harvest Torn Fin Eyes from Torn Fin murlocs on the Western Strand of Hillsbrad Foothills, along the coast west of Southshore.",al={"where to get torn fin eyes","torn fin eye location","who drops torn fin eye"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who orders the gathering of these eyes?",a="Forsaken researchers in the Undercity and Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill need the eyes to complete the Elixir of Agony.",al={"who needs torn fin eyes","torn fin eye quest giver"},it="motive"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society need murloc parts?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society studies local creatures for compounds that activate or intensify toxic contaminants. Torn Fin murloc ocular humors can catalyze volatile plague prototypes.",al={"why murloc eyes","apothecary murlocs"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is a Torn Fin Eye?",a="A Torn Fin Eye is an alchemical reagent harvested from the coastal murlocs prowling the shores of Hillsbrad Foothills. Viscous and saturated with amphibious humors, these eyes are utilized by Forsaken apothecaries who require biological catalysts to awaken volatile contaminating agents in their experimental concoctions.",al={"what is torn fin eye","torn fin eye info","about torn fin eyes"},it="identity",add="edd43501"},{q="Where do Torn Fin Eyes come from?",a="These organic reagents are carved from the Torn Fin tribe of murlocs, who inhabit the Western Strand along the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills, just west of the human settlement of Southshore. They are natural biological parts harvested directly from slain murlocs rather than crafted items.",al={"torn fin eye source","where to get torn fin eyes","who drops torn fin eye"},it="origin",add="3427cbae"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, gathering organic catalysts like Torn Fin Eyes advances the Royal Apothecary Society's aim to perfect a plague that will destroy both the Scourge and the living.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help its war effort in Hillsbrad Foothills by gathering coastal reagents, strengthening the Forsaken foothold against Alliance advances from Southshore."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of agony","hillsbrad foothills","murloc","royal apothecary society","torn fin","torn fin eye","undercity"},rel={"quest:509","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity","subzone:tarren-mill","item:daggerspine-scale","item:mudsnout-mixture","topic:murloc"},src={"Torn Fin Eye","Elixir of Agony (3)"}}
E["item:valdred-s-hands"] = {t="item",n="Valdred's Hands",z="undercity",s="In southern Silverpine Forest, Valdred Moray's severed hands become proof of Raleigh Andrean's vengeance for his wife's murder. Raleigh seeks them in the Undercity as a grim trophy.",h="In southern Silverpine Forest, Valdred Moray's severed hands become proof of Raleigh Andrean's vengeance for...",sec={{t="A Gruesome Trophy of Betrayal",b="The plague consumed Lordaeron and ended the friendship between Valdred Moray and Raleigh Andrean. Valdred had murdered Raleigh's wife, Deliah. Raleigh died and rose as one of the Forsaken, claiming he could no longer truly grieve. Yet he still wanted vengeance. When Valdred fled south past the Greymane Wall toward Gilneas, Raleigh sent an emissary after his former friend. He demanded Valdred's severed hands as proof that the deed was done.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Remembrance",b="Raleigh Andrean gives up Deliah's engraved ring when he receives Valdred's hands, calling the ring meaningless. Deliah has been dead to him for so long that keepsakes bring him no comfort. He keeps the hands as a cold reminder of betrayal and vengeance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Valdred Moray?",a="Valdred Moray was once a close friend of Raleigh Andrean. He betrayed that friendship by murdering Raleigh's wife, Deliah, then tried to flee south toward Gilneas.",al={"who is valdred","valdred moray lore","valdred story"},it="people"},{q="Why does Raleigh Andrean want Valdred's hands specifically?",a="Raleigh wants Valdred's hands because they were the instruments that strangled or struck down his wife. He keeps them as a physical trophy of his friend's betrayal and the revenge he took.",al={"why hands","why valdreds hands","raleigh hands trophy"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Valdred Moray found?",a="Valdred is in southern Silverpine Forest, near the Greymane Wall, as he tries to escape into Gilneas.",al={"where is valdred","valdred location","valdred moray spawn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens to the hands after bringing them to Undercity?",a="Raleigh keeps the hands in the Undercity as a lasting reminder of his vengeance. He also discards Deliah's engraved ring as a meaningless trinket.",al={"what does raleigh do with hands","turn in valdreds hands"},sp=1},{q="What are Valdred's Hands?",a="These are the severed hands of Valdred Moray, taken as proof of his death and as a macabre trophy of vengeance. Valdred was once a trusted friend to Raleigh Andrean before betraying him and murdering Raleigh's wife, Deliah. Now, the severed appendages serve as the physical culmination of Raleigh's bitter quest for retribution.",al={"valdreds hands item","what are valdreds hands","valdred hands"},it="identity",add="1f1d5250"},{q="Where do Valdred's Hands come from?",a="They are severed directly from the body of Valdred Moray. Desperate to flee the Forsaken and escape retribution for his crimes, Valdred retreated south through Silverpine Forest toward the Greymane Wall, hoping to slip into the walled kingdom of Gilneas before his hunter could claim him.",al={"origin of valdreds hands","who has valdreds hands","where do valdreds hands come from"},it="origin",add="ba2ecc3a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Valdred's hands show the Forsaken's cold, vengeful nature. Unable to feel conventional sorrow, they often channel that loss into lingering, obsessive grudges."},kw={"a husband's revenge","deliah","greymane wall","raleigh andrean","silverpine forest","valdred","valdred moray","valdred's hands"},rel={"npc:raleigh-andrean","quest:530","quest:440","quest:441","subzone:greymane-wall","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity"},src={"Valdred's Hands","A Husband's Revenge"}}
E["item:wolf-heart-samples"] = {t="item",n="Wolf Heart Samples",z="undercity",s="In Silverpine Forest, wolf hearts hold a poison their living hosts endure. Apothecary Renferrel sends samples to the Royal Apothecary Society, whose members study them.",h="In Silverpine Forest, wolf hearts hold a poison their living hosts endure.",sec={{t="A Toxic Paradox",b="Apothecary Renferrel found a deadly compound in certain wolf hearts while examining carcasses in Silverpine Forest. The poison saturates the tissue at a level that should kill the wolves, yet they live. Renferrel set tissue samples aside for delivery to Undercity. The Forsaken study organisms that withstand toxins as they seek to master biological warfare and prepare new reagents.",sp=0},{t="Consignment to Undercity",b="Couriers carry the samples beneath the ruins of Lordaeron to Apothecary Zinge at the Royal Apothecary Society's headquarters in the Apothecarium. Zinge and her colleagues prize new toxins. They dissect and test the tainted tissue to isolate its virulent compounds and learn how the beasts survive them, hoping to use that knowledge in their alchemical work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are these wolf hearts significant to the Forsaken?",a="The wolf hearts contain intense, unexplained toxicity that should have killed their hosts. The Royal Apothecary Society wants to understand both the poison and how the wolves survive it.",al={"why are wolf hearts important","what makes the hearts special","why do apothecaries want wolf hearts"}},{q="Who requests these samples?",a="Apothecary Renferrel collected the samples after studying wolves in Silverpine Forest. He arranged for a courier to take them to his colleague, Apothecary Zinge, at the Society's headquarters in Undercity.",al={"who wants the wolf hearts","who sent the samples","who receives the samples"}},{q="What will Apothecary Zinge do with them?",a="Apothecary Zinge dissects and tests the samples. The Royal Apothecary Society catalogs and weaponizes new toxins to develop plagues and concoctions for Queen Sylvanas.",al={"what does zinge do with the hearts","zinge experiments","apothecary zinge research"}},{q="Where did the wolves originate?",a="The wolves came from Silverpine Forest, where dark magic, decay, and strange corruption afflict the wilds and alter the local fauna.",al={"where are the wolves from","silverpine wolves","wolf location"}},{q="What are the Wolf Heart Samples?",a="These are harvested tissue specimens preserved from corrupted wolves. Unlike ordinary beast remains, these hearts exhibit an extraordinary internal toxicity—a venomous quality so severe that, by rights, it should have proved fatal to the beasts while they still lived.",al={"what are wolf heart samples","wolf heart samples item","wolf heart samples"},it="identity",add="61543e32"},{q="Where do the Wolf Heart Samples come from?",a="They were prepared and portioned out by Apothecary Renferrel from the tainted wolf hearts you gathered for his research. Recognizing their unusual properties, Renferrel set aside these specific cuts to be carried directly to his peers in the Undercity.",al={"where did wolf heart samples come from","who made wolf heart samples","wolf heart samples source"},it="origin",add="33618b83"},{q="Why does anyone want the Wolf Heart Samples?",a="Apothecary Zinge and the Royal Apothecary Society seek them to investigate novel forms of poison. The unnatural venom coursing through the specimens offers fresh insight into virulent agents, which the apothecaries are eager to isolate, test, and adapt for their own lethal concoctions.",al={"why want wolf heart samples","who wants wolf heart samples","why does zinge want wolf heart samples"},it="why_wanted",add="6a0e6447"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you depend on the Royal Apothecary Society's pursuit of lethal reagents to defend the Forsaken against living and undead enemies alike."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","apothecary zinge","royal apothecary society","silverpine forest","toxin","undercity","wolf heart samples"},rel={"quest:1359","npc:apothecary-zinge","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:undercity","item:wolf-heart-sample"},src={"Wolf Heart Samples","Zinge's Delivery"}}
E["item:woven-wand"] = {t="item",n="Woven Wand",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, the Woven Wand has returned to Bethor Iceshard. Three Dalaran apprentices made it as a pledge of brotherhood, before betrayal and the fall of Lordaeron scattered them.",h="In the Undercity, the Woven Wand has returned to Bethor Iceshard.",sec={{t="The Hidden Alcove",b="Thule Ravenclaw could not destroy the wand or surrender it to his former friends, though he came to despise what it meant after turning to darkness. He carried it to Silverpine Forest and hid it in an alcove deep within Fenris Keep. Years later, Thule's lair was breached, and his servant Alaric directed Horde agents to the hiding place. They recovered the relic intact. Thule had never invoked its dormant enchantments, and the wand was delivered to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity's Magic Quarter.",sp=1},{t="A Sundered Bond",b="When Dalaran still trained the young magi of the north, apprentices Bethor Iceshard, Gunther Arcanus, and Thule Ravenclaw joined their wands into one talisman. The Woven Wand focused their combined magical power and marked their friendship. The Scourge's march through Lordaeron broke that bond. Thule swore fealty to the Lich King and turned to necromancy. The Plague of Undeath claimed Bethor and Gunther, severing their ties to Dalaran.",sp=1,bt={"q358.4"}}},faq={{q="Who created the Woven Wand?",a="Bethor Iceshard, Gunther Arcanus, and Thule Ravenclaw made the Woven Wand as Dalaran apprentices. They joined their three wands into one to mark their friendship.",al={"who made woven wand","creators of woven wand","wand creators"},sp=1,it="origin",bt={"q358.4"}},{q="Why was the wand hidden in Fenris Keep?",a="After Thule betrayed his former friends and served the Lich King, he despised the wand and what it represented. Still, he could neither destroy it nor part with it, so he hid it in an alcove in Fenris Keep.",al={"why did thule hide the wand","where was woven wand found","why fenris keep"},it="history"},{q="Why did Bethor Iceshard think the wand was lost?",a="Bethor believed the wand was lost when the plague ravaged the land and the apprentices' friendship broke apart. Thule never used its magic; Bethor would have sensed its power through their lingering magical link.",al={"what does bethor say about the wand","bethor reaction to wand"}},{q="How was the wand recovered?",a="Horde agents recovered the wand from Fenris Keep after breaching Thule Ravenclaw's lair. Alaric, his former servant, directed them to the hidden alcove.",al={"who found the wand","how to get woven wand"},sp=1},{q="What is the Woven Wand?",a="The Woven Wand is a enchanted relic woven together from the apprentice wands of three Dalaran magi: Thule Ravenclaw, Bethor Iceshard, and Gunther Arcanus. Created as a token of their early camaraderie, it binds their magical crafts into a single instrument. That bond shattered when Thule pledged himself to the Scourge and his companions were claimed by the plague.",al={"what is woven wand","woven wand lore","woven wand"},it="identity",add="de7c3f0d"},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard want the Woven Wand?",a="Bethor Iceshard believed the wand was lost forever when their fellowship fell apart and Thule Ravenclaw defected to the Lich King. Beyond its sentimental value from their mortal days studying in Dalaran, the wand holds dormant magical power that Thule never invoked—power Bethor feared falling into Scourge hands and is eager to keep secure.",al={"why does bethor want woven wand","why wand to bethor","who wants the woven wand"},it="why_wanted",add="a3970439"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how Dalaran's apprentices joined their personal wands to focus their shared arcane power.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you can see the wand as a reminder of mortal lives lost to the Scourge. It connects two Forsaken survivors in memory of their fallen former friend."},kw={"alaric","bethor iceshard","dalaran","fenris keep","gunther arcanus","magic quarter","thule ravenclaw","woven wand"},rel={"npc:bethor-iceshard","quest:491","quest:461","quest:446","subzone:fenris-keep","npc:gunther-arcanus","subzone:dalaran","subzone:magic-quarter"},src={"Woven Wand","Wand to Bethor"}}
E["npc:anastasia-hartwell"] = {t="npc",n="Anastasia Hartwell",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Anastasia Hartwell trains Forsaken and Horde mages in the arcane arts. She guides spellcasters in their studies and directs magical research and field work across Lordaeron and beyond.",h="In the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Anastasia Hartwell trains Forsaken and Horde mages in the arcane arts.",sec={{t="Arcane Mastery in the Ruins",b="In the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Anastasia Hartwell teaches Forsaken and Horde mages to channel arcane energies. Though Lordaeron has fallen to ruin, former human practitioners such as Anastasia preserve their scholarly traditions in undeath. She demands discipline in the practice of magic. Careless incantations can consume the untrained.",sp=0},{t="Field Research and Relics",b="Anastasia sends promising students into the field as well as teaching them spells. At Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal Glades, mages gather snapdragons to learn how far the plague has spread. In the Apothecarium, they visit Algernon's alchemist shop to capture invisible creatures of pure magic behind a strange disturbance. Her assignments bring them face to face with magic's dangers, even within their own city.",sp=0},{t="Allies of the Craft",b="Anastasia's connections reach beyond Tirisfal. As Horde spellcasters grow more skilled, she coordinates with trainers in distant lands, including Deino in Orgrimmar. She also directs advanced students to solitary masters such as Tabetha in the swamplands of Dustwallow Marsh. Her guidance keeps Forsaken mages connected to the Horde's wider magical pursuits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Anastasia Hartwell?",a="Anastasia Hartwell trains Forsaken mages in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. She teaches spells and assigns work retrieving arcane artifacts and reagents across Lordaeron.",al={"anastasia hartwell","who is anastasia","hartwell undercity"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Anastasia Hartwell?",a="You can find Anastasia Hartwell in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, among arcane practitioners and trainers beneath the city's vaulted subterranean ceilings.",al={"anastasia hartwell location","where is anastasia hartwell","undercity mage trainer location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Anastasia say to non-mages?",a="Anastasia warns non-mage visitors to beware of magic on their travels. It readily burns the untrained.",al={"anastasia gossip","anastasia dialogue","hartwell advice"}},{q="What quests does Anastasia Hartwell offer?",a="Anastasia gives mages training assignments, including gathering snapdragons at Balnir Farmstead and investigating a magical disturbance in an alchemist's shop in the Apothecarium. She also directs them to work with distant teachers such as Deino in Orgrimmar and Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"anastasia quests","hartwell tasks","undercity mage quests"},gp=true},{q="Is Anastasia Hartwell related to other Hartwells in Tirisfal?",a="Anastasia shares a surname with Andrew Hartwell and Geoffrey Hartwell, but their family relationship is unconfirmed.",al={"hartwell family","andrew hartwell","geoffrey hartwell"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Anastasia send mages to the Balnir Farmstead?",a="Anastasia asks mages to gather Balnir Snapdragons to measure the plague's spread in Tirisfal Glades and send the flowers to the apothecaries.",al={"balnir farmstead quest","why balnir farmstead","hartwell balnir"},it="motive"},{q="Whose side is Anastasia Hartwell on?",a="Anastasia Hartwell stands firmly with the Forsaken and the Horde. Stationed deep within the Undercity's Magic Quarter, she serves Lady Sylvanas Windrunner by preparing newly risen mages to harness the arcane in defense of their fledgling kingdom.",al={"anastasia hartwell faction","who does anastasia hartwell serve","anastasia hartwell loyalty"},it="side",add="686de903"},{q="Why is Anastasia Hartwell here?",a="She resides in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity to train aspiring Forsaken and Horde practitioners in the arcane arts. She offers guidance to fledgling spellcasters, warning the uninitiated of magic's perils while directing capable mages on critical missions across Lordaeron and beyond.",al={"why is anastasia hartwell in undercity","what is anastasia hartwell doing here","anastasia hartwell role"},it="why_here",add="bc0bb7e5"},{q="What does Anastasia Hartwell want?",a="She seeks to ensure that arcane practitioners are disciplined, capable, and cautious, frequently reminding outsiders that wild power burns the untrained. Through rigorous tasks and magical investigations, she works to strengthen the arcane capabilities of the Forsaken.",al={"anastasia hartwell goals","what are anastasia hartwell's motives"},it="wants",add="18e123e6"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can learn higher spell ranks from Anastasia Hartwell in the Undercity. She mentors Horde mages passing through and gives them important assignments.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see the arcane traditions of Dalaran and Lordaeron carried on among the Forsaken, despite the tragedy of undeath.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see Anastasia connect Lordaeron's arcane heritage with the Horde's wider magical work through trainers such as Deino in Orgrimmar."},kw={"anastasia","balnir","deino","forsaken","hartwell","lordaeron","mage","magic quarter","tabetha","trainer","undercity"},rel={"subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","quest:1882","quest:1960","quest:1943","npc:deino","npc:tabetha"},src={"Anastasia Hartwell"}}
E["npc:andron-gant"] = {t="npc",n="Andron Gant",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity's Apothecarium, Andron Gant handles occasional commissions and relic recoveries for local scholars. He is a reclusive Forsaken, often drunk, and rarely leaves the city.",h="In the Undercity's Apothecarium, Andron Gant handles occasional commissions and relic recoveries for local...",sec={{t="A Slurring Recluse",b="Andron Gant spends his time in the Apothecarium, among its noxious fumes, and rarely ventures beyond the Undercity's stone walls. He seems little more than a drunken scholar. For local mages, he sometimes hires couriers to seek obscure relics on distant shores, including the Tablet of Markri.",sp=0},{t="Unmasked by the Deathstalkers",b="The Undercity's intelligence network noticed Gant's treacherous dealings. The Syndicate sent Astor Hadren to collect a ledger of compromised data, but aspiring Deathstalker operatives intercepted the courier. One agent took Hadren's place and tricked the drunken Gant into handing over the incriminating ledger without raising suspicion. The ledger gave Lord Varimathras definitive proof of Gant's treason against the Forsaken.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Andron Gant?",a="Andron Gant can be found in the lower levels of the Apothecarium district, inside the Undercity.",al={"andron gant location","where is andron gant","gant undercity location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Andron Gant interested in Azshara tablets?",a="Gant arranges payments for certain Undercity mages, sending scavengers and contacts such as Jediga to recover ancient relics from the ruins of Azshara.",al={"andron gant azshara","tablet of markri andron gant","why does gant want tablets"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do the Deathstalkers investigate Andron Gant?",a="The Deathstalkers investigate Gant's dealings with outside contacts and seek intelligence about his research commissions.",al={"gant investigation","andron gant contacts","who does andron gant work for"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Who directs the investigation into Andron Gant?",a="The Deathstalkers investigate Gant on behalf of Lord Varimathras, seeking intelligence about his contacts and research.",al={"who investigates andron gant","deathstalkers andron gant","varimathras andron gant"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Who is Andron Gant?",a="Andron Gant is a Forsaken resident who frequents the Apothecarium in the Undercity. To outward appearances, he is little more than a habitual drunkard who rarely ventures outside the capital, acting as a broker for odd scholarly tasks like procuring ancient tablets for local mages.",al={"who is andron gant","andron gant lore","who is gant"},it="identity",add="1e42df39"},{q="Whose side is Andron Gant on?",a="While he lives among the Forsaken in the Undercity, Gant secretly works as an informant for the Syndicate. He gathers intelligence from within the capital and passes sensitive ledgers to Syndicate messengers, making him a covert traitor to the Dark Lady's realm.",al={"is andron gant loyal","who does andron gant serve","andron gant loyalty"},sp=1,it="side",add="24992602"},{q="What does Andron Gant want?",a="Publicly, Gant spends his time drinking and brokering curiosities, such as paying adventurers to retrieve relics like the Tablet of Markri from Azshara for the Undercity's mages. In secret, his main endeavor is compiling sensitive ledgers and intelligence to sell to the Syndicate.",al={"what does andron want","andron gant motives","andron gant goals"},sp=1,it="wants",add="e54869d5"},{q="Why is Andron Gant in the Undercity?",a="Gant stays sequestered in the Apothecarium under the pretense of being a harmless, drunken scholar and broker. The Undercity provides him the ideal cover to quietly gather intelligence and maintain a covert channel of communication with outside conspirators.",al={"why is andron gant here","why is andron in undercity","andron gant apothecarium"},sp=1,it="why_here",add="1151765b"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Forsaken rogue, you learn while rising through the Deathstalkers that the Undercity's halls demand as much vigilance as its borders.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you may know Gant as a familiar sight in the Apothecarium: a drunken Forsaken who rarely leaves the city and brokers odd errands for its mages."},kw={"andron gant","apothecarium","astor hadren","deathstalkers","jediga","tablet of markri","varimathras"},rel={"npc:varimathras","subzone:apothecarium","topic:syndicate","topic:forsaken","zone:undercity","zone:azshara"},src={"Andron Gant"}}
E["npc:austil-de-mon"] = {t="npc",n="Austil de Mon",z="undercity",s="In Brill, Austil de Mon trains Forsaken warriors at Gallows' End Tavern. He teaches the newly risen to fight in service of the Dark Lady.",h="In Brill, Austil de Mon trains Forsaken warriors at Gallows' End Tavern.",sec={{t="A Veteran in Gallows' End",b="Austil de Mon trains Forsaken warriors inside Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. Warriors leaving Deathknell come to him among their first instructors. The living once drank and rested in the inn. Now Austil teaches newly liberated undead to master martial discipline and combat against the foes surrounding the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Austil de Mon?",a="Austil de Mon trains undead warriors in Brill, Tirisfal Glades, teaching Forsaken fighters.",al={"austil de mon","austil","who is austil"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Austil de Mon?",a="You can find Austil de Mon in Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, Tirisfal Glades, just north of the Undercity.",al={"austil de mon location","where is austil","austil de mon map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does he play in Brill?",a="Austil teaches novice warriors fighting techniques, stances, and martial abilities, strengthening the Forsaken military against local threats.",al={"what does austil do","austil trainer","austil role"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Austil de Mon on?",a="Austil de Mon is loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, Queen Sylvanas Windrunner. As part of the nascent undead kingdom carved from Lordaeron's ruins, he serves alongside his brethren in the Horde, offering his martial experience to hone the strength of incoming Forsaken warriors fighting to defend Tirisfal Glades from the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade.",al={"austil de mon faction","austil de mon loyalty","who does austil serve"},it="side",add="00da3c5d"},{q="What does Austil de Mon want?",a="Austil de Mon seeks to strengthen the Forsaken military line against Lordaeron's many enemies. By training freshly awakened warriors at Gallows' End Tavern, he works to ensure that those who take up arms under the Dark Lady possess the discipline and technique required to survive against both the relentless Scourge and the fanatical zealots of the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"austil de mon goal","what does austil want","austil de mon purpose"},it="wants",add="d899e308"},{q="Why is Austil de Mon in Brill?",a="Austil is stationed at Gallows' End Tavern in Brill to greet and drill fighters emerging from Deathknell. Because Brill serves as the primary outpost and logistical center for northern Tirisfal Glades, warrior trainers like Austil are essential to turn newly risen undead into capable front-line combatants before they march deeper into contested territory.",al={"why is austil in brill","why is austil de mon here","austil de mon location why"},it="why_here",add="aed6134f"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a Forsaken warrior leaving Deathknell, you can seek Austil de Mon as a mentor for guidance and formal ability training in Tirisfal Glades.",["race:Undead"]="As newly risen undead, you can train with Austil to become a frontline fighter ready to defend Lordaeron against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade."},kw={"austil de mon","brill","forsaken warrior","gallows' end tavern","tirisfal glades","warrior trainer"},rel={"subzone:brill","subzone:gallows-end-tavern","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:1818"},src={"Austil de Mon"}}
E["npc:bethor-iceshard"] = {t="npc",n="Bethor Iceshard",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Bethor Iceshard commands the Magic Quarter's arcane and shadow practitioners. He holds authority in Sylvanas's realm, while old friendships still shape his past.",h="In the Undercity, Bethor Iceshard commands the Magic Quarter's arcane and shadow practitioners.",sec={{t="Master of the Magic Quarter",b="Bethor Iceshard directs arcane and shadow practitioners from the Temple of the Damned in the Undercity. His intellect and icy resolve earn both respect and fear. He has the political and magical weight to instruct provincial magistrates across Lordaeron. Bethor sends Forsaken agents to secure valuable grimoires, investigate arcane anomalies, and suppress rival powers that threaten the Undercity's dominion.",sp=0},{t="Old Friends and Bittersweet Reunions",b="Bethor Iceshard still remembers his former companions. He tracks powerful undead spellcasters across Tirisfal and Silverpine, sending agents to learn whether rogue practitioners serve the Lich King or might join the Forsaken cause. When he finds Gunther Arcanus raising the dead at Brightwater Lake, Bethor patiently works to bring his old friend into Lady Sylvanas's fold. Thule Ravenclaw receives no such mercy; his willing betrayal doomed their brotherhood.",sp=1,bt={"q358.4"}},{t="Bonds of Apprenticehood",b="Before the Third War devastated Lordaeron, Bethor Iceshard studied magic as a mortal apprentice beside his close companions, Gunther Arcanus and Thule Ravenclaw. The three wove their practice wands together to mark their fellowship. The Scourge shattered that bond. As death and dark magic swept the kingdom, Thule willingly gave his soul to the Lich King. Gunther perished and rose again on an isolated island in Brightwater Lake. Bethor succumbed as well, then broke free as Forsaken.",sp=1,bt={"q358.4"}}},faq={{q="Who is Bethor Iceshard?",a="Bethor Iceshard commands arcane and shadow practitioners at the Temple of the Damned in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. He directs magical research, intelligence on rogue practitioners, and covert arcane operations for the Dark Lady.",al={"bethor iceshard","who is bethor","bethor lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Bethor Iceshard be found?",a="Bethor Iceshard resides inside the Temple of the Damned, in the Undercity's Magic Quarter.",al={"where is bethor","bethor location","find bethor iceshard"},it="why_here",gp=true},{q="What is Bethor's history with Gunther Arcanus?",a="Bethor Iceshard and Gunther Arcanus were close friends and fellow apprentice mages in Lordaeron. Both died during the Scourge invasion and later broke free from the Lich King's control. Bethor arranged for Gunther to join the Forsaken.",al={"gunther and bethor","gunther arcanus friendship","how does bethor know gunther"},sp=1,it="ties",bt={"q358.4"}},{q="Who was Thule Ravenclaw to Bethor?",a="Thule Ravenclaw was the third member of Bethor Iceshard and Gunther Arcanus's apprentice circle. During the Scourge invasion, he willingly pledged his soul to the Lich King and became a hated necromancer living at Fenris Isle.",al={"thule ravenclaw connection","thule and bethor","bethor ravenclaw"},sp=1,it="ties",bt={"q437.6"}},{q="What is the story behind Bethor's wand?",a="As young apprentices, Bethor Iceshard, Gunther Arcanus, and Thule Ravenclaw wove their practice wands together as a sign of eternal friendship. The braided keepsake connects the three fractured spellcasters to their mortal past.",al={"woven wand","wand to bethor","bethor apprentice wand"},it="item"},{q="What role does Bethor play in Forsaken society?",a="Bethor Iceshard is one of the Undercity's leading arcane authorities. He guides newly risen magi and warlocks, directs intelligence on rogue necromancers, and holds authority over regional Forsaken civil officials such as magistrate Sevren.",al={"bethor role","what does bethor do","bethor authority"},it="fame"},{q="Whose side is Bethor Iceshard on?",a="Bethor is fully devoted to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. From his sanctum in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, he commands significant authority within the Forsaken hierarchy, directing arcane practitioners and marshaling resources against the Scourge and other threats to their people.",al={"bethor iceshard faction","bethor iceshard allegiance","who does bethor serve"},it="side",add="31504eb7"},{q="What does Bethor Iceshard want?",a="Bethor seeks to strengthen the Forsaken's arcane power and safeguard their fledgling kingdom. This includes recruiting gifted practitioners like his former friend Gunther Arcanus to the Forsaken cause, while ruthlessly confronting the Scourge and holding traitors like Thule Ravenclaw accountable for selling their souls to the Lich King.",al={"bethor iceshard goals","what does bethor want","bethor iceshard motives"},it="wants",add="14082dd0"},{q="Why is Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity?",a="Bethor presides over the Temple of the Damned in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, serving as a leader for the Forsaken's mages and warlocks. He remains here to orchestrate arcane affairs, guide promising spellcasters, and coordinate strategic efforts across Lordaeron from the heart of the capital.",al={"why is bethor in undercity","bethor iceshard location lore","why is bethor here"},it="why_here",add="50a70545"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Forsaken mage, you can see in Bethor Iceshard how the arcane arts endure through undeath.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you may know the pain of losing friends and home to the Scourge, then facing former allies as enemies.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you benefit from Bethor Iceshard's offensive magic and counter-necromancy efforts, which protect the Horde's foothold across Lordaeron."},kw={"bethor iceshard","forsaken","gunther arcanus","magic quarter","prodigal lich","temple of the damned","thule ravenclaw","undercity"},rel={"npc:gunther-arcanus","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:405","quest:411","quest:446","quest:491","topic:forsaken"},src={"Bethor Iceshard"}}
E["npc:cain-firesong"] = {t="npc",n="Cain Firesong",z="undercity",s="At the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, Cain Firesong guides Forsaken mages in the arcane. He trains them in Tirisfal Glades before sending advanced students to the Undercity for deeper study.",h="At the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, Cain Firesong guides Forsaken mages in the arcane.",sec={{t="A Practitioner in Brill",b="Cain Firesong teaches traditional arcane arts in Brill, where Forsaken mages begin their studies. Many Forsaken spellcasters turn to shadow or necromancy, but Cain keeps to the arcane. He mentors mages who set out from Deathknell. The Deathguards point visitors to the upstairs landing of the Gallows' End Tavern, where Cain can be found. They joke that he arrived too late to get a room.",sp=0},{t="Guiding New Talent",b="Cain sends capable students onward when they outgrow their first studies in Tirisfal Glades. He directs them to Anastasia Hartwell, a master sorceress who lives in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Cain Firesong?",a="Cain Firesong trains Forsaken mages in Brill, in Tirisfal Glades. He teaches them arcane spells and directs advanced students to continue their studies in the Undercity.",al={"who is cain firesong","cain firesong lore","cain firesong brill"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Cain Firesong stay in Brill?",a="Cain Firesong can be found on the upstairs landing of the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. The local Deathguards joke that he arrived too late to get a room.",al={"where is cain firesong","cain firesong location","cain tavern room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where does Cain send mages after their initial training?",a="Cain sends mages who advance under his guidance to the Undercity's Magic Quarter, where Anastasia Hartwell continues their instruction.",al={"cain firesong quest","who does cain send mages to","speak with anastasia"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Cain Firesong on?",a="Cain Firesong stands firmly with the Forsaken and the Horde. Stationed in Brill, he serves the Dark Lady by schooling newly risen undead in the arcane arts, ensuring that Forsaken spellcasters have the magical prowess needed to defend Tirisfal Glades and advance the realm of the Undercity.",al={"cain firesong faction","cain firesong loyalty","who does cain firesong serve"},it="side",add="265be98f"},{q="What does Cain Firesong want?",a="Cain aims to hone the arcane discipline of fledgling Forsaken mages before sending them onward to master trainers in the Undercity.",al={"cain firesong goal","what is cain firesong doing","cain firesong purpose"},it="wants",add="5ce3d117"},{q="Why is Cain Firesong here?",a="Cain is stationed in Brill to instruct young mages emerging from Deathknell. He can be found on the upstairs landing of the Gallows' End Tavern.",al={"why is cain firesong in brill","cain firesong location reason","why is cain firesong here"},it="why_here",add="f96c1f09"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Forsaken mage setting out from Deathknell, you can learn the arcane from Cain Firesong in Tirisfal Glades before continuing your studies in the Undercity.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you can wield the arcane traditions of former human magi as a weapon for the Forsaken."},kw={"anastasia hartwell","arcane","brill","cain firesong","gallows' end tavern","mage trainer","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","quest:1881","quest:1959","subzone:gallows-end-tavern","topic:forsaken"},src={"Cain Firesong"}}
E["npc:carendin-halgar"] = {t="npc",n="Carendin Halgar",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Carendin Halgar trains Forsaken warlocks in the dark arts. Sharp-tongued and impatient, he teaches them to bind demons from the Twisting Nether, including Voidwalkers and Succubi.",h="In the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Carendin Halgar trains Forsaken warlocks in the dark arts.",sec={{t="Master of the Dark Arts",b="Carendin Halgar trains warlocks in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. He demands focus and obedience, with little patience for failure, hesitation, or weakness. His students move beyond simple incantations to summon demons and manipulate souls. Under his direction, they learn the Forsaken way of making demons serve.",sp=0},{t="Subjugating the Nether",b="Carendin Halgar teaches warlocks to bind dangerous demons to their will. He sends students across Lordaeron and beyond to gather ancient runes, runic stones, and pure mortal essence for summoning circles. His lessons cover creatures of the void and Succubi. Before a warlock can command a demon, the summoner must bind it, lest it devour its master.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can Carendin Halgar be found?",a="Carendin Halgar can be found in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, among practitioners of fel and shadow magic.",al={"carendin halgar location","undercity warlock trainer location","where is halgar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Carendin Halgar play for warlocks?",a="Carendin Halgar mentors Horde warlocks in the rituals for summoning and binding demons, including Voidwalkers and Succubi.",al={"what does carendin do","halgar purpose","carendin quests"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Carendin Halgar's personality like?",a="Carendin Halgar is blunt and demanding, with little patience. He expects quick results and despises wasted time and excuses.",al={"halgar temperament","is carendin nice","carendin halgar lore"}},{q="Why does Carendin require pure hearts for summoning rituals?",a="In lessons on summoning a Succubus, Carendin Halgar's assistant Godrick Farsan sends acolytes to obtain the untainted hearts of the pure. Their innocence and essence lure the demon into a binding circle.",al={"hearts of the pure purpose","succubus summoning carendin","why hearts of the pure"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Does Carendin Halgar interact with warlocks outside the Undercity?",a="Yes. Carendin Halgar sends promising students to Strahad Farsan in the Barrens to continue their studies.",al={"carendin connections","halgar orgrimmar","gan'rul bloodeye carendin"}},{q="Who does Carendin send advanced warlocks to see?",a="Carendin Halgar sends acolytes who have mastered basic demons to seek further instruction, including from the eccentric summoner Strahad Farsan in the Barrens.",al={"seeking strahad","who does carendin send you to","halgar next mentor"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Carendin Halgar?",a="Carendin Halgar is a prominent Forsaken warlock trainer residing in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Known for his stern and impatient demeanor, he instructs aspiring practitioners in the dark arts of summoning and binding demonic entities to their will.",al={"who is carendin halgar","carendin halgar lore","who is halgar"},it="identity",add="3b100529"},{q="Whose side is Carendin Halgar on?",a="Carendin is loyal to the Forsaken and the Horde. He operates openly from the Undercity, dedicating his dark expertise to strengthening the magical might of Lady Sylvanas's followers against their shared enemies across Lordaeron.",al={"carendin halgar faction","who does carendin serve","is carendin loyal to sylvanas"},it="side",add="b7e57faa"},{q="What does Carendin Halgar want?",a="Carendin seeks to shape disciplined, capable warlocks who command demons without hesitation or weakness. He demands rigorous adherence to binding rituals and tests his students thoroughly to ensure they control their summoned servitors rather than falling victim to them.",al={"what does carendin want","carendin halgar motives","carendin halgar goals"},it="wants",add="ba046d55"},{q="Why is Carendin Halgar here?",a="He is stationed in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity to mentor emerging Forsaken warlocks. Beneath the ruins of Capital City, he oversees the hazardous summonings necessary to bind greater minions of the Twisting Nether into service.",al={"why is carendin in undercity","why is carendin halgar here","carendin halgar location reason"},it="why_here",add="ea246188"},{q="Who is Carendin Halgar tied to?",a="Carendin's assistant is Godrick Farsan. He also sends students to the summoner Strahad Farsan in the Barrens for further instruction.",al={"carendin halgar allies","carendin halgar connections","who does carendin work with"},it="ties",add="743d4acc"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can learn from Carendin Halgar in Lordaeron as he guides you through trials to bind Voidwalkers and Succubi.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you may recognize the Forsaken spirit in Carendin Halgar: he treats demons as tools to break and exploit, without pity or hesitation.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can look to Carendin Halgar for eastern warlock training and his coordination with dark practitioners across the sea in Kalimdor."},kw={"carendin halgar","creature of the void","forsaken","halgar","magic quarter","succubus","the binding","trainer","undercity","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:1473","quest:1471","quest:1476","quest:1472","quest:1798","npc:gan-rul-bloodeye"},src={"Carendin Halgar"}}
E["npc:elder-darkcore"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Darkcore",z="undercity",s="During the Lunar Festival, Elder Darkcore keeps watch in the throne room above the Undercity. He honors the world's ancestors and blesses travelers who come to pay their respects.",h="During the Lunar Festival, Elder Darkcore keeps watch in the throne room above the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Spirit in the Throne Room",b="During the Lunar Festival, ancient elders appear across Azeroth to share their wisdom with travelers. Elder Darkcore keeps watch in the throne room of the Ruins of Lordaeron, directly above the Undercity entrance. King Terenas Menethil II fell on the blood-stained floor there. Those who enter the heart of Forsaken territory to pay their respects receive a Coin of Ancestry and his blessing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Darkcore?",a="During the Lunar Festival, Elder Darkcore appears as one of the honored ancestral spirits. In the throne room above the Undercity, he gives visitors blessings and Coins of Ancestry.",al={"elder darkcore","darkcore","who is darkcore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Elder Darkcore?",a="Elder Darkcore waits in Capital City's ruined throne room, in the Ruins of Lordaeron above the Undercity entrance.",al={"where is darkcore","darkcore location","undercity elder"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Elder Darkcore hostile to the Alliance?",a="Elder Darkcore is neutral and welcomes travelers who come to honor him. Alliance visitors must evade hostile guards patrolling the Forsaken stronghold in the Ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"can alliance talk to darkcore","is darkcore horde","undercity lunar festival alliance"},it="hostile",gp=true},{q="What does honoring Elder Darkcore give you?",a="Paying respects to Elder Darkcore earns a Coin of Ancestry.",al={"darkcore reward","darkcore quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Elder Darkcore on?",a="Elder Darkcore does not align with the modern conflicts of the Horde or Alliance. As an honored ancestral spirit participating in the Lunar Festival, he stands peacefully above mortal squabbles, welcoming any traveler who approaches him with respect, regardless of which banner they march under.",al={"elder darkcore faction","is elder darkcore horde or alliance","darkcore allegiance"},it="side",add="3a0e846b"},{q="What does Elder Darkcore want?",a="Elder Darkcore seeks to share the ancient wisdom and blessings of the ancestors during the Lunar Festival. He waits for travelers to pay their respects to the past, offering his blessing and tokens of elder heritage to those who honor his long-enduring memory.",al={"what does elder darkcore want","elder darkcore purpose","why visit elder darkcore"},it="wants",add="32c6e8a4"},{q="Why is Elder Darkcore in the Ruins of Lordaeron?",a="Elder Darkcore appears in the ruined throne room above the Undercity as part of the worldwide observance of the Lunar Festival. The spirits of the ancients manifest in places steeped in profound history and sorrow across Azeroth, allowing mortals to commune with ancestral memories even amid fallen kingdoms.",al={"why is elder darkcore in undercity","why ruins of lordaeron darkcore","elder darkcore location lore"},it="why_here",add="e5445cfd"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you must slip past high-level Forsaken sentries and royal guards around Capital City's ruins to reach Elder Darkcore. That makes him one of the festival's most perilous stops for you.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you find Elder Darkcore only steps from the Undercity's surface elevators, on the very stones where the kingdom of Lordaeron was torn down."},kw={"ancestor","coin of ancestry","darkcore","elder darkcore","lunar festival","ruins of lordaeron","throne room","undercity"},rel={"quest:8648","zone:undercity","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Elder Darkcore"}}
E["npc:godrick-farsan"] = {t="npc",n="Godrick Farsan",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity’s Magic Quarter, Godrick Farsan aids Forsaken warlocks beside Carendin Halgar. Though blind, he says he sees in a different way.",h="In the Undercity’s Magic Quarter, Godrick Farsan aids Forsaken warlocks beside Carendin Halgar.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Dark",b="Among the summoning circles in the Magic Quarter, Godrick Farsan aids Master Carendin Halgar as he guides aspiring Forsaken warlocks. Godrick is blind, yet says he sees in a different way and does not explain how. He tests those who seek to bind greater demons, sending them to gather pure hearts and essences for intricate summoning rites.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Godrick Farsan?",a="Godrick Farsan is a Forsaken warlock in the Undercity’s Magic Quarter. He assists Master Carendin Halgar in teaching fledgling warlocks and guiding their rituals.",al={"godrick farsan","who is godrick"},it="identity"},{q="How can Godrick see if he is blind?",a="Godrick Farsan says he sees in a different way despite his blindness. He does not explain how.",al={"is godrick blind","how does godrick see"}},{q="Is Godrick related to Strahad Farsan?",a="Godrick Farsan and Strahad Farsan share a surname, but no family connection is confirmed.",al={"strahad farsan relation","strahad farsan brother","are godrick and strahad related"},it="ties"},{q="What role does he play in warlock training?",a="Godrick Farsan guides warlocks through binding rites, including acquiring pure hearts to lure and bind a succubus.",al={"godrick warlock quests","hearts of the pure quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Godrick Farsan on?",a="Godrick is loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, dwelling deep within the Undercity. He serves alongside Carendin Halgar, aiding practitioners of the dark arts and guiding Horde warlocks who seek to master demonic powers.",al={"godrick farsan allegiance","who does godrick serve","godrick farsan faction"},it="side",add="5d2f41c4"},{q="Why is Godrick Farsan here?",a="You will find Godrick lurking in the shadowy quarters of the Undercity as the devoted assistant to Carendin Halgar. He remains stationed here to oversee trials for aspiring warlocks, helping them bind potent demonic entities such as the succubus.",al={"why is godrick in undercity","godrick farsan purpose undercity","what is godrick farsan doing here"},it="why_here",add="f8f4201c"},{q="What does Godrick Farsan want?",a="Godrick seeks to further the dark studies of the Undercity's warlocks. Through grueling trials involving ritual components—such as the hearts of the pure and the innocent—he tests your resolve and ability to command dangerous demons of the Nether.",al={"godrick farsan goal","what does godrick want","godrick farsan motives"},it="wants",add="57b226ed"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can consult Godrick to prepare lures for summoning a succubus and learn the devouring nature of demonic servants.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you can see Godrick embracing physical ruin and blindness while honing dark magical awareness to replace mortal frailties."},kw={"carendin halgar","godrick farsan","hearts of the pure","strahad farsan","succubus","undercity","warlock"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1476","quest:1472","npc:strahad-farsan","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},src={"Godrick Farsan"}}
E["npc:gordon-wendham"] = {t="npc",n="Gordon Wendham",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity's Trade Quarter, Gordon Wendham sells weapons and helps couriers from the surface find their way.",h="In the Undercity's Trade Quarter, Gordon Wendham sells weapons and helps couriers from the surface find their...",sec={{t="Armaments of the Trade Quarter",b="Gordon Wendham sells weapons to those who take up arms for the Forsaken. His stock ranges from daggers and hand axes to broadswords and maces. Fledgling fighters can find dependable iron here before they venture into the contested reaches of Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="A Courier's Destination",b="Travelers sent by flight masters and couriers are often directed to Gordon Wendham's stall. Some arrive from the bat handlers atop the ruins. His place in the Trade Quarter makes him easy to find when travelers need supplies or have dispatches to carry through the underground city.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gordon Wendham?",a="Gordon Wendham sells weapons in the Undercity's Trade Quarter and helps couriers arriving from the surface.",al={"gordon wendham lore","who is wendham","undercity gordon"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Gordon Wendham located?",a="You can find Gordon Wendham at his weapon stall in the Trade Quarter, within the Undercity's underground halls.",al={"gordon wendham location","where is gordon undercity","trade quarter weapon vendor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does he sell?",a="He sells basic weapons, including swords, daggers, maces, staves, axes and thrown weapons.",al={"wendham wares","what does gordon sell","gordon wendham weapons"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What quests involve him?",a="Gordon Wendham receives deliveries from the surface bat roosts, including deliveries from bat handler Michael Garrett.",al={"gordon wendham quests","ride to the undercity","michael garrett quest"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Gordon Wendham on?",a="Gordon Wendham is loyal to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken, standing aligned with the broader Horde. From his shop in the Undercity, he supports his undead kin by outfitting travelers and soldiers defending their reclaimed kingdom beneath the ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"gordon wendham faction","who does gordon wendham serve","is gordon wendham horde"},it="side",add="84654bd5"},{q="Why is Gordon Wendham in the Undercity?",a="Gordon Wendham plies his trade as a weaponsmith in the bustling Trade Quarter of the Undercity. Surrounded by the subterranean halls of the Forsaken capital, he remains on hand to supply blades, axes, and bludgeons to anyone preparing to venture into the hostile lands above.",al={"why is gordon wendham here","gordon wendham purpose undercity","what brings gordon wendham here"},it="why_here",add="d70aab3f"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken newly freed from Deathknell, you can find merchants like Gordon Wendham in the Trade Quarter, supplying the young nation's war effort.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can buy dependable basic blades and blunt weapons from Gordon Wendham to practice your weapon skills in the capital."},kw={"forsaken","gordon wendham","michael garrett","trade quarter","undercity","weapon vendor"},rel={"subzone:trade-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:6323","quest:6322","topic:forsaken","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Gordon Wendham"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-norman"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Norman",z="undercity",s="Innkeeper Norman keeps the Trade Quarter tavern ready for travelers in the Undercity. The quiet, diligent Forsaken offers Horde travelers rest, hearthstone bindings, and food for the living and the dead.",h="Innkeeper Norman keeps the Trade Quarter tavern ready for travelers in the Undercity.",sec={{t="Hospitality in the Sewers",b="Beneath Lordaeron's ruined capital, Innkeeper Norman tends the main tavern in the Undercity's Trade Quarter. Emissaries, mercenaries, and adventurers passing through the Forsaken stronghold find lodging there. Travelers come to bind their hearthstones, share news from across Azeroth, or prepare for journeys into the Plaguelands.",sp=0},{t="Festive Eccentricities",b="Innkeeper Norman sells provisions and manages rooms through most of the year. During Hallow's End, he joins the holiday revelry and asks adventurous patrons for peculiar displays, such as clucking like a chicken. Those who oblige can earn holiday treats like Undercity mints.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Innkeeper Norman?",a="Innkeeper Norman keeps the main tavern along the southern curve of the Undercity's inner ring, in the Trade Quarter.",al={"norman location","undercity innkeeper location","where is norman"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does Innkeeper Norman provide?",a="Innkeeper Norman offers rooms, hearthstone bindings, and food and drink suited to the living and the undead. Travelers can also rest there and earn rest while away.",al={"norman services","undercity hearthstone"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why does Norman ask patrons to cluck like a chicken?",a="During Hallow's End, Innkeeper Norman asks patrons to cluck like a chicken as part of the holiday trickery. Adventurers who swallow their pride can earn special holiday mints.",al={"chicken clucking mints","norman chicken quest"}},{q="Is Norman related to Innkeeper Bates?",a="No kinship between Innkeeper Norman and Innkeeper Bates is known, and neither mentions the other in life or undeath. Their shared name is a playful nod to Norman Bates from the film Psycho.",al={"norman bates connection","innkeeper bates norman"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Innkeeper Norman?",a="Innkeeper Norman is a Forsaken barkeep who tends the bustling tavern in the Undercity's Trade Quarter. While many undead have abandoned the comforts of their mortal lives, Norman caters to the weary travelers, soldiers, and emissaries making their way through Lady Sylvanas's subterranean stronghold, offering food, drink, and a place to rest.",al={"who is norman","innkeeper norman lore","norman undercity"},it="identity",add="543a0ebc"},{q="Whose side is Innkeeper Norman on?",a="Norman is loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, and by extension serves the broader Horde. Located in the heart of the Trade Quarter, he opens his doors to visiting orcs, trolls, and tauren, offering them shelter beneath the ruins of Lordaeron while remaining fiercely devoted to his undead kin.",al={"norman faction","norman allegiance","is norman horde"},it="side",add="bc99de77"},{q="Why is Innkeeper Norman here?",a="Norman manages the primary inn of the Undercity, stationed directly in the Trade Quarter where trade, travel, and politics intersect. Even in undeath, visitors and citizens need a gathering place to exchange rumors, bind hearthstones, and stock up on provisions, and Norman keeps the tavern running smoothly amid the gloom.",al={"why is norman in undercity","norman trade quarter","what is norman doing here"},it="why_here",add="58ea57aa"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For living Horde allies, Innkeeper Norman's tavern offers a secure place to rest and recover in the otherwise unwelcoming fortress beneath the Undercity.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you can rest at Innkeeper Norman's gathering place in the heart of the Trade Quarter between assignments for the Dark Lady."},kw={"bates","hallow's end","hearthstone","innkeeper","norman","trade quarter","undercity"},rel={"subzone:trade-quarter","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","quest:8353","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Innkeeper Norman"}}
E["npc:josef-gregorian"] = {t="npc",n="Josef Gregorian",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity’s Magic Quarter, Josef Gregorian trains tailors of the Horde. His skill guides them toward enchanted fabrics and specialized garments.",h="In the Undercity’s Magic Quarter, Josef Gregorian trains tailors of the Horde.",sec={{t="Weaver of the Magic Quarter",b="Josef Gregorian teaches tailoring in the Undercity’s Magic Quarter, where Forsaken and their Horde allies practice the craft. Tailoring remains vital to warlocks, mages, and priests who channel raw energies through woven fibers. Gregorian teaches foundational patterns and stitches the first robes for young mages who bring him the right materials.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Josef Gregorian?",a="Josef Gregorian works and teaches in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, among the city’s casters and scholars.",al={"josef gregorian location","where is gregorian","undercity tailor trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Josef Gregorian serve in the Undercity?",a="Josef Gregorian trains Horde crafters in sewing patterns and techniques. He also stitches the first robes for young mages sent to him by Anastasia Hartwell.",al={"what does josef gregorian do","josef gregorian trainer","undercity tailoring"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What quests does Josef Gregorian offer?",a="Anastasia Hartwell sends young mages to Josef Gregorian with linen cloth and Dalaran mana gems taken in Silverpine. He uses the materials to stitch them a set of Lesser Spellfire Robes.",al={"josef gregorian quests","robe quests undercity"},gp=true},{q="Who is Josef Gregorian?",a="Josef Gregorian is an undead artisan who serves as a tailoring trainer within the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Like many Forsaken craftsmen, he has retained the fine skills of his former life, putting his knowledge of thread, cloth, and enchanted garments to work for Queen Sylvanas's people and their Horde allies.",al={"who is josef gregorian","josef gregorian lore","who is the tailor josef gregorian"},it="identity",add="d179720d"},{q="Whose side is Josef Gregorian on?",a="He is loyal to the Forsaken and the Horde. Stationed deep within the Undercity, he offers his tailoring knowledge, patterns, and trade wisdom exclusively to those who stand in service to the Dark Lady and the Horde.",al={"josef gregorian faction","is josef gregorian horde","who does josef gregorian serve"},it="side",add="057f78ac"},{q="Why is Josef Gregorian in the Undercity?",a="Josef remains in the Undercity to practice and instruct others in the craft of tailoring. Setting up his workshop among the spellcasters and scholars of the Magic Quarter allows him to weave robes, enchanted garments, and cloth armor for adventurers venturing out into the Plaguelands and beyond.",al={"why is josef gregorian here","what brought josef gregorian to undercity","why is josef in the magic quarter"},it="why_here",add="3b87a245"}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="For Horde clothiers, Josef Gregorian is a tailoring instructor in Lordaeron who also stitches robes for young mages who bring him the materials.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead tailor, Josef Gregorian carries on the delicate art of human tailoring, which survived Lordaeron’s fall and now serves Forsaken society."},kw={"gathering materials","josef gregorian","magic quarter","spellfire robes","tailoring trainer","undercity"},rel={"subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:1961","quest:1962","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Josef Gregorian"}}
E["npc:master-apothecary-faranell"] = {t="npc",n="Master Apothecary Faranell",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Master Apothecary Faranell leads the Royal Apothecary Society from the depths of the Apothecarium. Once a respected Dalaran scholar, he now directs the Forsaken's search for a New Plague to destroy the Scourge and the living.",h="In the Undercity, Master Apothecary Faranell leads the Royal Apothecary Society from the depths of the...",sec={{t="A Mind Unhinged by Death",b="Before the Third War, Faranell spent decades studying alchemy alongside Dalaran's learned mages. In life, he sought cures, remedies, and potions to improve mortal health. The Scourge plague killed him, but he rose again as a free-willed Forsaken. His scientific curiosity turned cruel, and he traded healing salves for catastrophic reagents. His encyclopedic knowledge made him one of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner's most valued researchers in the depths of Lordaeron's fallen capital.",sp=0},{t="The Master of the Apothecarium",b="From the Apothecarium, Faranell coordinates the Royal Apothecary Society's far-reaching research. He oversees the construction of lumbering abominations and directs apothecaries stationed throughout Lordaeron and beyond. Field researchers gather strange venom, tainted blood, and cursed flora across the continents. Each batch passes through his vats for distillation and refinement.",sp=0},{t="Crafting the New Plague",b="Faranell works to fulfill the Dark Lady's command and uncover the New Plague. He seeks a contagion that can destroy Arthas and his mindless Scourge legions. To that end, he coordinates the gathering of many reagents. He sends adventurers to recover the research notes of his fallen colleague Apothecary Berard from Pyrewood Village. He seeks bat guano from the deep dens of Razorfen Kraul and tests acidic colloids against the organs of zealots from the Scarlet Monastery.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Faranell heads the Royal Apothecary Society, the alchemical guild serving Lady Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity. He oversees research into toxins, stitched abominations, and the New Plague.",al={"who is faranell","faranell lore","apothecary leader"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Faranell be found?",a="Faranell resides in the Apothecarium, the alchemical quarter in the Undercity's western sector. Bubbling cauldrons and testing cages surround him, along with his apothecary subordinates.",al={"faranell location","where is master apothecary faranell","find faranell"},it="why_here",gp=true},{q="What was Faranell's background before he died?",a="Before his death, Faranell was an acclaimed alchemist and doctor who studied with Dalaran's wizards. He invented remedies to heal disease, until the plague killed him and turned his curiosity toward lethal toxins.",al={"faranell history","was faranell in dalaran","faranell mortal life"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society trying to create?",a="At Queen Sylvanas's direction, the Royal Apothecary Society is creating a New Plague. The society seeks a weapon virulent enough to destroy the Scourge and avenge the Forsaken against the Lich King, while defending them from mortal enemies.",al={"what is the new plague","what are apothecaries making","apothecary goals"},it="wants"},{q="Why does Faranell send adventurers to Pyrewood Village?",a="Faranell seeks the research journal of his former colleague, Apothecary Berard, who went mad and succumbed to the worgen curse in Pyrewood. Berard's field notes hold critical data on toxic agents needed to refine the plague experiments.",al={"recipe for death quest faranell","why pyrewood village","apothecary berard journal"}},{q="Why does he need reagents from Razorfen Kraul and the Scarlet Monastery?",a="Faranell tests how volatile compounds interact. He uses kraul guano from razorfen quilboar dens and freshly harvested hearts of Scarlet Crusade zealots to test acidic colloids and biological contamination.",al={"kraul guano faranell","hearts of zeal","scarlet monastery hearts"}},{q="Whose side is Master Apothecary Faranell on?",a="Faranell is devoted entirely to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. As Master of the Royal Apothecary Society, he aligns his research directly with the Dark Lady's ambitions, mobilizing his alchemists to eradicate their enemies and secure the undead nation's survival, whatever the moral cost.",al={"faranell allegiance","who does faranell serve","is faranell loyal to sylvanas"},it="side",add="90cc21c1"},{q="Why is Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity?",a="Faranell oversees the Apothecarium, the alchemical heart of the Undercity. From this sprawling laboratory of bubbling vats and toxic fumes, he directs the Royal Apothecary Society's research, testing dangerous concoctions and coordinating the synthesis of powerful new blights and abominations for the Forsaken.",al={"why is faranell here","faranell apothecarium","why is faranell in undercity"},it="why_here",add="b168fd3d"},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell tied to?",a="Faranell directly serves Queen Sylvanas Windrunner and leads the Royal Apothecary Society, directing subordinate researchers like Apothecary Renferrel in Silverpine and Apothecary Lydon in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He also maintains ties to fellow researchers, piecing together work from former colleagues like Apothecary Berard.",al={"faranell connections","who works with faranell","faranell allies"},it="ties",add="79d7ca05"},{q="Why is Master Apothecary Faranell feared?",a="Once a reputable scholar in Dalaran, Faranell's intellectual brilliance turned into depthless sadism after rising in undeath. He is notorious as the dark architect behind the Forsaken's most lethal poisons and plagues, testing horrific new concoctions on living and dead alike without a shred of remorse.",al={"why is faranell famous","faranell reputation","is faranell dangerous"},it="fame",add="d3e005f3"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can see Faranell at work on weapons meant to shatter the Lich King's power and secure your people's future.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you may find the green ooze and caged subjects unsettling. Faranell's research is tolerated as vital warfare against the Scourge.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know how rare flora, mosses, and fungal extracts can fill Faranell's vats. His work turns botanical study toward destruction."},kw={"abomination","apothecarium","blight","faranell","master apothecary faranell","new plague","renferrel","royal apothecary society","sylvanas","undercity"},rel={"topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","npc:apothecary-renferrel","quest:447","quest:509","topic:forsaken"},src={"Master Apothecary Faranell"}}
E["npc:raleigh-andrean"] = {t="npc",n="Raleigh Andrean",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Raleigh Andrean lives among the Forsaken. His requests show how little regard he has for his human life and those he once knew.",h="In the Undercity, Raleigh Andrean lives among the Forsaken.",sec={{t="A Bitter Afterlife",b="Before the Third War, Raleigh Andrean lived in Lordaeron as a human. He was married to Deliah and counted Valdred Moray as a friend. The Scourge swept through the kingdom, killing Raleigh and raising him as a mindless thrall in service to the Lich King. After the Lich King's grip shattered and Sylvanas Windrunner led her uprising, Raleigh regained his free will and joined the Forsaken in the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance over Grief",b="Raleigh Andrean's requests reveal how undeath has worn away his feelings. When Deliah's wedding ring is brought to him, he shows no sorrow or lingering love for his late wife. He dismisses her death and asks for the severed hands of Valdred Moray, his former friend who murdered her. Raleigh keeps the hands as a reminder of betrayal, not out of affection for Deliah. Whoever helps him receives a ring forged of pure scorn.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Raleigh Andrean located?",a="Raleigh Andrean lives in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity, among the Forsaken.",al={"raleigh andrean location","where is raleigh","find raleigh andrean"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who was Raleigh when he was alive?",a="Before the Scourge swept through Lordaeron, Raleigh lived there as a human. He was married to Deliah and was friends with Valdred Moray.",al={"raleigh backstory","who was raleigh","raleigh andrean lore"},it="history"},{q="Why does Raleigh want revenge on Valdred Moray?",a="Raleigh wants revenge because Valdred Moray, his former friend, murdered Deliah. Raleigh asks for Valdred's severed hands.",al={"why kill valdred","raleigh wife","valdred moray murder"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="How did Raleigh become free from the Scourge?",a="During the Third War, the Scourge killed Raleigh and raised him as a thrall. After the Lich King's grip shattered, Sylvanas Windrunner led an uprising that freed Raleigh and many others, who formed the Forsaken.",al={"how did raleigh become forsaken","raleigh scourge freedom"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Raleigh Andrean?",a="Raleigh Andrean is a Forsaken citizen residing in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity. In life, he was a citizen of Lordaeron who was murdered during the Scourge invasion and raised into undeath. After breaking free from the Lich King's grasp alongside Sylvanas Windrunner, he pledged himself to the Forsaken, lingering in the capital consumed by bitterness and a cold hunger for vengeance against those who betrayed him in his former life.",al={"who is raleigh andrean","who is raleigh","raleigh andrean identity"},it="identity",add="1c49ed7c"},{q="Whose side is Raleigh Andrean on?",a="Raleigh is entirely loyal to Queen Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken, and by extension the Horde. Once liberated from the Scourge's control following the Dark Lady's uprising, he found sanctuary beneath the ruins of Lordaeron. Though primarily consumed by personal grudges, he stands firmly among his fellow undead in the Undercity.",al={"raleigh andrean faction","is raleigh horde","whose side is raleigh on"},it="side",add="c1a05a30"},{q="What does Raleigh Andrean want?",a="Raleigh seeks revenge against his former friend, Valdred Moray. He feels nothing for the death of his late wife Deliah, yet a cold desire for vengeance still burns in his dead heart, and he wants Valdred hunted down and his hands brought back as a grim trophy.",al={"what does raleigh want","raleigh andrean goal","raleigh andrean revenge"},sp=1,it="wants",add="49f29ff4"},{q="Why is Raleigh Andrean in the Undercity?",a="Like many former citizens of Lordaeron who regained their free will, Raleigh took refuge in the Undercity after breaking the Lich King's domination. He now lingers in the Trade Quarter, brooding over past grievances and seeking passing adventurers willing to help him carry out vengeance against his living enemies.",al={"why is raleigh here","why is raleigh in undercity","raleigh andrean trade quarter"},it="why_here",add="5288ca4a"},{q="Who is Raleigh Andrean tied to?",a="In life, Raleigh was married to a woman named Deliah and was close companions with Valdred Moray. That friendship has since turned into a bitter, enduring hatred that spans across death itself.",al={"raleigh andrean wife","raleigh andrean connections","raleigh valdred deliah"},sp=1,it="ties",add="396cb243"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you can see how one Forsaken responds to undeath through Raleigh's treatment of his former human ties."},kw={"a husband's revenge","deliah","forsaken","raleigh andrean","ring of scorn","trade quarter","undercity","valdred moray"},rel={"quest:530","quest:441","zone:undercity","subzone:trade-quarter","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","topic:lich-king"},src={"Raleigh Andrean"}}
E["npc:sylvanas-windrunner"] = {t="npc",n="Sylvanas Windrunner",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Sylvanas Windrunner rules the Forsaken from beneath Lordaeron's ruins. Once Silvermoon's Ranger-General, she was slain and raised by Arthas Menethil, then broke free of the Lich King's control. She joined Thrall's Horde to help secure her people's future and seeks vengeance on the Scourge.",h="In the Undercity, Sylvanas Windrunner rules the Forsaken from beneath Lordaeron's ruins.",sec={{t="Fall of the Ranger-General",b="Sylvanas Windrunner once commanded Quel'Thalas's defense as Silvermoon's Ranger-General. When Prince Arthas Menethil led the Scourge into the high elven kingdom to reach the Sunwell, she fought to hold him back. Angered by her resistance, Arthas murdered her and denied her a clean death. He tore her soul from her body and made her a vengeful banshee, forcing her to serve the Scourge and help slaughter her own people.",sp=0},{t="Rise of the Forsaken",b="After the Third War, the Lich King's weakening grip let Sylvanas break free and reclaim her preserved body. She gathered other undead who had regained their free will, then drove the dreadlords from Lordaeron's ruins. She named her people the Forsaken and made the Undercity their realm beneath the ruins. Isolated and threatened by Scourge remnants, zealous Scarlet crusaders, and wary human realms, the Forsaken needed allies. Sylvanas made an uneasy alliance with Warchief Thrall and the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sylvanas Windrunner?",a="Sylvanas Windrunner rules the Forsaken from the Royal Quarter of the Undercity. Once Quel'Thalas's elven Ranger-General, she was slain and raised by Arthas Menethil, then broke free of the Scourge and took command of the free-willed undead.",al={"banshee queen","who is the dark lady","lady sylvanas","undercity leader"},it="identity"},{q="Why did Sylvanas align the Forsaken with the Horde?",a="Sylvanas allied the Forsaken with the Horde because the living nations of the Alliance revile them as monsters. With the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade threatening them in Lordaeron, she sought strong allies for her people's survival and petitioned Warchief Thrall to join the Horde.",al={"why are undead in horde","forsaken horde alliance","sylvanas thrall pact"},it="side"},{q="How did Sylvanas break free from the Lich King?",a="Sylvanas broke free when the Lich King's psychic power began to fade after the Third War, fracturing his control over the Scourge. Among the first powerful spirits to regain autonomy, she reclaimed her mortal remains and turned her wrath on Arthas.",al={"how did sylvanas escape arthas","sylvanas free will","lich king control"},it="history"},{q="What is Sylvanas's primary goal?",a="Sylvanas seeks retribution against Arthas Menethil and the Scourge for destroying her homeland and enslaving her soul. She also works to fortify the Undercity and secure a lasting haven for the Forsaken in Lordaeron.",al={"what does sylvanas want","sylvanas motivation","dark lady goal"},it="wants"},{q="Why is Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity?",a="Sylvanas rules the Forsaken from the Royal Quarter deep within the Undercity, the subterranean labyrinth carved beneath the ruins of the Capital City of Lordaeron. After seizing the capital from the Scourge and Dreadlords, she established it as the stronghold of her free-willed undead. From here, she directs the defense of Tirisfal Glades against the Scarlet Crusade and remnants of the Scourge, while working to forge a secure future for her people in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"why is sylvanas here","why undercity sylvanas","sylvanas location reason"},it="why_here",add="830cd396"},{q="Who is Sylvanas Windrunner allied with?",a="Sylvanas is supreme ruler of the Forsaken and leads them under an alliance of convenience with Warchief Thrall's Horde. Within her court, she is guarded and advised by figures like the dreadlord Varimathras, who pledged fealty to her after the fall of Lordaeron. Beyond her undead nation, she maintains fraught geopolitical ties with the orcs and tauren, who granted her people entry into the Horde despite lingering mutual suspicions.",al={"sylvanas allies","who is sylvanas tied to","sylvanas windrunner connections"},it="ties",add="de176d94"},{q="Why is Sylvanas Windrunner famous?",a="Before her death, Sylvanas was revered as the Ranger-General of Silvermoon, celebrated for her valiant defense of Quel'Thalas against the Scourge. Today, she is feared across Azeroth as the Banshee Queen. Having endured execution and banshee torment at the hands of Prince Arthas, she reclaimed her mortal vessel and wrested an entire faction of undead from the Lich King's psychic grasp. Her lethal archery, banshee scream, and ruthless cunning make both living and dead tread carefully around her.",al={"why is sylvanas feared","banshee queen fame","why is sylvanas famous"},it="fame",add="aee4c591"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="To the Forsaken, Sylvanas is a liberator and protector. They credit her with giving them free will and a fortified home instead of leaving them to serve the Scourge mindlessly.",["faction:Horde"]="Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem and Thrall's compassion helped bring Sylvanas into the Horde, but many orcs and trolls remain wary of her and her court."},kw={"arthas","banshee queen","dark lady","forsaken","lordaeron","ranger-general","sylvanas","undercity","windrunner"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:horde","npc:thrall","zone:tirisfal","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Sylvanas Windrunner"}}
E["npc:varimathras"] = {t="npc",n="Varimathras",z="undercity",s="In the Royal Quarter, Varimathras advises Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and commands her forces. Defeated during the civil war for Lordaeron, the dreadlord pledged himself to the Banshee Queen and now stands at her right hand in the Undercity.",h="In the Royal Quarter, Varimathras advises Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and commands her forces.",sec={{t="Jailor of the Lich King",b="Before the Third War, Kil'jaeden sent Varimathras and his fellow dreadlords to Azeroth to guard the Lich King and ensure Ner'zhul's spirit served the Legion's plans. With his brothers Detheroc and Balnazzar, Varimathras oversaw the Scourge in Lordaeron while Archimonde invaded Kalimdor. The Legion fell at Mount Hyjal, but the three dreadlords remained entrenched in the ruins of the Capital City. They did not learn of their master's defeat until Prince Arthas returned and drove them into hiding.",sp=0},{t="A Demon's Surrender",b="As the Lich King's hold over his undead forces weakened, Varimathras tried to make the newly freed banshee Sylvanas Windrunner serve the dreadlords' new regime. Sylvanas refused and rallied liberated undead to destroy his outpost. Facing execution, Varimathras begged for his life and offered tactical secrets, including knowledge of his brothers' fortifications. Sylvanas spared him and bound him to her service as a weapon against his kin.",sp=0},{t="Brother Against Brother",b="Varimathras was ordered to kill his fellow dreadlord Balnazzar after the conquest of the Capital City to earn Sylvanas's trust. He seemed to obey, but Balnazzar survived the deception. At Sylvanas's command, Varimathras then executed the human warlord Grand Marshal Garithos. Now beside Sylvanas's throne, he coordinates military excursions across Lordaeron, while many in the Horde regard this demonic ally with deep unease.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is a demon serving the Forsaken?",a="During the Lordaeron civil war, Sylvanas Windrunner led newly liberated undead against Varimathras's forces and defeated them. Facing death, he begged for mercy and offered his cunning, military knowledge, and service. Sylvanas spared him to serve as her tactician and enforcer.",al={"why is varimathras in undercity","why dreadlord with sylvanas","varimathras allegiance"},it="motive"},{q="What kind of creature is Varimathras?",a="Varimathras is a nathrezim, or dreadlord. Nathrezim are intelligent, manipulative demons who serve the Burning Legion, using mental domination, shadow magic, plague, and discord.",al={"what race is varimathras","is varimathras a vampire","varimathras species"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Varimathras stand in the Undercity?",a="Varimathras stands on the dais in the Undercity's Royal Quarter, directly beside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and surrounded by Forsaken royal guards.",al={"where is varimathras","varimathras location","find varimathras"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened between Varimathras and Balnazzar?",a="After the conquest of the Capital City, Sylvanas ordered Varimathras to attack his brother Balnazzar as a test of loyalty. Varimathras turned on his fellow dreadlord at her command.",al={"did varimathras kill balnazzar","varimathras brother","dreadlord taboo"},it="conflict"},{q="What role did Varimathras play in creating the Scourge?",a="Kil'jaeden bound the orc shaman Ner'zhul's spirit inside the Frozen Throne and hurled it to Azeroth as the Lich King. He sent Varimathras and the other dreadlords to guard the Lich King and oversee the Scourge's work in Lordaeron.",al={"varimathras nerzhul","varimathras lich king origin"},it="history"},{q="Do the other Horde leaders trust Varimathras?",a="No. The orcs, trolls, and tauren bear deep scars from demonic corruption and see dreadlords as monstrous manipulators. Many Forsaken also regard Varimathras as an uneasy weapon kept on a tight leash, not a true brother-in-arms.",al={"does the horde trust varimathras","thrall varimathras","is varimathras trusted"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Varimathras on?",a="Outwardly, Varimathras serves Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. When Sylvanas defeated his forces after the Third War, he begged for his life and pledged his loyalty to her, even aiding in the overthrow of his dreadlord brothers. However, he remains a nathrezim of the Burning Legion at heart. While he acts as the Banshee Queen's majordomo, few in the Horde believe a demon's loyalty can ever truly be trusted.",al={"is varimathras loyal","varimathras allegiance","who does varimathras serve"},sp=1,it="side",add="b37d7c5f"},{q="What does Varimathras want?",a="Above all else, Varimathras wants survival and influence. When Sylvanas had him at her mercy, he willingly betrayed his fellow dreadlords to preserve his own skin. By embedding himself as Sylvanas's second-in-command within the Undercity, he maintains a position of tremendous authority in Lordaeron while continuing to advance the ruin of his enemies—namely the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"varimathras goals","what does varimathras want","varimathras motives"},it="wants",add="3e1da8be"},{q="Why is Varimathras in the Undercity?",a="Varimathras stands beside Lady Sylvanas in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity as her chief lieutenant and master tactician. Bound into her service after she defeated him, he helped her conquer Lordaeron's capital and overthrow his fellow dreadlords Detheroc and Balnazzar. He now coordinates military actions, directs spies, and helps oversee the Forsaken kingdom under the Dark Lady's watchful eye.",al={"why is varimathras here","varimathras undercity why","what is varimathras doing here"},it="why_here",add="e0cdf0b9"},{q="Why is Varimathras so feared?",a="Varimathras is a dreadlord, one of the cunning nathrezim whom Kil'jaeden sent to watch over the Lich King and the Scourge's devastation of Azeroth. Renowned for masterful manipulation, mind control, and ruthless cunning, he and his brothers once commanded the undead legions across Lordaeron. To see such a powerful demon bound into servitude is both a terrifying testament to Sylvanas's power and an unsettling omen to anyone who enters the Undercity.",al={"why is varimathras dangerous","varimathras reputation","is varimathras feared"},it="fame",add="9df47492"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see Varimathras as proof that the Forsaken will turn their oppressors' weapons against them. He stands subdued beside the Dark Lady who freed Lordaeron from his grip.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may find a high-ranking nathrezim serving a mortal undead queen an impressive, unsettling display of will.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you find Varimathras's presence in the Undercity a source of friction with Orgrimmar. The Horde spent decades breaking free from the demonic masters he served."},kw={"balnazzar","detheroc","dreadlord","nathrezim","royal quarter","sylvanas","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"npc:sylvanas-windrunner","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:lordaeron","topic:burning-legion","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","topic:third-war"},src={"Varimathras"}}
E["npc:varok-saurfang"] = {t="npc",n="Varok Saurfang",z="undercity",s="In Orgrimmar, Varok Saurfang commands the Horde's war forces under Warchief Thrall. The veteran of the Old Horde's wars lends the young Horde his strength and experience.",h="In Orgrimmar, Varok Saurfang commands the Horde's war forces under Warchief Thrall.",sec={{t="A Living Legend of the Wars",b="Varok Saurfang carries the Old Horde's wars into the present. Few living warriors match his record, and many regard him as unstoppable in battle. Now High Overlord in Orgrimmar, he helps hold together Thrall's newborn Horde.",sp=0},{t="The Weight of the Blood",b="Varok Saurfang defends the Horde and enforces Thrall's rule against threats. He does not seek battle for its own sake. He despises warmongering and fights for honor and the Horde's preservation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Varok Saurfang?",a="Varok Saurfang is a renowned orc warrior and the primary military commander serving Warchief Thrall in the Horde.",al={"varok saurfang backstory","who is saurfang","high overlord saurfang"},it="identity"},{q="What wars did Saurfang fight in?",a="Varok Saurfang fought in the Old Horde's wars against the Alliance. Now he fights for Thrall's Horde.",al={"saurfang war history","did saurfang fight in the first war","saurfang battles"},it="history"},{q="How does Saurfang view the Horde's past?",a="Varok Saurfang fought for the Old Horde in the days of the demon blood curse. Now he serves Thrall's Horde, which has turned from that path.",al={"saurfang blood curse","why does saurfang regret the past"},it="motive"},{q="What is Saurfang's role in the current Horde?",a="Varok Saurfang leads Thrall's forces as High Overlord. He oversees military readiness, enforces the Warchief's commands, and mentors younger Horde warriors.",al={"what does saurfang do now","saurfang orgrimmar role"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Varok Saurfang on?",a="Saurfang is fiercely devoted to Thrall's Horde. A veteran of the Old Horde's wars, today he stands unreservedly behind the new Horde. He enforces the Warchief's will and protects the people with absolute dedication.",al={"what faction is saurfang","who does saurfang serve","saurfang loyalty"},it="side",add="30353091"},{q="What does Varok Saurfang want?",a="Saurfang desires honor and stability for his people. He will defend Thrall's Horde to his dying breath and strives to keep the orcs from succumbing to the dark past of the Old Horde.",al={"what does saurfang want","saurfang goal","saurfang motives"},it="wants",add="275ad83b"},{q="Who is Varok Saurfang tied to?",a="He is one of Warchief Thrall's most trusted commanders, standing as High Overlord of the Horde in Orgrimmar.",al={"saurfang family","saurfang brother","who is saurfang related to"},it="ties",add="d09cd640"},{q="Why is Varok Saurfang famous?",a="Saurfang is legendary across Azeroth as an unstoppable force on the battlefield. A veteran of the Old Horde's wars, his unmatched martial prowess and tactical ferocity have earned him immense renown and fear among enemies and allies alike.",al={"why is saurfang feared","is saurfang famous","saurfang reputation"},it="fame",add="593a9ba3"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you can look to High Overlord Saurfang as a paragon of martial strength and a reminder of the spiritual toll of the demonic blood curse.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can revere Saurfang as a peerless veteran. His axe technique, tactical brilliance, and enduring resolve embody the ideal soldier."},kw={"korkron","overlord","saurfang","thrall","varok","warrior"},rel={"npc:thrall","topic:first-war","topic:second-war","topic:third-war"},src={"Varok Saurfang"}}
E["quest:1359"] = {t="quest",n="Zinge's Delivery",z="undercity",s="Apothecary Renferrel sends Zinge's Delivery from the Sepulcher to the Undercity. The wolf hearts he sends from Silverpine Forest carry toxins that should have killed the beasts, and Apothecary Zinge receives them for study by the Royal Apothecary Society.",h="Apothecary Renferrel sends Zinge's Delivery from the Sepulcher to the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Toxic Anomaly",b="Apothecary Renferrel found a strange trait in the wolves roaming Silverpine Forest's ruined woods. Their hearts held such powerful toxins that they should have killed the beasts. Renferrel preserved several tissue samples and packed them for colleagues at the Apothecarium in the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="The Eyes of the Apothecarium",b="Apothecary Zinge receives the preserved organs at the Undercity's underground headquarters of the Royal Apothecary Society. The society seeks potent plagues and new alchemical compounds, so poisons that sustain their hosts draw its attention. Zinge welcomes the samples as the start of further laboratory trials across the Forsaken alchemical network.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the wolf heart samples?",a="The samples are preserved tissue from wolves in Silverpine Forest. Apothecary Renferrel found natural toxins in their hearts so deadly the animals should not have survived carrying them.",al={"wolf hearts","what are wolf heart samples","renferrel samples"},it="item"},{q="Who is Apothecary Renferrel?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is a member of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He leads field research on regional plants and animals to gather ingredients and knowledge for Forsaken alchemy.",al={"who is renferrel","renferrel silverpine"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Apothecary Zinge?",a="Apothecary Zinge is an alchemical researcher in the Apothecarium quarter of the Undercity. She studies incoming biological specimens for new toxins and alchemical agents for the Forsaken.",al={"who is zinge","zinge undercity","apothecary zinge lore"},it="target"},{q="Where does this delivery lead next?",a="Apothecary Zinge receives and inspects the strange heart tissue, then samples go to other alchemical outposts. One such outpost is Apothecary Helbrim's, across the sea in the Barrens.",al={"next quest","what happens after zinge's delivery","follow up quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Royal Apothecary Society interested in wolf hearts?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society seeks unusual poisons, diseases, and biological anomalies. A beast that survives lethal toxins in its own heart may reveal chemical paths to new plagues and compounds.",al={"why do apothecaries want wolf hearts","ras wolf hearts"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Apothecarium in Undercity?",a="The Apothecarium occupies the southwestern wing of the Undercity. It is the Royal Apothecary Society's main laboratory complex and headquarters.",al={"undercity apothecary location","where is zinge","apothecarium map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel send you instead of going himself?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is stationed out at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, conducting active fieldwork and ongoing research into the local wildlife. Leaving his outpost to carry samples back to the Capital would pull him away from his experiments, making an able-bodied traveler the ideal courier to transport the fragile specimens directly to Apothecary Zinge in the Apothecarium.",al={"why me renferrel","why does renferrel need a courier","why send an adventurer with the delivery"},it="why_me",add="37fb7d35"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know field samples from Lordaeron reach the alchemical laboratories beneath the Capital City ruins and advance Forsaken science.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know messengers carrying biological reagents link distant outposts like the Sepulcher with the Undercity's leaders and research halls."},kw={"apothecarium","apothecary renferrel","apothecary zinge","sepulcher","silverpine","undercity","wolf heart samples","zinge's delivery"},rel={"npc:apothecary-zinge","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:undercity","quest:1358","quest:3221"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="Apothecary Zinge",level="15",faction="Horde",id=1359},src={"Zinge's Delivery"}}
E["quest:1471"] = {t="quest",n="The Binding",z="undercity",s="In the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, Forsaken warlocks seek to summon, conquer, and permanently command a voidwalker. Carendin Halgar oversees the rite that grants them this power.",h="In the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, Forsaken warlocks seek to summon, conquer, and permanently command a...",sec={{t="A Rite of Subjugation",b="Forsaken warlocks must prove they can master a voidwalker before they may summon one. Unlike minor imps, which dark magic easily draws into pacts, creatures of the Void despise reality and possess formidable physical might. In the Magic Quarter, mentor Carendin Halgar provides the mystic runes required to tear a voidwalker from the Nether into the physical realm.",sp=0},{t="Within the Circle",b="Beneath Carendin Halgar's dais, a glowing summoning circle is etched into the floor. When the runes are activated, an unbound voidwalker appears in fury. You cannot subdue it through diplomacy; you must break it with arcane force and raw will. Only after the creature is thoroughly crushed does Carendin reveal the true summoning formula, which binds its essence to you indefinitely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this ritual?",a="The rite tests whether you can overpower a creature of the Void. Defeating an unbound voidwalker proves your will is strong enough to control it, and Carendin Halgar then teaches you the permanent summoning spell.",al={"why do the binding","what does the binding quest do","binding reward"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the summoning take place?",a="The summoning takes place in the purple circle etched into the floor beneath Carendin Halgar's platform in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",al={"where do i summon voidwalker","where is the summoning circle","circle of summoning undercity"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Carendin Halgar?",a="Carendin Halgar is the primary warlock trainer in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. He oversees instruction and dark initiations for newly raised Forsaken practitioners.",al={"who is halgar","carendin halgar lore"},it="identity"},{q="Do warlocks need to defeat every demon they want to summon?",a="Warlocks must establish authority over powerful extradimensional beings before commanding them. Smaller entities like imps are bound by simple contracts and rituals, while voidwalkers require physical and magical dominance before they submit to servitude.",al={"do warlocks always fight demons","why fight the voidwalker"}},{q="What happens if a warlock fails to subdue the voidwalker?",a="An unbound voidwalker relentlessly batters anyone nearby. Halgar warns that failing to meet his expectations is nothing compared to the danger of being torn apart by the untamed entity within the circle.",al={"what if i fail the binding","failure lore warlock"},it="danger"},{q="What is a voidwalker?",a="Voidwalkers are shadowy, extradimensional beings from the Void. They have immense physical resilience and an innate desire to extinguish living light and energy, making them ideal protective shields for practitioners of dark magic.",al={"what is a voidwalker","voidwalker lore"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar want this ritual done?",a="Carendin Halgar seeks to cultivate formidable power within the Undercity's warlock ranks. By compelling you to summon and bend an unbound creature of the void entirely to your will, he ensures that Forsaken practitioners master true subjugation rather than fall prey to the otherworldly entities they seek to command.",al={"why carendin halgar binding","carendin halgar motive","why summon voidwalker"},it="motive",rc="Undead",add="abacfa90"},{q="What is the entity you are sent to summon and defeat?",a="You are drawing forth an unbound voidwalker straight from the Twisting Nether into the summoning circle. Voidwalkers are shadowy demons formed from pure void energy, hostile and resentful of servitude, requiring outright magical and martial defeat before accepting a master's will.",al={"what do you fight in the binding","target of the binding","who am i summoning"},it="target",rc="Undead",add="68d93197"},{q="Why must you subdue the voidwalker yourself rather than having Carendin Halgar do it?",a="Demonology demands personal dominance. A summoned demon yields only to the individual who demonstrates the magical authority and physical fortitude to conquer it. If Carendin or the city guards intervened to subdue the creature, the voidwalker would be bound to their will rather than your own.",al={"why do i have to fight it","why doesn't carendin help","why me binding quest"},it="why_me",rc="Undead",add="15849809"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, this rite takes you from petty trickery with imps to domination over beings that can absorb immense physical punishment on the battlefield.",["race:Undead"]="As one of the Forsaken, binding a creature of shadow extends your resilience and your lack of moral restraint regarding forbidden magic."},kw={"carendin halgar","magic quarter","runes of summoning","subjugation","the binding","undercity","voidwalker","warlock quest"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1473","quest:1478","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity"},m={start="Carendin Halgar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1471},src={"The Binding (Voidwalker, Undercity)"}}
E["quest:1472"] = {t="quest",n="Devourer of Souls",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity's Temple of the Damned, Carendin Halgar guides Forsaken warlocks toward binding a succubus. Godrick Farsan knows how to lure one from the Twisting Nether with the hearts of pure, loving mortals.",h="In the Undercity's Temple of the Damned, Carendin Halgar guides Forsaken warlocks toward binding a succubus.",sec={{t="Baiting the Nether",b="Carendin Halgar teaches that a succubus must be enticed across the threshold, not summoned by command. The demon hungers to ruin virtue and consume mortal essence. To draw it forth, you offer the hearts of genuinely virtuous, loving men as bait. Halgar sends you to Godrick Farsan, who knows where such rare quarry can be found.",sp=0},{t="The Blind Assistant",b="Deeper in the Temple of the Damned, Godrick Farsan helps Carendin prepare for demonic binding. Farsan has lost his physical eyesight, but says this grants him a deeper sight. He claims to perceive spiritual currents and distant souls with uncanny clarity, and can guide you to the pure hearts needed to draw out the demon.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="It bridges Carendin Halgar's initial summons and the practical hunt needed to bind a succubus. You go to Godrick Farsan, who explains the ritual's grim requirements.",al={"why do devourer of souls","succubus quest undercity","warlock quest level 20"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does a succubus need pure hearts to be summoned?",a="Carendin Halgar says a succubus cannot easily cross into this world without an irresistible lure. The demon hungers to corrupt goodness, tempt mortal hearts, and devour virtuous souls, so the untainted devotion of good men draws it across.",al={"why hearts of the pure","succubus bait lore"}},{q="Who is Godrick Farsan?",a="Godrick Farsan is an undead warlock acolyte who assists Carendin Halgar in the Temple of the Damned. Though physically blind, he has mystical senses that help him perceive spiritual truths and locate suitable prey across the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"who is farsan","blind warlock assistant"},it="identity"},{q="Where is this quest completed?",a="You complete it in the Temple of the Damned in the Undercity, where Godrick Farsan waits just a few paces from Carendin Halgar.",al={"where is godrick farsan","devourer of souls turn in"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What comes after Devourer of Souls?",a="Godrick Farsan next sends you to Hearts of the Pure. You travel to the Wetlands and the Greymane Wall in Silverpine Forest to claim the hearts of two virtuous mortals.",al={"next quest after devourer of souls","hearts of the pure next"},it="next_step"},{q="Can any race undertake this ritual?",a="Any Horde warlock seeking to bind a succubus through Undercity mentors can follow Halgar and Farsan's ritual steps. Though Forsaken practitioners teach it in the Undercity, the ritual is open to those warlocks.",al={"who can do devourer of souls","undead only warlock quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar want to summon a succubus?",a="Carendin Halgar oversees the development of warlocks within the Undercity. A succubus is a creature of deceit, temptation, and malice—a potent tool for bending enemy wills and turning desires into fatal weaknesses. Carendin directs you through the ritual so you can bind the demon directly to your command, expanding the Forsaken's dark arsenal while proving your mastery over the Nether.",al={"carendin halgar motive","why summon succubus carendin","carendin goal devourer of souls"},it="motive",add="99fee797"},{q="Why does Carendin send you instead of handling this himself?",a="Demonic enslavement cannot be performed on another caster's behalf. A succubus answers only to the will that directly lures, binds, and dominates her. As a mentor, Carendin Halgar guides your studies and provides the ritual's foundational lore, but you alone must acquire the bait, face the demon, and assert absolute control over its soul.",al={"why does carendin need me","why me devourer of souls","why warlock player succubus"},it="why_me",add="2acf7f0a"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, binding a succubus marks a major step in your training. You use a demon's vices and appetites to enslave it.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you train among Forsaken warlocks in the Temple of the Damned. They treat living purity and devotion as reagents for Nether rituals without moral restraint."},kw={"bait","carendin halgar","godrick farsan","hearts of the pure","succubus","temple of the damned","undercity"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","npc:godrick-farsan","quest:1476"},m={start="Carendin Halgar",["end"]="Godrick Farsan",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1472},src={"Devourer of Souls (Undercity)"}}
E["quest:1473"] = {t="quest",n="Creature of the Void",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, a lost grimoire holds the key to summoning a voidwalker. Forsaken warlocks must recover Egalin's Grimoire from the Scarlet Crusade in western Tirisfal Glades to learn how to summon and bind one.",h="In the Undercity, a lost grimoire holds the key to summoning a voidwalker.",sec={{t="A Teacher's Legacy",b="Carendin Halgar guides Forsaken summoners in the Temple of the Damned. When an acolyte can wield more than the power of petty imps, Halgar points them toward the voidwalker, a creature forged from pure shadow and chaos. Forsaken warlocks rely on the careful research of Egalin, Halgar's former master, who wrote the rituals for subduing these beings of the void.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Grimoire",b="Egalin's Grimoire holds the methods for channeling the volatile magic needed to master a voidwalker. Perrine, a Scarlet Crusade zealot stationed in an outpost tower to the west, stole the book. The Crusade may see it only as blasphemous contraband to seize and hoard, but recovering it gives the Forsaken the ritual secrets they need before they try to tear open the veil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Egalin's Grimoire?",a="Egalin's Grimoire is a magical manual written by Egalin, Carendin Halgar's teacher. It describes the channeling techniques and spells needed to breach the void and summon a voidwalker under the caster's control.",al={"egalins grimoire","what is the book","who was egalin"},it="item"},{q="Why did the Scarlet Crusade steal the book?",a="The Scarlet Crusade considers demonic and shadow magic corrupt. Perrine seized the grimoire and hid it in a western watchtower in Tirisfal Glades, seemingly unaware of the summoning power it holds.",al={"why did scarlet crusade take it","perrine grimoire","scarlet tower west"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Carendin Halgar?",a="Carendin Halgar is a master warlock trainer in the Temple of the Damned in the Undercity. He guides novice Forsaken warlocks, teaching respect for volatile cosmic forces and caution from his own past summoning mistakes.",al={"carendin halgar","warlock trainer undercity","temple of the damned trainer"},it="identity"},{q="What happens if a warlock loses control of a voidwalker?",a="Voidwalkers are beings of pure chaos and shadow. Carendin Halgar warns that without flawless discipline and binding will, a conjured voidwalker will violently tear its summoner apart.",al={"can voidwalker kill you","voidwalker danger","summoning failure"},it="danger"},{q="What comes after recovering the grimoire?",a="Once Halgar has the book, he studies it and teaches you the ritual runes. Then you enter The Binding, where you use the summoning circle to conjure a voidwalker and defeat it in personal combat to establish dominance.",al={"what next after grimoire","next quest","binding ritual"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is the Scarlet Crusade outpost located?",a="The Scarlet Crusade outpost is a watchtower west across Tirisfal Glades. Crusaders under Perrine guard it, and the grimoire is hidden inside.",al={"where is perrine","scarlet tower location","where is the book"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar want this done?",a="Carendin Halgar recognizes your growing strength and considers you ready to bind a voidwalker. That dangerous art requires the precise rituals recorded by his own mentor, Egalin. Beyond training you, Halgar cannot allow such dark, potent knowledge to remain in the hands of the Scarlet Crusade, whose fanatics would gladly use or destroy the stolen text.",al={"halgar motive","why recover the grimoire","why does halgar need the book"},it="motive",add="4bce35a3"},{q="Who has Egalin's Grimoire?",a="An agent of the Scarlet Crusade named Perrine stole the grimoire and keeps it stashed inside a Scarlet outpost to the west. While Perrine likely remains ignorant of the true demonological power contained within its musty pages, the zealots maintain a constant presence there to monitor and strike against the Undercity.",al={"who stole the grimoire","who has egalins grimoire","scarlet crusader target"},it="target",add="b85cee29"},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar send you instead of going himself?",a="Halgar serves as a master summoner within the Temple of the Damned, guiding fledgling warlocks and overseeing the Forsaken's dark craft. More importantly, retrieving the grimoire is a vital test of your resourcefulness and resolve. A warlock who cannot reclaim their own tools from zealous mortal crusaders will surely fail when attempting to dominate a chaotic creature torn from the Nether.",al={"why send me","why cant halgar get the book","why does halgar need me"},it="why_me",add="9e338ab7"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you move beyond dabbling with imps toward controlling heavy frontline shadow entities that can absorb immense physical punishment.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you strike the Scarlet Crusade to reclaim dark knowledge, deepening the bitter struggle between the Forsaken and the living zealots occupying Lordaeron's ruins.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you learn how the Undercity's dark arts use strict scholarship to turn dangerous planar forces into reliable assets in the Horde's frontier wars."},kw={"carendin halgar","egalin","egalins grimoire","perrine","scarlet crusade","temple of the damned","tirisfal glades","undercity","voidwalker"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1471","quest:1478","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:undercity"},m={start="Carendin Halgar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1473,ri={"Egalin's Grimoire"}},src={"Creature of the Void (Undercity)"}}
E["quest:1474"] = {t="quest",n="The Binding",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, an initiate faces the rite that grants command of a succubus. Carendin Halgar directs the warlock to use Pure Hearts to draw a demon from the Twisting Nether into a ritual circle, then master it through combat.",h="In the Undercity, an initiate faces the rite that grants command of a succubus.",sec={{t="A Test of Will",b="In the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Forsaken warlocks hone their command of demons. Summoning a succubus marks a critical passage in their training. A voidwalker relies on brute force, and an imp on lesser malice, but a succubus can ensnare its summoner with seductive and mental enchantments. Carendin Halgar demands that each initiate prove mind and magic unshakable before he entrusts them with lasting dominion over such a demon.",sp=0},{t="Subjugation in the Circle",b="Pure Hearts gathered from innocent souls in the Wetlands and Silverpine Forest open a passage to the Twisting Nether. A succubus summoned into the binding circle attacks at once, seeking to overpower or entrance the warlock. The warlock must break its physical form and cast its essence back into the void to claim mastery and learn to summon the demon at will.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The rite lets Forsaken warlocks prove they can master a succubus. By summoning and defeating one in the Magic Quarter, a warlock proves its charms cannot sway them and earns the power to summon and command one in battle.",al={"why do the binding","what does the binding reward","what is this quest for"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Carendin Halgar?",a="Carendin Halgar trains warlocks in the Undercity's Magic Quarter and oversees the training and trials of Forsaken spellcasters. He tests their mental endurance and dark arts before entrusting them with more dangerous summoning rites.",al={"who gives the binding","carendin halgar lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why were pure hearts needed to summon the demon?",a="Pure Hearts gathered in earlier steps serve as irresistible metaphysical bait for a succubus. The hearts draw the demon through the summoning circle to manifest in the mortal realm.",al={"why pure hearts","hearts of the pure purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the summoning take place?",a="The summoning takes place in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, in a ritual circle near Carendin Halgar and the warlock mentors.",al={"where do i summon the succubus","undercity summoning circle location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the succubus need to be slain?",a="Warlocks do not negotiate with their minions; they subjugate them. By shattering the succubus's form in the circle, the warlock bends its spirit to their will, so it returns as a thrall rather than a master.",al={"why fight the succubus","why kill summoned succubus"},it="motive"},{q="Are succubi dangerous to Undercity warlocks?",a="Yes. A succubus's charms have bound many strong minds, despite the Forsaken's resilience against fear and sleep. Carelessness in the ritual can bring death or enslavement.",al={"can a succubus charm undead","succubus danger"},it="danger"},{q="What is the summoned succubus and why is it here?",a="You are conjuring a succubus across the void directly into the Magic Quarter's summoning circle. Succubi are cunning demons adept at enthralling mortal minds, making them among the most perilous minions for a warlock to bind. This particular fiend does not dwell here naturally; it is drawn into our world solely by the pure hearts you gathered, specifically so you can break its will in combat.",al={"who is the summoned succubus","what am i fighting","succubus target"},it="target",add="c35097a2"},{q="Why must you summon and defeat the succubus yourself?",a="Demonic subjugation is a personal trial that cannot be delegated. Carendin Halgar serves as a mentor, but the demonic bond requires the summoner's own mind and magic to shatter the creature's defenses. If Halgar or the city guards stepped in to subdue the succubus for you, the demon would never bow to your command, and your authority as a warlock would remain incomplete.",al={"why cant carendin fight the succubus","why does carendin need me","why me succubus"},it="why_me",add="8c406b80"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, this rite marks a crucial step in your dark path. It tests your power to master seductive mental forces and bind cunning Nether-spawn to your will.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you use whatever dark tools are needed to secure survival and dominion in Lordaeron. Demonic subjugation is a practical means to those ends."},kw={"binding","carendin halgar","magic quarter","pure hearts","succubus","undercity","warlock"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1476","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity"},m={start="Carendin Halgar",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1474},src={"The Binding (Succubus, Undercity)"}}
E["quest:1476"] = {t="quest",n="Hearts of the Pure",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Godrick Farsan assigns a warlock trial on Carendin Halgar’s behalf. To prepare bait for a succubus, you hunt two righteous human men; their pure hearts are an irresistible temptation to the demon.",h="In the Undercity, Godrick Farsan assigns a warlock trial on Carendin Halgar’s behalf.",sec={{t="Bait for a Demon",b="Carendin Halgar, master summoner in the Temple of the Damned, assigns Godrick Farsan the groundwork for binding a succubus. Succubi prey on desire and ruin, yet untainted virtue draws them from the Twisting Nether, ripe for corruption. Godrick scours human lands for souls whose goodness remains pristine and unbroken.",sp=0},{t="The Quarry",b="Godrick Farsan names two men whose virtue marks them for sacrifice. Dalin Forgewright cares for desperate Lordaeron refugees barred from sanctuary outside the sealed Greymane Wall in southern Silverpine. Comar Villard searches the perilous marshlands of the Wetlands tirelessly for any trace of his lost wife. Their devotion, empathy, and loyalty make them prime sacrifices to a Forsaken warlock.",sp=0},{t="A Forsaken Perspective",b="The hunt takes you through dangerous Alliance-held and wild territories, where you butcher both men. When you return their bloody hearts to the Temple of the Damned, Carendin Halgar observes that a good man’s heart looks no different from any other corpse’s remains. Yet the spiritual purity clinging to their flesh is potent bait, enough to lure a succubus into captivity.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why do warlocks need pure hearts to summon a succubus?",a="A succubus is drawn to mortal innocence and virtue, which she seeks to corrupt. Carendin Halgar uses the hearts of genuinely pure and selfless men as irresistible spiritual bait to draw one across the Nether and trap her in a binding circle.",al={"why pure hearts","succubus bait lore","why kill dalin and comar"},it="item"},{q="Who is Dalin Forgewright?",a="Dalin Forgewright is an honorable human who patrols on horseback along the closed gates of the Greymane Wall in southern Silverpine Forest. He devotes his life to caring for and protecting Lordaeron refugees rejected and shut out by Gilneas.",al={"dalin forgewright lore","who is dalin","greymane wall guy"},it="target"},{q="Who is Comar Villard?",a="Comar Villard is a devoted human searching the northern road of the Wetlands, just south of the Thandol Span. Grief and steadfast love drive him to keep seeking any trace of his missing wife.",al={"comar villard lore","who is comar","wetlands human heart"},it="target"},{q="Where does this quest chain lead?",a="Delivering the two hearts to Carendin Halgar lets him prepare the summoning circle in the Temple of the Damned. From there, you summon and subdue a succubus to serve as a permanent minion.",al={"what comes next","after hearts of the pure","succubus quest reward"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Godrick Farsan, an assistant in the Temple of the Damned in the Undercity’s Magic Quarter, gives the assignment on Carendin Halgar’s behalf. He projects magical illusions of Dalin and Comar to show you whom to hunt.",al={"who starts hearts of the pure","godrick farsan quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar dismiss the appearance of the hearts?",a="Carendin Halgar says a good man’s heart looks much like any other slab of flesh. As an Undead practitioner of the dark arts, he cares for its use as a magical reagent, not its physical morality.",al={"carendin dialogue","heart appearance"}},{q="Why does Godrick Farsan want these hearts collected?",a="Godrick aids Carendin Halgar in training worthy Forsaken warlocks. To summon and dominate a succubus, Halgar requires rare conduits—specifically the hearts of truly pure, noble men whose virtues can lure a demon of temptation into a binding circle. Godrick tracked down suitable targets so you could harvest their hearts and prove your dark arts.",al={"why does godrick need hearts","godrick farsan motive","why harvest pure hearts"},it="motive",add="4332c870"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you learn to wield not only misery and fear, but the nobility of others, to bind demons to your will.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you see the Forsaken’s chilling view of Lordaeron’s survivors and their virtues as fitting material for ritual slaughter.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know the victims as tragic human figures: one guards refugees shut out by Gilneas, while the other searches the marshlands for his lost wife."},kw={"carendin halgar","comar villard","dalin forgewright","godrick farsan","greymane wall","hearts of the pure","succubus","temple of the damned","thandol span","undercity"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","npc:godrick-farsan","subzone:greymane-wall","subzone:thandol-span","zone:silverpine","zone:wetlands","topic:lordaeron","topic:alliance"},m={start="Godrick Farsan",["end"]="Carendin Halgar",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1476,ri={"Comar's Heart","Dalin's Heart"}},src={"Hearts of the Pure"}}
E["quest:1478"] = {t="quest",n="Halgar's Summons",z="undercity",s="A formal summons calls promising Forsaken warlocks to advanced training in Undercity. Carendin Halgar expects those who have reached a threshold in their craft to join him in the Magic Quarter, where dangerous Nether beings await.",h="A formal summons calls promising Forsaken warlocks to advanced training in Undercity.",sec={{t="A Master's Notice",b="Word of a warlock's control over basic fel energies travels from Brill or the Tirisfal wilderness to Undercity. Ageron Kargal, a senior practitioner who spots talent, sends notice to those who show promise. Carendin Halgar's summons marks a rare privilege and a perilous step in a warlock's training. Basic imps and petty curses no longer suffice.",sp=0},{t="The Magic Quarter",b="Carendin Halgar oversees warlock rites in Undercity's Magic Quarter, near the Temple of the Damned. Forsaken darkcasters lack the living's moral restraint, but planar summonings still demand discipline. Halgar tolerates neither hesitation nor sentimentality. Those called to him are expected to show deference and be ready to face the hostile horrors of the Twisting Nether.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Carendin Halgar?",a="Carendin Halgar is the chief warlock trainer in Undercity's Magic Quarter. He oversees the dark development of Forsaken summoners and tests their resolve before teaching them to bind powerful Nether creatures.",al={"carendin halgar","master halgar","who is halgar"},it="identity"},{q="Who directs me to Halgar?",a="Ageron Kargal, an established warlock trainer stationed in Brill, sends you after learning that Master Halgar has taken a personal interest in your progress.",al={"who gives halgars summons","ageron kargal","who gives quest"}},{q="Where can I find Carendin Halgar in Undercity?",a="Halgar is in Undercity's Magic Quarter, near the dark dais called the Temple of the Damned.",al={"halgar location","where is halgar","magic quarter halgar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is this summons important?",a="The summons marks your passage from basic spellcasting to dangerous demonic subjugation. It begins the trials required to bind a Voidwalker to your service.",al={"why do i need this quest","quest purpose","what does halgars summons lead to"},it="purpose"},{q="Is Halgar willing to teach anyone?",a="Halgar gives his attention to promising warlocks. He has little time for idle pleasantries and expects any apprentice brought before him to have proven capable with volatile fel arts.",al={"can anyone talk to halgar","halgar requirements"}},{q="What happens after reporting to Halgar?",a="When you report to Halgar, he tests your magic by assigning you to gather the components needed to summon and bind an otherworldly shadow minion.",al={"what comes next","after halgars summons"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Ageron Kargal send you to Carendin Halgar?",a="Ageron Kargal serves as a warlock mentor in Brill, but your growing mastery requires advanced instruction beyond what a village tutor can provide. When word arrives from Master Carendin Halgar himself requesting your presence, Ageron dutifully directs you to the Undercity. For Ageron, guiding promising warlocks upward strengthens the Forsaken's dark arts and honors the hierarchy among the practitioners in the Magic Quarter.",al={"ageron kargal motive","why send me to halgar","why does ageron want this"},it="motive",add="169af240"},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar summon you specifically?",a="Carendin Halgar rarely reaches out to instruct just any novice. Having proven your affinity for the dark arts in Tirisfal Glades, you have reached a critical threshold in your craft where foundational spells no longer suffice. Halgar summons you directly because unlocking deeper and more volatile powers—such as reaching into the Nether to command greater fiends—demands personal oversight from a true master of the craft.",al={"why does halgar need me","why halgars summons me","why am i summoned"},it="why_me",add="be0d43df"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you pass from elementary training to planar enslavement under the scrutiny of Undercity's foremost master of the dark arts.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you pursue shadow and fel with ruthless ambition. Halgar's sanctum reflects your people's practical disregard for the caution of the living."},kw={"ageron kargal","carendin halgar","halgar's summons","magic quarter","temple of the damned","undercity","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1473","quest:1471","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity"},m={start="Ageron Kargal",["end"]="Carendin Halgar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1478},src={"Halgar's Summons"}}
E["quest:1803"] = {t="quest",n="Tome of the Cabal",z="undercity",s="Horde warlocks seek the Tome of the Cabal's severed halves for Jorah Annison in the Undercity. Once kept in Lordaeron, the grimoire was torn apart and scattered across the world. Its damp, tattered remnants lie along hostile Eastern Kingdoms waters and deep in Kalimdor's centaur territory.",h="Horde warlocks seek the Tome of the Cabal's severed halves for Jorah Annison in the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Divided Legacy",b="The Tome of the Cabal once rested in the library of Lordaeron. Someone deliberately defaced the sinister grimoire, stripping away nearly half its pages and splitting it in two. The surviving formal text was bound for the dwarven halls of Ironforge, but the transport wrecked along the rocky coast west of Southshore. Its pages now rot in the shallows beneath the watch of scavenging murlocs.",sp=0},{t="Scattered across Continents",b="The vandalized half traveled far from Lordaeron to southern Kalimdor. Deep in Splithoof Hold in Thousand Needles, the Galak centaur hold the manuscript roughly. A warlock must search the damp Hillsbrad shoreline for the Moldy Tome, then enter the dusty, savage centaur canyons for the Tattered Manuscript. When both remnants reach Jorah Annison, the legendary dark text is restored to one readable volume.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Tome of the Cabal?",a="The Tome of the Cabal is an arcane grimoire of demonic rituals once kept in Lordaeron's capital. Someone defaced it and split it in two before it was lost across two continents.",al={"tome of the cabal lore","what is this book","tome of cabal"},it="item"},{q="Why is one part of the book near Southshore?",a="After the tome was vandalized, its surviving bound portion was meant for scholars in Ironforge. The vessel carrying it wrecked on the coast west of Southshore, leaving the book stranded among local murlocs.",al={"why southshore","moldy tome origin","coast west of southshore"},it="history"},{q="How did the pages end up with the centaur in Thousand Needles?",a="Roughly half the pages were torn from the original tome in Lordaeron and smuggled away. Through trade, plunder, or wandering hands, the tattered manuscript eventually came to rest deep inside Splithoof Hold, where the Galak centaur keep it in a chest.",al={"why centaur have it","thousand needles pages","splithoof hold book"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Jorah Annison?",a="Jorah Annison is a Forsaken warlock in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. He guides rising Horde warlocks in recovering forgotten, forbidden lore to deepen their mastery of demonic forces.",al={"jorah annison lore","who is jorah"},it="identity"},{q="Who vandalized the tome in the first place?",a="Who vandalized the tome remains unknown. Jorah Annison laments the damage and wonders who could commit such an act against a text with such occult power.",al={"who tore the book","who stole the pages","tome vandal"}},{q="What does Jorah do with the book once you bring both parts back?",a="When you bring both the Moldy Tome and the Tattered Manuscript, Jorah Annison assembles them into one volume and reads its pages, preparing you for the next steps in your demonic rites.",al={"what happens after turn in","restored tome"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Jorah Annison want the Tome of the Cabal?",a="Jorah Annison is a Forsaken warlock scholar dedicated to unearthing lost fel lore once housed in Lordaeron. Recovering the fractured Tome of the Cabal allows him to study its occult secrets firsthand while guiding promising warlocks in mastering dangerous, advanced summonings.",al={"why does jorah want this","jorah annison motive","why collect the tome of the cabal"},it="motive",add="a3cceb5d"},{q="What is the Moldy Tome?",a="The Moldy Tome contains the salvaged remains of the original text meant for transfer to Ironforge. Lost in a shipwreck along the coast near Southshore and scavenged by murlocs, it holds one vital half of the Cabal's rituals.",al={"what is moldy tome","moldy tome lore","use of moldy tome"},it="item",add="968099ef"},{q="What is the Tattered Manuscript?",a="The Tattered Manuscript is the missing half of the Tome of the Cabal, torn away when the book was vandalized in Lordaeron. Through unknown hands, these stolen pages crossed the sea into Kalimdor, eventually ending up locked in a chest among the Galak centaur of Thousand Needles.",al={"what is tattered manuscript","tattered manuscript lore","use of tattered manuscript"},it="item",add="2b99c3ce"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you reclaim the Tome of the Cabal as a rite of passage for an intermediate practitioner. Its lost Lordaeron arcana can expand your summoning repertoire.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you recover a tome once kept in Lordaeron, before the kingdom fell. Its return reclaims occult heritage from your past human lives.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you track the manuscript through the canyons of Thousand Needles. Horde forces at Freewind Post wage constant war against the native centaur."},kw={"galak","jorah annison","lordaeron","moldy tome","southshore","splithoof hold","tattered manuscript","thousand needles","tome of the cabal","warlock quest"},rel={"npc:jorah-annison","zone:undercity","subzone:southshore","subzone:splithoof-hold","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","topic:murloc","quest:4841"},m={start="Jorah Annison",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1803,ri={"Moldy Tome","Tattered Manuscript"}},src={"Tome of the Cabal (Horde, 2)"}}
E["quest:1846"] = {t="quest",n="Dragonmaw Shinbones",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Velora Nitely sends Horde warriors to gather Dragonmaw Shinbones for Brutal Legguards. The hunt leads to the southern Wetlands, where the hostile orcs carry bones thick enough to brace the armor.",h="In the Undercity, Velora Nitely sends Horde warriors to gather Dragonmaw Shinbones for Brutal Legguards.",sec={{t="A Gruesome Armature",b="Velora Nitely, a Forsaken armorer in the Undercity, needs a strong brace for Brutal Legguards. She sends Horde warriors to the Wetlands for thick, resilient bone from the Dragonmaw orcs. Their dense frames can bear the heavy blows a seasoned warrior faces.",sp=0},{t="Testing the Marrow",b="Velora needs more than any bone taken from the Dragonmaw. Each one must withstand a hand test; a bone that snaps is too brittle for the forge. Warriors scour the renegade camps along the Wetlands' crags, breaking weak specimens until eight sturdy shinbones remain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Velora Nitely need orc shinbones specifically?",a="Velora needs thick, dense bone to brace the Brutal Legguards. She judges the Dragonmaw orcs' heavy frames better suited to the work than ordinary game or scavenged remains.",al={"why orc shinbones","why dragonmaw bones","velora bone armor"},it="item"},{q="Why are the Dragonmaw orcs fair game for Horde warriors?",a="The Dragonmaw remnants in the Wetlands are hostile renegades still tied to the dark legacy of the Second War. They owe no allegiance to Thrall's Horde, so Horde warriors may hunt them as enemies.",al={"are dragonmaw in the horde","why fight dragonmaw","dragonmaw horde standing"},it="target"},{q="Where are the Dragonmaw found for this task?",a="The Dragonmaw are in the Wetlands, south across the Thandol Span from the Arathi Highlands. Warriors hunt near the mountainous bluffs of Angerfang Encampment, southwest of the main northern highway.",al={"dragonmaw location","where to find dragonmaw shinbones","angerfang encampment location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do so many of the bones break during the quest?",a="Velora needs the densest bones for the armor's frame. Warriors test each one by hand and discard any that snap under force, since brittle bone cannot protect a warrior's legs in battle.",al={"broken shinbones","why do shinbones snap","sturdy bone test"},gp=true},{q="Who is Velora Nitely?",a="Velora Nitely is a Forsaken armorer in the Undercity. Gruff and morbidly dry, she uses grim humor while helping Horde warriors make specialized gear for battle-hardened veterans.",al={"velora nitely lore","who is velora","undercity armorer"},it="identity"},{q="What armor piece is forged from these bones?",a="The bones frame the Brutal Legguards, durable mail legguards made for mid-level Horde warriors.",al={"shinbones reward","what are the shinbones for","brutal legguards craft"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Velora Nitely want this done?",a="Velora Nitely needs shinbones from Dragonmaw orcs in the Wetlands to craft your Brutal Legguards. Their sturdy bones provide material for the armor she has agreed to make.",al={"velora nitely motive","why does velora want shinbones","velora nitely why"},it="motive",add="0579d748"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you test your strength in the field and gather grim materials to make stronger armor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you weaken a dangerous Old Horde remnant in Khaz Modan and strengthen Thrall's coalition.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc loyal to Orgrimmar, you face the unrepentant Dragonmaw and the violent cost of your people's redemption from their fel past.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see Velora Nitely put humanoid remains to practical use, as the Forsaken make use of every resource, however grim."},kw={"angerfang encampment","brutal legguards","dragonmaw","shinbones","thandol span","undercity","velora nitely","wetlands"},rel={"npc:velora-nitely","quest:1841","subzone:angerfang-encampment","zone:wetlands","subzone:thandol-span","zone:undercity","zone:arathi","subzone:hammerfall"},m={start="Velora Nitely",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1846,ri={"Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbone"}},src={"Dragonmaw Shinbones"}}
E["quest:1881"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Anastasia",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Cain Firesong sends a promising Forsaken mage to Anastasia Hartwell. Her summons calls you to the Magic Quarter for work among the Forsaken magi, with investigations in Tirisfal Glades ahead.",h="In the Undercity, Cain Firesong sends a promising Forsaken mage to Anastasia Hartwell.",sec={{t="A Call to the Magic Quarter",b="Cain Firesong trains young Forsaken mages in Brill, then sends those with promise to the Undercity. In its Magic Quarter, the Forsaken magi pursue arcane study and plan defenses across Lordaeron. Cain judges which students are ready to serve more experienced practitioners. Those who show real talent are sent to Anastasia Hartwell, who needs capable hands in the field.",sp=0},{t="Anastasia Hartwell's Ambition",b="Anastasia Hartwell is one of the Undercity's prominent mage instructors. She puts promising students to work for the Forsaken's practical and territorial interests instead of leaving them to study incantations in safety. Answering her call marks a step into service for the Forsaken's mages and their pragmatic magical work in the years after the Scourge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Anastasia Hartwell?",a="Cain Firesong, your Forsaken mage trainer in Brill, sends you to Anastasia Hartwell when he judges your arcane talent ready for harder work in the Undercity.",al={"who gives speak with anastasia","quest giver speak with anastasia","cain firesong summons"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Anastasia Hartwell be found?",a="Anastasia Hartwell is in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, where she instructs Forsaken practitioners of the arcane arts.",al={"where is anastasia hartwell","anastasia hartwell location","find anastasia"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this summons?",a="Anastasia seeks a capable caster for practical work beyond the city walls, beginning with field assignments in Tirisfal Glades, such as investigating the Balnir Farmstead.",al={"why does she want me","speak with anastasia purpose","what does anastasia need"},it="purpose"},{q="What quest follows Speak with Anastasia?",a="After you report to Anastasia, she sends you to The Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal Glades to gather snapdragons from its garden.",al={"what quest comes next","next quest after speak with anastasia","speak with anastasia followup"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest limited to certain classes?",a="Yes. This summons is for Forsaken mages, marking a step in their class training as they reach early competence around circle ten.",al={"is this a mage only quest","who can do speak with anastasia","class requirement"},gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken mages maintain their own quarters in Undercity?",a="The Magic Quarter gives Forsaken arcanists, warlocks, and researchers a place to study and cast apart from the physical quarters. There, they continue traditions from before the Third War beneath Lordaeron.",al={"why magic quarter","forsaken mages undercity"},it="history"},{q="Why does Cain Firesong send you to Anastasia Hartwell?",a="Cain Firesong serves as an instructor for fledgling Forsaken mages in Brill. Once you demonstrate sufficient skill in the arcane arts, his duty is to direct promising spellcasters to Anastasia Hartwell in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Hartwell coordinates greater undertakings for the Forsaken's magical order, and Cain ensures their ranks are replenished with capable practitioners ready for service.",al={"why does cain send you","cain firesong motive","why visit anastasia hartwell"},it="motive",add="34129032"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you move from basic arcane training into active service for the mages of the Undercity.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken arcanist, you can put Lordaeron's intellectual past to work against the perils facing it now."},kw={"anastasia hartwell","balnir farmstead","cain firesong","mage quest","magic quarter","undercity"},rel={"npc:anastasia-hartwell","npc:cain-firesong","quest:1882","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","subzone:balnir-farmstead","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Cain Firesong",["end"]="Anastasia Hartwell",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1881},src={"Speak with Anastasia"}}
E["quest:1882"] = {t="quest",n="The Balnir Farmstead",z="undercity",s="In eastern Tirisfal, snapdragons at the Balnir Farmstead may show how far the Scourge's corruption has spread. Anastasia Hartwell sends young Forsaken mages to gather them for study in the Undercity.",h="In eastern Tirisfal, snapdragons at the Balnir Farmstead may show how far the Scourge's corruption has spread.",sec={{t="A Magical Barometer",b="Forsaken mages watch the borderlands for signs of magical corruption. Anastasia Hartwell sends novice spellcasters to the Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal Glades to gather snapdragons from its gardens. The flowers absorb magical energies from the soil and air. By examining them, arcane scholars in the Undercity can judge whether corruption from the Lich King's domain has reached Tirisfal.",sp=0},{t="The Eastern Border",b="The Balnir Farmstead lies near the edge of the glades, close to the blighted wilderness of the Western Plaguelands. The Forsaken know the Lich King's plague rots the land, while Scourge corruption threatens their borders and security. The Forsaken wield dark arts of their own, but Anastasia plans to pass the snapdragons to the apothecaries for study. Mages and alchemists can examine the danger together and help defend Lordaeron's reclaimed heartland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell want snapdragons specifically?",a="Balnir snapdragons are sensitive to magical forces and absorb energy from the earth and air. Studying them can show Forsaken mages whether the Plaguelands' arcane and necromantic blight is reaching Tirisfal Glades.",al={"why snapdragons","balnir snapdragons purpose","what are snapdragons for"},it="item"},{q="Where is the Balnir Farmstead located?",a="The Balnir Farmstead lies in eastern Tirisfal Glades, near the border with the blighted Western Plaguelands. Snapdragons grow in the plots and gardens around its decrepit farm buildings.",al={"balnir farmstead location","where is balnir farm","find balnir farmstead"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Anastasia Hartwell?",a="Anastasia Hartwell is a Forsaken mage and trainer in the Undercity's Mage Quarter. She teaches newly risen undead casters discipline, arcane balance, and how to defend their borders against rival powers.",al={"anastasia hartwell lore","who is anastasia"},it="identity"},{q="Why do Forsaken mages care about stopping the plague?",a="The Forsaken see the Lich King's infectious scourge magic as uncontrolled, even as they experiment with plagues and blights of their own. Left unchecked, the Scourge could consume Tirisfal Glades and threaten Forsaken independence.",al={"why stop the plague","do forsaken hate the plague"},it="motive"},{q="What happens to the flowers after you collect them?",a="Anastasia plans to pass the snapdragons to the Undercity's apothecaries. Alchemists and mages will examine them to learn how deeply the Scourge has tainted the soil and plants.",al={"what does anastasia do with the flowers","who gets the snapdragons"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest restricted to mages?",a="Yes. Anastasia offers this trial only to young Forsaken mages who have finished their first lessons in Deathknell and reached the capital to prove their grasp of arcane theory.",al={"is balnir farmstead mage only","mage class quest"},gp=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you learn early that arcane study can help watch for and defend against foreign magical corruption.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you depend on keeping the Scourge from Tirisfal's borders to protect your survival and sovereignty.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you see how a plant can hold traces of magical pollution and reveal its presence."},kw={"anastasia","balnir","farmstead","hartwell","mage","plaguelands","snapdragons","tirisfal","undercity"},rel={"npc:anastasia-hartwell","quest:1881","subzone:balnir-farmstead","subzone:mage-quarter","zone:undercity","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:lich-king"},m={start="Anastasia Hartwell",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1882,ri={"Balnir Snapdragons"}},src={"The Balnir Farmstead"}}
E["quest:1885"] = {t="quest",n="Mennet Carkad",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Marion Call sends you to report to Mennet Carkad. He waits deep in the Rogues' Quarter, where promising operatives are tested for the Deathstalkers.",h="In the Undercity, Marion Call sends you to report to Mennet Carkad.",sec={{t="A Summons from the Shadows",b="Marion Call has a summons for you from Mennet Carkad. In the Undercity, covert operatives draw the notice of higher leadership, and Marion passes along word when a scout or assassin is invited to report. The Forsaken's intelligence apparatus has a lethal reputation, so ignoring its orders is no real choice.",sp=0},{t="Joining the Deathstalkers",b="Mennet Carkad waits in the Rogues' Quarter, watching recruits and judging whether they are ready. Those who answer his call are tested for entry into the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken's feared arm of espionage and assassination. Obedience is the first test for anyone who seeks to serve the Dark Lady from the shadows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mennet Carkad?",a="Mennet Carkad trains rogues and handles Deathstalkers in the Undercity's Rogues' Quarter. He oversees promising covert agents and assigns critical work for the Forsaken leadership.",al={"mennet carkad lore","who is carkad"},it="target"},{q="What happens if someone ignores Mennet Carkad's summons?",a="Marion Call warns that you would not want to know what happened to those who ignored Carkad's call. She does not explain their exact fate.",al={"ignoring carkad","what happens if you ignore summons"},it="danger"},{q="Who are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are an elite order of rogues, spies, and assassins who serve the Forsaken. From the shadows of the Undercity, they eliminate high-value targets, gather intelligence, and defend Lordaeron from enemies such as the Scarlet Crusade and the Scourge.",al={"deathstalker lore","what are the deathstalkers"},it="people"},{q="Where can I find Mennet Carkad?",a="You can find Mennet Carkad in the Undercity's Rogues' Quarter, among covert operatives, trainers, and shadowcraft supplies.",al={"carkad location","where is mennet carkad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives the quest to seek out Mennet Carkad?",a="Marion Call sends you to find Mennet Carkad from Brill's Gallows' End Tavern. She has noticed your growing skills and warns that Carkad expects prompt obedience.",al={"who starts this quest","marion call quest"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What comes after reporting to Mennet Carkad?",a="Reporting to Mennet Carkad leads directly into service for the Deathstalkers. Your first duties are meant to prove your cunning and loyalty to the Forsaken cause.",al={"next quest after carkad","what does carkad want"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Marion Call send you to Mennet Carkad?",a="Marion Call says that Mennet Carkad has taken notice of you and expects a meeting. She urges you to heed his summons and gives an ominous warning about those who ignored it, without explaining their fate.",al={"why does marion call want this done","why go to mennet carkad","marion call motive"},it="motive",add="f971228d"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you answer a summons that marks your passage from unproven cutpurse to recognized asset of the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken's elite shadow network.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the Deathstalkers help keep the Forsaken alive. They hunt Scarlet zealots and Scourge remnants, and protect Queen Sylvanas from hidden threats."},kw={"assassin","deathstalkers","forsaken rogue","marion call","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","undercity"},rel={"quest:1886","subzone:rogues-quarter","zone:undercity"},m={start="Marion Call",["end"]="Mennet Carkad",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1885},src={"Mennet Carkad (quest)"}}
E["quest:1886"] = {t="quest",n="The Deathstalkers",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Mennet Carkad tests hopeful Deathstalkers with a demand for ruthless initiative: intercept a traveling messenger. The trial opens the way into the covert order serving Lord Varimathras.",h="In the Undercity, Mennet Carkad tests hopeful Deathstalkers with a demand for ruthless initiative: intercept...",sec={{t="A Test in the Shadows",b="The Deathstalkers serve Varimathras as the Forsaken's secret police and elite assassination corps. In the Rogues' Quarter, handler Mennet Carkad sets a trial for anyone seeking a place among them. A hopeful agent must show cunning, discretion, and the will to eliminate a target. Carkad's test is meant to turn away the weak and those troubled by too many scruples.",sp=0},{t="The Interception",b="Astor Hadren carries a letter along the road between the Undercity and Silverpine Forest. Carkad leaves the approach to the recruit. To secure Hadren's personal introduction, the initiate must intercept him and seize his credentials, so the Deathstalkers can pass their recruit off in his place to Andron.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the Forsaken's covert order and elite stealth and assassination branch. From the Rogues' Quarter in the Undercity, they handle espionage, covert executions, and information gathering, reporting to Lord Varimathras.",al={"deathstalkers lore","what are deathstalkers","undead rogues"},it="people"},{q="Who is Mennet Carkad?",a="Mennet Carkad is a Deathstalker handler in the Undercity's Rogues' Quarter. He oversees early trials and tests recruits hoping to join the covert ranks.",al={"mennet carkad role","who gives quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Mennet need Astor Hadren's letter?",a="Astor Hadren's letter of introduction lets a new operative take his place. The Deathstalkers can use it to deceive Andron.",al={"astor hadren letter","why intercept messenger","astor letter of introduction"},it="item"},{q="Where does Astor Hadren travel?",a="Astor Hadren travels the road between the Undercity and Silverpine Forest, carrying correspondence for his contacts.",al={"astor hadren route","astor hadren location","where is astor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Lord Varimathras?",a="Lord Varimathras is a Nathrezim dreadlord who allied with Queen Sylvanas Windrunner to preserve his own existence. From the Royal Quarter, he oversees the Undercity's security, defense, and rogue operations.",al={"varimathras role","dreadlord in undercity"},it="leader"},{q="What happens after this trial?",a="Passing the trial proves an operative's competence. It leads to a covert impersonation assignment: deliver Astor's papers and infiltrate Andron's dealings.",al={"what comes next","deathstalkers questline continuation"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad want this done?",a="Mennet Carkad is running an infiltration operation that hinges on intercepting communication meant for a contact named Andron. By stealing Astor Hadren's letter, Mennet secures the credentials needed to slip an operative into Andron's confidence unnoticed.",al={"why does mennet need this","mennet carkad motive","why steal the letter"},it="motive",add="1398690a"},{q="Who is Astor Hadren?",a="Astor Hadren is a courier traveling between Silverpine Forest and the Undercity. He carries an introductory letter intended for a contact named Andron, unaware that the Deathstalkers are targeting his correspondence for their own covert schemes.",al={"who is hadren","astor hadren","target astor hadren"},it="target",add="763d70d5"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad send you instead of an established agent?",a="You are seeking to prove yourself worthy of joining the Deathstalkers, the elite rogues serving Lord Varimathras. Mennet deliberately uses aspiring recruits for dangerous, expendable field trials to see if they possess the cunning and lethality needed for the order.",al={"why me deathstalkers","why send me mennet","why not use existing deathstalker"},it="why_me",add="f8c6b26b"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Forsaken rogue, joining the Deathstalkers means reaching the highest echelon of state service, where streetwise scoundrels become sworn instruments of Varimathras and the Dark Lady.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see the Deathstalkers enforce Lordaeron's internal security with an iron grip. They watch for external foes and keep a watchful, paranoid eye on potential traitors within the Forsaken.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you may not know how deeply the Deathstalkers operate in secrecy. They maintain vital intelligence networks while the Horde's southern allies remain largely unaware of the Forsaken's shadier domestic affairs."},kw={"astor hadren","deathstalkers","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","silverpine","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"npc:varimathras","subzone:rogues-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:1885"},m={start="Mennet Carkad",level="13",faction="Horde",id=1886,ri={"Astor's Letter of Introduction"}},src={"The Deathstalkers"}}
E["quest:1898"] = {t="quest",n="The Deathstalkers",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, the Deathstalkers move against suspected treason in the Forsaken's own ranks. Under Lord Varimathras's orders, you pose as an expected messenger and question a merchant who may be aiding an outside faction.",h="In the Undercity, the Deathstalkers move against suspected treason in the Forsaken's own ranks.",sec={{t="A Web of Deceit",b="Deathstalker Mennet Carkad sets an infiltration in motion at Lord Varimathras's urging. The Deathstalkers watch the Forsaken's own citizens as closely as they guard against outside threats. With Astor Hadren's letter of introduction, forged or acquired, you approach the local merchant Andron Gant and try to pass as the courier he expects.",sp=0},{t="The Shop Near the Apothecarium",b="Andron Gant keeps a shop near the Apothecarium. Mennet believes the shopkeeper lacks the wit to spot an impostor. When you show the letter, Gant accepts your cover as a courier, lowers his guard, and begins describing dealings with an unidentified third party.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Andron Gant?",a="Andron Gant is a shopkeeper in the Undercity, near the Apothecarium. The Deathstalkers and Lord Varimathras suspect he is funneling intelligence and aid to an unknown outside faction.",al={"andron gant","who is gant","where is andron gant"},it="target"},{q="Why is Lord Varimathras interested in this merchant?",a="Lord Varimathras suspects Gant is working with an organization outside the Forsaken. He wants proof of Gant's contacts and intentions to protect the city and root out subversion.",al={"why varimathras cares","varimathras andron gant","why spy on andron"},it="conflict"},{q="How does the player deceive Andron Gant?",a="Mennet Carkad gives you Astor's Letter of Introduction. Gant expects a courier, and the Deathstalkers consider him easy to fool, so the letter wins his confidence.",al={"astors letter","how to trick andron gant","messenger disguise"}},{q="What group are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the Forsaken's elite rogue order and secret intelligence agency. They work from the shadows under Queen Sylvanas and Lord Varimathras to uncover sedition, sabotage enemies, and remove threats within their ranks.",al={"deathstalkers lore","who are deathstalkers","undercity rogues"},it="history"},{q="Where can Andron Gant be found?",a="Andron Gant works in his shop near the entrance to the Apothecarium quarter in the Undercity. He does business under the watch of the Royal Apothecary Society and the Deathstalkers.",al={"andron gant location","where is gant shop"},gp=true},{q="What happens after Gant accepts the letter?",a="Gant accepts the letter without suspicion and takes you for a messenger with nothing to hide. He hints at cooperation with mutual acquaintances, giving you a chance to seek further proof of his betrayal.",al={"what does gant do","gant reaction"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad want Andron Gant investigated?",a="Mennet Carkad is acting directly on the orders of Lord Varimathras. The dreadlord suspects that Andron Gant is secretly funneling aid and intelligence to an unknown rival faction from within the Undercity. To protect the Forsaken leadership from internal subversion, Mennet needs definitive proof of Gant's betrayal and the identity of the shadowy organization he serves.",al={"why investigate andron gant","mennet carkad motive","why does mennet send me to gant"},it="motive",add="6d39edb7"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad send you instead of going himself?",a="Mennet Carkad has already met Andron Gant in person, making his own presence an immediate compromise of the mission. Gant would instantly recognize a known Deathstalker operative. Because you possess Astor Hadren's letter of introduction, Gant has no reason to suspect you are anything other than the courier he was scheduled to meet.",al={"why does mennet need me","why cant mennet speak to gant","why use an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="3bf738ba"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you use a dead man's identity to draw out a careless conspirator, a method the Deathstalkers know well.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know vigilance means survival. A citizen found aiding outside factions risks being purged by the dark lady's secret police.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you know political intrigue reaches beneath the Undercity. Even within Horde borders, trust is scarce."},kw={"andron gant","apothecarium","astor hadren","deathstalkers","espionage","forsaken","mennet carkad","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1886","npc:andron-gant","npc:varimathras","quest:1885","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity"},m={start="Mennet Carkad",["end"]="Andron Gant",level="13",faction="Horde",id=1898},src={"The Deathstalkers (2)"}}
E["quest:1899"] = {t="quest",n="The Deathstalkers",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, the Deathstalkers turn Andron Gant's trust against him. Still believing you are the messenger he expected, Gant gives you a ledger for his secret contacts. You carry it to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter, opening the way to deeper covert work for the Forsaken state.",h="In the Undercity, the Deathstalkers turn Andron Gant's trust against him.",sec={{t="A Courier in the Shadows",b="Andron Gant works from the Undercity, keeping names and information in a personal ledger. Believing you are the courier he expected, he hands it over for delivery to the secret contacts he serves. Gant asks that the same courier carry future messages, unaware that the ledger is bound for the Deathstalkers.",sp=0},{t="Intelligence in the Rogues' Quarter",b="Mennet Carkad receives Gant's ledger in the Rogues' Quarter and finds more useful intelligence in it than expected. The details give Carkad leads for widening the Deathstalkers' investigations. In the wary Forsaken realm, those records can help uncover subversion within and threats beyond its borders before they reach the capital.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is in Andron's Ledger?",a="Andron Gant's ledger holds sensitive information and records he gathered. Mennet Carkad finds more detail and valuable intelligence in it than the Deathstalkers expected.",al={"andron ledger contents","what does the ledger say","deathstalker ledger"},it="item"},{q="Who are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the Forsaken's covert organization and assassin guild. Based in the Undercity's Rogues' Quarter, they serve Lady Sylvanas Windrunner as eyes, ears, and hidden daggers, handling espionage, intelligence, and targeted assassinations across Lordaeron.",al={"deathstalker lore","who are deathstalkers","undercity rogues"},it="people"},{q="Why does Gant want the same courier used in the future?",a="Gant asks for the same courier because he wants future sensitive documents handled by a runner he trusts, preserving their working arrangement and reducing the risk of theft or tampering.",al={"why does gant like you","andron gant trust","gant courier"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Mennet Carkad?",a="Mennet Carkad is a Deathstalkers operative stationed in the Rogues' Quarter. He coordinates local agents, gathers field intelligence from informants such as Andron Gant, and directs covert assignments throughout the capital and surrounding territories.",al={"mennet carkad lore","who is carkad"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Rogues' Quarter located?",a="The Rogues' Quarter lies in the southern district of the Undercity. It is the main base for Forsaken stealth operatives, thieves, and assassins, with training grounds and dark alcoves away from the public plazas of the upper ruins.",al={"rogues quarter location","where is rogues quarter","undercity rogues quarter"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken need an internal intelligence agency?",a="The Forsaken need internal intelligence to uncover subversion within Lordaeron's borders. The Deathstalkers work to help the young nation survive threats from the Scourge, the Scarlet Crusade, wary Alliance remnants, infiltration, and rebellion.",al={"why deathstalkers exist","forsaken spies","undercity intelligence"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Andron Gant want the ledger delivered?",a="Andron Gant believes you are the messenger sent by the secret contacts he has been supplying with information. He hands over the ledger for them and asks that you be sent again if they wish to continue the arrangement, never suspecting that it will go straight to the Deathstalkers.",al={"why deliver the ledger","andron gant motive","why is andron cooperating"},it="motive",add="63e535f7"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue in the Undercity, you can show your discretion by carrying sensitive messages for Mennet Carkad without drawing unwanted attention.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know that the Undercity's security is a matter of survival. Helping the Deathstalkers strengthens the Dark Lady's hold over the capital against living infiltrators and rival undead."},kw={"andron gant","assassins","deathstalkers","espionage","ledger","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","undercity"},rel={"npc:andron-gant","subzone:rogues-quarter","zone:undercity"},m={start="Andron Gant",["end"]="Mennet Carkad",level="13",faction="Horde",id=1899,ri={"Andron's Ledger"}},src={"The Deathstalkers (3)"}}
E["quest:1960"] = {t="quest",n="Investigate the Alchemist Shop",z="undercity",s="An arcane disturbance has brought invisible creatures into Algernon's shop in the Undercity. Anastasia Hartwell sends Horde mages to reveal and contain them before they can cause harm.",h="An arcane disturbance has brought invisible creatures into Algernon's shop in the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Disturbance in the Apothecarium",b="Anastasia Hartwell sends arcane initiates to investigate a disturbance in the Apothecarium. Invisible magical creatures have been wandering through Algernon's alchemy shop, among its cauldrons and reagents. The Undercity's mage instructor suspects a breach in the flow of magic. The creatures must be contained before they cause serious damage.",sp=0},{t="Manifestation and Containment",b="Anastasia gives her students a Cantation of Manifestation to reveal the invisible creatures, along with sturdy containment coffers. Ordinary tracking cannot find beings made entirely of raw arcane force. Once visible, the rift spawns must be weakened and sealed in the coffers before they can unravel further or harm the alchemists at work.",sp=0},{t="Accident or Arcane Assault?",b="Anastasia wants to learn where the creatures came from. A spontaneous rift in the flow of magic is troubling; an intentional breach could mean a coordinated magical assault on the Forsaken capital. The captured creatures go to Undercity scholars for study, who must determine whether the Apothecarium suffered an accident or faces a targeted threat.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest and where do I find them?",a="Anastasia Hartwell, the mage trainer, offers this in the Undercity's Magic Quarter.",al={"quest giver","where to start","anastasia location"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Where is the disturbance located?",a="The disturbance is in Algernon's alchemy shop, in the Undercity's Apothecarium district.",al={"where do i go","alchemist shop location","where is algernon"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are the creatures wandering the shop?",a="The creatures are rift spawns, invisible beings made of concentrated magical energy that appeared through an anomaly in the local flow of magic.",al={"what are the monsters","invisible creatures","rift spawns"},it="target"},{q="How do you capture the creatures?",a="You recite the Cantation of Manifestation in the shop to reveal the rift spawns, weaken them with spells, then use a containment coffer to trap them.",al={"how to catch them","using the coffer","how to complete"},gp=true},{q="Why does Anastasia want these creatures captured alive?",a="Anastasia and the Undercity's scholars need live specimens to learn whether the tear in magic came from a natural rift or an intentional attack on the city by an outside magical force.",al={"why capture them","containment coffers purpose","why study them"},it="motive"},{q="Can classes other than mages do this quest?",a="Only Horde mages can take part; this is part of their early training.",al={"mage only","who can take this quest"},gp=true},{q="What is the Cantation of Manifestation for?",a="The Cantation of Manifestation is an incantation inscribed upon a scroll, provided by Anastasia Hartwell to reveal the unseen. The entities haunting Algernon's shop are pure magical energy and naturally invisible to the naked eye. Reading the cantation within the shop tears away their veil of concealment, forcing them into physical manifestation so you can battle and subdue them.",al={"cantation of manifestation purpose","why use cantation of manifestation","what does the cantation do"},it="item",add="20993eae"},{q="What is the Chest of Containment Coffers for?",a="The Chest of Containment Coffers holds specially warded vessels crafted to bind raw magical entities. Because the rift spawns in the Apothecarium cannot simply be carried by hand, you must deploy these arcane coffers once the creatures are weakened in combat, securely trapping them inside so they can be transported without dissipating.",al={"chest of containment coffers","what are containment coffers","purpose of containment coffers"},it="item",add="355e23e2"},{q="What is the Filled Containment Coffer for?",a="Each Filled Containment Coffer holds a living rift spawn captured from Algernon's shop. Anastasia Hartwell requires three of these trapped entities brought back intact so the Undercity's greatest arcane scholars can examine them, unraveling whether their sudden manifestation was an accidental tear in the weave of magic or a deliberate assault.",al={"filled containment coffer use","why bring filled coffers","filled containment coffer purpose"},it="item",add="01d568c5"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you test your command of arcane forces with manifestation cantations and containment vessels, not destructive force alone.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you see the Undercity's arcane scholars guarding the city against magical infiltration, alongside apothecaries focused on alchemy and plaguecraft."},kw={"algernon","anastasia hartwell","apothecarium","cantation of manifestation","containment coffer","magic quarter","rift spawn","undercity"},rel={"npc:anastasia-hartwell","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","quest:1959"},m={start="Anastasia Hartwell",["end"]="Anastasia Hartwell",level="16",faction="Horde",id=1960,ri={"Cantation of Manifestation","Chest of Containment Coffers","Filled Containment Coffer"}},src={"Investigate the Alchemist Shop"}}
E["quest:1961"] = {t="quest",n="Gathering Materials",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Anastasia Hartwell sends aspiring Horde mages to Silverpine Forest for Dalaran mana gems. They also need linen to make their first true mage's robes.",h="In the Undercity, Anastasia Hartwell sends aspiring Horde mages to Silverpine Forest for Dalaran mana gems.",sec={{t="A Rite of Arcane Standing",b="Undercity initiates gather the materials for their first true robes: a bolt of simple linen and potent Dalaran mana gems. The robes mark their station and personal worth, and Anastasia Hartwell directs the novices to harvest these raw components for an enchanted weave.",sp=0},{t="Pragmatism of the Forsaken",b="The mana gems cannot be bought or conjured. Dalaran mages are stationed across Silverpine Forest, especially near Ambermill, and the gems must be taken from them. Anastasia Hartwell says Dalaran's arcane philosophies mirror those of the Forsaken, but sentiment has no place in the Undercity. To the Forsaken, wizards too weak to defend their relics forfeit both their treasures and their lives.",sp=0},{t="The Tailor of the Magic Quarter",b="Josef Gregorian, a tailor in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, receives the gathered cloth and gems. He admits he lacks the magical talent to judge the pristine quality of Dalaran's enchanted stones, but he has the rare artisan skill to weave their raw power into the robes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Gathering Materials?",a="The rite initiates Horde mages into their first formal enchanted robes. The linen and mana gems go to tailor Josef Gregorian, who uses them to craft the robes.",al={"why do gathering materials","gathering materials quest purpose","mage robe quest undercity"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell send you after Dalaran mages?",a="Dalaran wizards stationed across Silverpine Forest carry refined mana gems that channel strong magical currents. Anastasia Hartwell sees their shared arcane philosophies, but believes weakness in the field forfeits their lives and resources to the Forsaken.",al={"why kill dalaran mages","dalaran mana gems lore","why silverpine mages"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the Dalaran wizards located?",a="Dalaran wizards are stationed across Silverpine Forest, particularly near Ambermill and around the grounds southeast of the Sepulcher.",al={"where to find dalaran mana gems","silverpine mages location","ambermill mages"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who is Josef Gregorian?",a="Josef Gregorian is an Undead tailor in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. Though he is no arcane spellcaster, he specializes in stitching enchanted garments like spellfire robes.",al={"josef gregorian undercity","who is the tailor in magic quarter","gregorian tailor"},it="identity"},{q="What robes are crafted from these materials?",a="Josef Gregorian uses the linen and Dalaran mana gems to stitch Spellfire Robes, a classic garment that marks an apprentice's passage into an established mage.",al={"what robe do you get","spellfire robes reward","gathering materials reward robe"},it="item"},{q="Why does Anastasia find killing Dalaran mages somewhat distasteful?",a="Anastasia Hartwell finds the killing distasteful because Dalaran mages share many arcane beliefs and philosophies with Forsaken mages. Still, survival and necessity outweigh sentiment.",al={"hartwell dalaran feelings","forsaken mages vs dalaran","anastasia hartwell lore"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Linen Cloth for?",a="The linen cloth serves as the mundane foundation for your Spellfire Robes. Josef Gregorian, the tailor in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, weaves the fabric into fine garments before weaving magical reagents into the threads to empower them.",al={"linen cloth use","why linen cloth","what is linen for"},it="item",add="e61c0dee"},{q="What is the Dalaran Mana Gem for?",a="Dalaran mana gems hold raw arcane energy channeled by the Kirin Tor mages. Josef Gregorian stitches them directly into your robes to infuse the fabric with the magical power required to forge true spellfire garments.",al={"dalaran mana gem use","why dalaran mana gems","what are the mana gems for"},it="item",add="8f9ef647"},{q="Who are the Dalaran mages in Silverpine Forest?",a="They are human sorcerers loyal to Dalaran, stationed around Ambermill in eastern Silverpine Forest. Though their arcane discipline mirrors that of the Forsaken mages, their presence directly threatens Undercity's dominion over the region, making them prime targets for ambitious apprentices.",al={"dalaran wizards silverpine","who are the dalaran mages","dalaran humans silverpine"},it="target",add="608132d5"},{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell send an apprentice instead of handling it herself?",a="Earning your first mage's robes is a rite of passage. Anastasia Hartwell expects you to prove your worth and arcane station by taking reagents from rival spellcasters through force of will and personal power.",al={"why me gathering materials","why send apprentice","why doesn't anastasia get the gems"},it="why_me",add="1cfe23fe"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Horde mage, you reach a milestone when you leave simple apprentice attire for tailored robes woven with captured arcane power.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you see the Forsaken's ruthless outlook: shared arcane philosophies with Dalaran's sorcerers bring no mercy when those wizards prove too weak to hold Silverpine.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you bind mundane linen cloth with potent mana gems to make enduring enchanted garments."},kw={"ambermill","anastasia hartwell","dalaran mana gem","gathering materials","josef gregorian","linen cloth","magic quarter","spellfire robes","undercity"},rel={"quest:1962","npc:anastasia-hartwell","npc:josef-gregorian","subzone:magic-quarter","subzone:ambermill","subzone:dalaran","subzone:sepulcher","quest:1960"},m={start="Anastasia Hartwell",["end"]="Josef Gregorian",level="15",faction="Horde",id=1961,ri={"Dalaran Mana Gem","Linen Cloth"}},src={"Gathering Materials (Horde)"}}
E["quest:1962"] = {t="quest",n="Spellfire Robes",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Spellfire Robes mark a young Horde mage's rite of passage. Josef Gregorian, a tailor, completes the robes after the apprentice gathers rare components from across the realm.",h="In the Undercity, Spellfire Robes mark a young Horde mage's rite of passage.",sec={{t="A Mage's Vestment",b="In Lordaeron, you seek more than ordinary cloth to channel and shield your growing magic. Josef Gregorian works as a tailor in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, where he weaves magical garments from specialized materials gathered by promising Horde spellcasters. The final stitching marks your passage beyond basic incantations toward mastery of arcane and fire magic.",sp=0},{t="Woven Power",b="Josef Gregorian needs alchemical and arcane components to make robes that focus powerful magic. You gather those supplies through dangerous trials and bring them to his sanctum in the Undercity. There, Gregorian weaves them together, giving you a sign of growing status and protection as an aspiring mage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Spellfire Robes quest?",a="This rite is the final step in an early class rite for Horde mages. After gathering tailoring components, you receive specially enchanted robes from Josef Gregorian.",al={"spellfire robes purpose","what do spellfire robes do","why do this quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Josef Gregorian?",a="Josef Gregorian is a Forsaken tailor in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. He stitches the first proper class garments for newly minted mages sent to him by Anastasia Hartwell.",al={"who is josef","who makes the robe","josef gregorian undercity"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The interaction takes place in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, at Josef Gregorian's tailor shop.",al={"spellfire robes location","where to turn in spellfire robes"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why don't you have to leave to do another task for this quest?",a="You gathered the materials in the preceding assignment, Gathering Materials. Hand the reagents to Josef, and he weaves the garment and gives you the finished robes.",al={"why is it instant","how to complete spellfire robes","auto complete robe"},gp=true},{q="Can classes other than Mages obtain these robes?",a="No. The chain and its enchanted robes are for mages allied with the Horde.",al={"is this mage only","can warlock get this","who can do spellfire robes"},gp=true},{q="What materials were required to make these robes?",a="The robes use rare supplies gathered earlier, including linen cloth and Dalaran mana gems taken from the Kirin Tor mages of Silverpine Forest.",al={"what goes into the robe","robe ingredients","gathering materials turn in"},it="item"},{q="Why does Josef Gregorian tailor the Spellfire Robes for you?",a="Josef Gregorian serves as a mentor to rising Forsaken and Horde mages within the Magic Quarter. By weaving the gathered reagents into suitable enchanted vestments, he ensures you are properly outfitted to channel and endure the arcane forces demanded of your growing craft.",al={"why does josef make the robes","josef gregorian motive","why does josef help you"},it="motive",add="c778cc7d"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Horde mage, you receive these robes as an early rite of passage. Their tailored cloth can handle volatile fire and arcane energies.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken spellcaster in the Undercity, you preserve Dalaran-style arcane discipline, joining old magical traditions with your new existence in Lordaeron's ruins.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can see how mundane cloth is strengthened to withstand powerful magical currents with exotic reagents."},kw={"arcane robes","gathering materials","josef gregorian","mage quest","magic quarter","spellfire robes","undercity"},rel={"quest:1961","npc:josef-gregorian"},m={start="Josef Gregorian",level="15",faction="Horde",id=1962},src={"Spellfire Robes"}}
E["quest:1978"] = {t="quest",n="The Deathstalkers",z="undercity",s="In Undercity, the Deathstalkers bring a new operative into their ranks. You carry Andron's Ledger to Varimathras, proof of the Syndicate's covert activities.",h="In Undercity, the Deathstalkers bring a new operative into their ranks.",sec={{t="Induction into the Shadows",b="Mennet Carkad welcomes you into the Deathstalkers after you uncover records from Andron Gant. The order serves Lady Sylvanas as eyes, ears, and daggers throughout Lordaeron. Its agents use intelligence networks, ruthless efficiency, and stealth to remove threats before they surface. Recognition by the order marks a step into service for the Forsaken.",sp=0},{t="The Syndicate Connection",b="Andron's Ledger reveals illicit ties between local agents and the Syndicate. Once the noble aristocracy of Alterac, the Syndicate turned to banditry and subversion after its realm fell in the Second War. Carkad is surprised and disdainful that Alterac's fallen lords have sunk to petty conspiracies to claw back power.",sp=1},{t="Audience with the Dreadlord",b="You deliver the sensitive ledger directly to Varimathras in the Royal Quarter of Undercity. The nathrezim commander oversees Forsaken tactical intelligence under Sylvanas Windrunner. Pleased by the Deathstalkers' initiative, Varimathras welcomes your demonstrated ability and says his intelligence division can use someone who delivers results.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the Forsaken's order of spies, scouts, and assassins, based in the Rogues' Quarter of Undercity. They work across Lordaeron to neutralize political rivals, infiltrate hostile factions, and guard the Forsaken realm against threats from outside and subversion within.",al={"who are the deathstalkers","deathstalker lore","forsaken assassins"},it="people"},{q="Why is the Syndicate involved?",a="Andron's Ledger reveals secret ties to the Syndicate, Alterac's displaced aristocracy, now given to organized banditry. The Forsaken watch Alterac's remnants in their territory, where Syndicate agents seek chances to reclaim lost land and plunder resources across northern Lordaeron.",al={"why syndicate","alterac connection","syndicate ledger"},it="conflict"},{q="Why report directly to Varimathras?",a="Varimathras advises Queen Sylvanas on tactics and oversees Undercity security and intelligence. Discoveries about foreign plots, including the Syndicate's covert work, go to him for review and broader military and diplomatic measures.",al={"why varimathras","who is varimathras","dreadlord role"},it="purpose"},{q="Who was Mennet Carkad?",a="Mennet Carkad is a senior handler and contact for the Deathstalkers in Undercity. He oversees field agents, evaluates recruits, and sifts through intelligence before sending critical findings up the chain of command.",al={"mennet carkad role","quest giver carkad"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this audience take place?",a="The audience takes place in the Hall of the Dark Lady, in Undercity's Royal Quarter. Varimathras stands beside Queen Sylvanas Windrunner at the heart of the Forsaken seat of power.",al={"where is varimathras","hall of the dark lady location"},it="place"},{q="What happens after joining the Deathstalkers?",a="With your credentials established and your reliability proven to Mennet Carkad and Varimathras, you are recognized as a trusted field operative for the Forsaken. Future reconnaissance and elimination contracts may take you across Lordaeron's contested lands.",al={"deathstalker questline continuation","what next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad want Andron's Ledger delivered to Varimathras?",a="The ledger exposes that the Syndicate—the fallen nobles of Alterac—is conspiring against the Forsaken. Uncovering their treachery is a vital intelligence victory for the Deathstalkers, and Mennet knows such urgent news concerning Lordaeron's security must be placed directly into the hands of Lord Varimathras, who oversees the order's operations.",al={"why deliver the ledger","mennet carkad motive","why report the syndicate to varimathras"},it="motive",add="123798f3"},{q="Why does Mennet send you instead of reporting to Varimathras himself?",a="You were the one who tracked down the conspirators and secured Andron's ledger in the field. Mennet believes it is only fitting that you present the intelligence yourself, allowing you to claim credit before Lord Varimathras and mark your formal induction into the ranks of the Deathstalkers.",al={"why me deathstalkers","why does mennet send me","why deliver ledger yourself"},it="why_me",add="b0e675df"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you pledge to guard Lordaeron's fragile sovereignty from human survivors and lurking traitors.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you enter the Forsaken's dedicated cadre and become a state intelligence operative rather than a simple cutpurse.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help protect northern territories from sabotage by monitoring the human remnants of Alterac."},kw={"alterac","andron's ledger","deathstalkers","hall of the dark lady","mennet carkad","syndicate","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1886","quest:1885","npc:varimathras","zone:undercity","topic:syndicate","topic:alterac-kingdom"},m={start="Mennet Carkad",["end"]="Varimathras",level="13",faction="Horde",id=1978},src={"The Deathstalkers (4)"}}
E["quest:1998"] = {t="quest",n="Fenwick Thatros",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Mennet Carkad sends promising rogues after Fenwick Thatros on Lord Varimathras's orders. Thatros is suspected of organizing independent undead forces along Silverpine Forest's shores. Killing him proves an operative's mettle to the Deathstalkers and opens the way to advanced trade training.",h="In the Undercity, Mennet Carkad sends promising rogues after Fenwick Thatros on Lord Varimathras's orders.",sec={{t="A Command from the Dreadlord",b="In the Undercity's Rogues' Quarter, Mennet Carkad handles Deathstalker contracts and training. The Deathstalkers are the Forsaken's secretive intelligence wing. Lord Varimathras has named Fenwick Thatros as a priority target, a charge too serious for novice recruits. Thatros has established a foothold among rogue undead in Silverpine Forest. If left alone, their independent leadership could threaten Forsaken control across Lordaeron's old holdings.",sp=0},{t="The Decrepit Dock on Lordamere",b="Deathstalker scouts report Fenwick Thatros near a decrepit dock on Lake Lordamere in Silverpine Forest. Reaching him means crossing wilderness claimed by feral beasts, Rot Hide gnolls, and Scourge remnants. Varimathras demands proof of the kill: Thatros's severed head. Bringing it back can earn an operative entry into deeper covert operations.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fenwick Thatros?",a="Fenwick Thatros leads undead near Lake Lordamere in Silverpine Forest. He commands pockets of undead who are unaligned with or hostile to the Undercity, unlike Forsaken who serve Lady Sylvanas. Lord Varimathras has marked him for execution.",al={"fenwick lore","who is thatros","fenwick thatros background"},it="target"},{q="Why does Varimathras want Fenwick Thatros dead?",a="Varimathras wants Fenwick Thatros dead because he could rally stray undead in Silverpine against the Forsaken. Rival leaders who threaten Sylvanas's control over the region must be eliminated to secure the Undercity's borders.",al={"varimathras thatros","why kill fenwick"},it="motive"},{q="Who are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the Forsaken's espionage, assassination, and reconnaissance agency. Based in the Undercity's Rogues' Quarter, they work across Lordaeron to remove internal threats, spy on rival factions, and secure territory for the Dark Lady.",al={"deathstalkers lore","what are deathstalkers","undead rogues faction"},it="people"},{q="Where is Fenwick Thatros located?",a="Deathstalker reports place Fenwick Thatros near a ruined dock on Lake Lordamere's shore in northeastern Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is fenwick","fenwick dock location","thatros lake lordamere"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does completing this mission earn with the Deathstalkers?",a="Killing Fenwick Thatros proves an operative's capability and loyalty to Mennet Carkad and the Deathstalkers. Once you have shown your reliability, Carkad offers specialized training in the shadow arts.",al={"fenwick reward lore","what comes after fenwick"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Mennet Carkad?",a="Mennet Carkad trains rogues and handles the Deathstalkers in the Undercity's Rogues' Quarter. He oversees field agents and assigns work tied to the Forsaken realm's security.",al={"mennet carkad","who gives fenwick quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad need Fenwick's Head?",a="Fenwick Thatros represents an organized threat lurking right along the borders of Silverpine Forest. Mennet Carkad demands his severed head as undeniable proof that the rogue undead commander has been eliminated. In the clandestine operations of the Deathstalkers and Lord Varimathras, an assassin's word is never enough without physical trophy to confirm the kill.",al={"what is fenwick's head for","why take fenwick's head","fenwicks head purpose"},it="item",add="eac48585"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad choose you for this mission?",a="Mennet Carkad operates as a handler and trainer for Deathstalkers in the Rogues' Quarter. When Lord Varimathras orders a surgical assassination, ordinary city guards are ill-suited for stealthy outdoor reconnaissance. Mennet specifically selects you because you have shown promise in the shadow arts, using this critical contract to evaluate whether you are ready for advanced training among the Forsaken's elite operatives.",al={"why send me","why does mennet pick me","why not send deathstalker guards"},it="why_me",add="bc8ca6fa"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you prove your stealth and lethality through this contract before the Deathstalkers trust you with deeper tools of their trade.",["race:Undead"]="As one of the Forsaken, you know rival undead factions cannot claim sovereignty so close to the Capital City. Fenwick Thatros's head is a political necessity."},kw={"deathstalkers","fenwick thatros","lake lordamere","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","silverpine forest","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1999","npc:varimathras","quest:1886","quest:1885","subzone:rogues-quarter","zone:undercity","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Mennet Carkad",level="16",faction="Horde",id=1998,ri={"Fenwick's Head"}},src={"Fenwick Thatros (quest)"}}
E["quest:1999"] = {t="quest",n="Tools of the Trade",z="undercity",s="Horde rogues are sent from the Undercity to steal a report from Ambermill. Lord Varimathras orders them to obtain lockpicking tools and recover Kirin Tor intelligence on Dalaran’s condition.",h="Horde rogues are sent from the Undercity to steal a report from Ambermill.",sec={{t="Eyes on Ambermill",b="A prisoner’s interrogation points the Deathstalkers toward intelligence hidden in Ambermill. Silverpine Forest remains a precarious front line, and human mages guard the village’s communications fiercely. Lord Varimathras orders Deathstalker handler Mennet Carkad to direct promising operatives around the Kirin Tor sentries and recover the Dalaran Status Report.",sp=0},{t="The Art of the Breach",b="Infiltration and lockpicking test skills beyond assassination. Before entering Kirin Tor territory, operatives receive specialized thieves’ tools from Estelle Gendry. Opening the secured chest in Ambermill proves an operative can move beyond street brutality and become an espionage asset for the Forsaken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders this mission?",a="Mennet Carkad, a Deathstalker rogue in the Undercity’s Rogues' Quarter, assigns the work. Lord Varimathras gives the order and oversees Forsaken intelligence gathering.",al={"who gives tools of the trade","quest giver","mennet carkad quest"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Dalaran Status Report?",a="The Dalaran Status Report is a sealed Kirin Tor dispatch about conditions in Dalaran. Deathstalker interrogators learned its location from a prisoner, revealing that vital information about the Forsaken’s southern neighbors was vulnerable.",al={"what are the documents","kirin tor papers","status report"},it="item"},{q="Where is the report kept?",a="The report is inside a locked chest at the Kirin Tor outpost of Ambermill in southern Silverpine Forest.",al={"where do i find the documents","ambermill chest location","where is the status report"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who provides the lockpicking tools?",a="Estelle Gendry, an outfitter in the Undercity’s Rogues' Quarter, provides the thieves’ tools needed to open the locked chest.",al={"where do i get tools","estelle gendry role","outfitter tools"},gp=true},{q="Why is Dalaran important to the Forsaken right now?",a="Dalaran’s surviving wizards are rebuilding their city across Lordamere Lake from Silverpine Forest. The Forsaken monitor the Kirin Tor to protect their holdings in Lordaeron.",al={"why care about dalaran","forsaken vs dalaran","kirin tor threat"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What prerequisite must be completed before taking this mission?",a="Operatives must first complete the assassination contract Fenwick Thatros, hunting a target in Silverpine Forest before Mennet Carkad trusts them with delicate infiltration work.",al={"prereq","what quest comes before","fenwick thatros quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad want this done?",a="Lord Varimathras tasked the Deathstalkers with retrieving the report after extracting its whereabouts from a prisoner. As an operative within the Rogues' Quarter, Mennet Carkad carries out the dreadlord's directives while simultaneously testing your burgeoning skills in infiltration and espionage.",al={"why does mennet carkad want this","mennet carkad motive","why recover dalaran status report"},it="motive",add="77cf7ea8"},{q="Who are you sent against at Ambermill?",a="Your target is the Kirin Tor stationed at Ambermill in Silverpine Forest. These human wizards maintain an enclave near the rebuilding city of Dalaran, guarding confidential intelligence about the broken city's current condition from the Forsaken.",al={"who holds the report","tools of the trade target","who are you targeting"},it="target",add="9b719de0"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad need you for this mission?",a="The mission serves as a rite of passage. After demonstrating basic aptitude by eliminating Fenwick Thatros, Mennet selected you to prove you can handle the Deathstalkers' more delicate tradecraft—relying on stealth, lockpicking, and infiltration rather than brute force.",al={"why send me","why me mennet carkad","why cant deathstalkers get the report"},it="why_me",add="6507a470"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Horde rogue, you prove your worth with formal lockpicking tools, stealth, and finesse instead of brute force.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you help the Forsaken outwit the Kirin Tor mages who seek to reclaim Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure human intelligence in Silverpine and strengthen the Horde’s foothold across northern Lordaeron against Alliance remnants."},kw={"ambermill","dalaran","deathstalkers","estelle gendry","kirin tor","lockpicking","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1998","quest:1886","subzone:rogues-quarter","zone:undercity","subzone:ambermill","npc:varimathras","subzone:dalaran"},m={start="Mennet Carkad",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1999,ri={"Dalaran Status Report"}},src={"Tools of the Trade (Classic)"}}
E["quest:357"] = {t="quest",n="The Lich's Identity",z="undercity",s="Bethor Iceshard seeks to learn who lives alone on Brightwater Lake. He sends an emissary to steal the recluse's spellbook and judge his power and allegiance.",h="Bethor Iceshard seeks to learn who lives alone on Brightwater Lake.",sec={{t="A Recluse on the Lake",b="A lone lich lives in exile on a small island in Brightwater Lake, north of the Undercity. He has free will, unlike the Lich King's mindless pawns, but paranoia rules his life. He believes any undead who approach are Scourge thralls sent to drag him back into servitude. So he unleashes summoned minions on anyone who sets foot on his shore.",sp=0},{t="A Valuable Asset",b="Word of the rogue lich reaches Bethor Iceshard, the archmage who oversees the Undercity's mages. Bethor knows Lady Sylvanas Windrunner seeks every scrap of magical mastery and every capable will to strengthen the Forsaken against their many foes. To judge whether the hermit can be recruited, Bethor needs proof of his identity and necromantic skill.",sp=0},{t="An Old Friend Found",b="When the stolen spellbook reaches the Magic Quarter, Bethor studies its arcane script and learns the lich's identity: Gunther Arcanus. Before the plague ravaged Lordaeron, Gunther was a talented necromancer and Bethor's close comrade. His independent will and greater necromantic power could aid the Dark Lady's realm.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you on this mission?",a="Bethor Iceshard, a powerful Forsaken mage in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, sends you.",al={"quest giver","bethor iceshard location","who gives the lichs identity"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the lich attack anyone who approaches him?",a="The lich freed himself from the Lich King's control, but wrongly believes every other undead in Lordaeron remains a mind-controlled Scourge thrall. He orders his minions to attack anyone approaching his island to protect his freedom.",al={"why is gunther hostile","why does the lich attack","brightwater lich hostile"},it="hostile"},{q="Where is the lich's camp located?",a="The lich lives on an island in Brightwater Lake, in Tirisfal Glades directly north of the Ruins of Lordaeron and Undercity.",al={"where is the lich","brightwater lake island","gunther arcanus location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Lady Sylvanas want him brought into the Forsaken?",a="Lady Sylvanas seeks rare, independent undead with great magical skill. A free-willed necromancer wielding potent death magic could help the Forsaken fight the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"why recruit the lich","forsaken interest in gunther","sylvanas lich"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who does the lich turn out to be?",a="Bethor reveals that the lich is Gunther Arcanus, a former Dalaran mage and skilled necromancer who was Bethor's close comrade-in-arms before the Third War.",al={"lich identity","who is the lich","identity of the lich"},sp=1,it="origin"},{q="What happens after you deliver the spellbook?",a="After confirming Gunther's identity, Bethor sends you back to Brightwater Lake with the spellbook. You are to convince Gunther that the Forsaken are free and want to welcome him.",al={"what next","return the book quest","after the lichs identity"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard want the lich's spellbook?",a="Bethor Iceshard seeks to bring the reclusive undead mage into the Forsaken fold on behalf of the Dark Lady. Because the lich violently drives off anyone who approaches, Bethor cannot simply talk to him. He needs to inspect the spellbook to uncover the caster's true identity, gauge the extent of his necromantic power, and determine whether his talents can truly serve the Forsaken cause.",al={"bethor motive","why does bethor want the book","why steal the lich spellbook"},it="motive",add="2f6ced1e"},{q="What is the Lich's Spellbook for?",a="The spellbook belongs to the reclusive lich living on Brightwater Lake. It contains his necromantic arcana and personal magical signatures. Bethor Iceshard uses it to identify the hermit and assess his necromantic prowess without needing to engage him in direct conversation.",al={"lich's spellbook","lich spellbook purpose","what is the spellbook for"},it="item",add="f276cf7d"},{q="Who is the lich on Brightwater Lake?",a="The target is a powerful, free-willed undead mage dwelling on an island in Brightwater Lake to the north. Mistrustful of everyone, he believes all other undead are still mindless slaves of the Scourge. Consequently, he has surrounded himself with summoned minions and violently repels any who draw near.",al={"who is the lich","brightwater lake lich","who do i steal the book from"},it="target",add="e5299862"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you know that freeing independent undead proves your break from the Lich King's control was no isolated miracle. Their necromantic power can also strengthen Sylvanas's court.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you see Bethor Iceshard in the Magic Quarter carry on Lordaeron's and Dalaran's magical traditions in service of Forsaken survival.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know powerful necromancers can strengthen its northern frontier against the Scarlet Crusade and the Scourge."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brightwater lake","forsaken","magic quarter","necromancer","sylvanas","the lich's spellbook","undercity"},rel={"npc:bethor-iceshard","npc:gunther-arcanus","quest:405","quest:366","subzone:brightwater-lake","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},m={start="Bethor Iceshard",level="8",faction="Horde",id=357,ri={"The Lich's Spellbook"}},src={"The Lich's Identity"}}
E["quest:405"] = {t="quest",n="The Prodigal Lich",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Bethor Iceshard needs an agent for a mission involving a wayward lich. After your work in Brill against Scourge remnants and Rot Hide gnolls, Magistrate Sevren sends you south with orders.",h="In the Undercity, Bethor Iceshard needs an agent for a mission involving a wayward lich.",sec={{t="Summons to the Capital",b="Magistrate Sevren judges you worthy of greater Forsaken work after your service in Brill. He sends you to Bethor Iceshard, a formidable mage in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, who wants an agent tested against the Scourge. Sevren gives you official orders to carry beneath the ruins of Lordaeron, into the corridors of the Forsaken capital.",sp=0},{t="A Wayward Lich",b="Magistrate Sevren does not know the exact details, but the orders concern finding and recruiting a rogue lich. Liches are among the Scourge's deadliest spellcasters, and dealing with one is perilous. You bring the orders to Bethor atop his arcane sanctum. The icy mage gets straight to business, ready to see whether Brill's magistrate has sent someone strong enough to track such dangerous quarry.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this task?",a="Magistrate Sevren, the Forsaken official who administers Brill in Tirisfal Glades, sends you to Bethor Iceshard with written orders.",al={"who gives the prodigal lich","quest giver prodigal lich","sevren orders"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Bethor Iceshard?",a="Bethor Iceshard resides in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, atop the central elevated structure surrounded by arcane energies.",al={"where is bethor","bethor iceshard location","how to find bethor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the mission mentioned in the orders?",a="Bethor intends to enlist a wandering, rogue lich. First, he needs an agent able to follow clues to the lich's identity and whereabouts.",al={"what is the lich mission","who is the wayward lich","prodigal lich purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Bethor require an agent tested against the Scourge?",a="Liches master necromantic frost and death magic, and were originally bound to the Lich King. Facing a free-willed or isolated lich calls for someone who has proved able to survive Scourge undead.",al={"why scourge testing","why does bethor need me"},it="motive"},{q="What prerequisite must be completed before receiving this quest?",a="Before receiving these orders, you must complete Magistrate Sevren's earlier assignment, 'Graverobbers', clearing Rot Hide gnolls and grave thieves from Garren's Haunt.",al={"prodigal lich prequest","how to unlock prodigal lich"},gp=true},{q="What comes after reporting to Bethor?",a="After you deliver Sevren's orders, Bethor offers 'The Lich's Identity'. He sends you to investigate artifacts and clues that may reveal who the mysterious being was in life.",al={"what is next after prodigal lich","prodigal lich follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Magistrate Sevren want this done?",a="Magistrate Sevren is acting on direct orders from Bethor Iceshard, a formidable mage dwelling in the Undercity. Bethor specifically requested a capable operative with proven experience fighting the Scourge to handle a delicate and perilous matter regarding a wayward lich. As the civic authority in Brill, Sevren ensures Undercity's commands are fulfilled promptly by sending his most capable champion.",al={"why sevren orders","sevren motive","why send me to bethor"},it="motive",add="a06b4328"},{q="Why does Magistrate Sevren choose you for this mission?",a="Bethor Iceshard explicitly demanded an agent who has already proven their worth and mettle against the Scourge. Rather than dispatching standard town guards or untested recruits, Sevren selected you because your recent actions around Brill demonstrated that you have both the resilience and the capability to survive whatever dangerous assignment Bethor has planned.",al={"why me prodigal lich","why sevren picks me","why not royal guard"},it="why_me",add="41da8612"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, your first direct orders from the capital take you from local militia work in Brill to carrying out the Undercity's wider aims.",["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you report to Bethor Iceshard, one of the Forsaken's most powerful arcane and frost masters.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, securing unaligned or powerful necromantic assets strengthens the Forsaken's precarious hold on Lordaeron's ruins against common enemies."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brill","magic quarter","magistrate sevren","prodigal lich","sevren's orders","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"npc:bethor-iceshard","npc:magistrate-sevren","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:357","quest:358","topic:scourge"},m={start="Magistrate Sevren",["end"]="Bethor Iceshard",level="8",faction="Horde",id=405},src={"The Prodigal Lich"}}
E["quest:411"] = {t="quest",n="The Prodigal Lich Returns",z="undercity",s="You carry an arcane communion gem to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity, after winning Gunther Arcanus's trust and restoring his grimoire.",h="You carry an arcane communion gem to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity, after winning Gunther Arcanus's trust...",sec={{t="A Rare Reconciliation",b="Gunther Arcanus spent years alone on an island in Brightwater Lake. By sheer force of will, he broke free from the Lich King's control, unaware that Sylvanas Windrunner had liberated Lordaeron. Bitter and wary of outsiders, he distrusted the Undercity's emissaries. An adventurer returned his spellbook and showed him their hostility toward the Scourge. Satisfied the visitor was no enemy, Gunther entrusted them with a Nether Gem to contact his former colleague.",sp=0},{t="Communion in the Magic Quarter",b="You return to the Undercity's Magic Quarter and deliver the Nether Gem to Bethor Iceshard. Bethor channels its power and conjures Gunther's ethereal visage in the sanctuary. Through their magical communion, Gunther formally agrees to ally with the Forsaken cause. Gaining a necromancer of his independent mastery bolsters the Dark Lady's young kingdom and its magical defenses against the Scourge and the living.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gunther Arcanus?",a="Gunther Arcanus is a powerful necromancer who broke free of the Lich King's mental domination by himself. He lived in reclusive exile on an island in Brightwater Lake, believing all other undead were mindless thralls until adventurers proved otherwise.",al={"gunther arcanus lore","who is the prodigal lich","gunther undercity"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Bethor Iceshard?",a="Bethor Iceshard is a senior mage and scholar who lives in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. An old colleague of Gunther Arcanus, he coordinated the effort to find and recruit him into the Forsaken.",al={"bethor lore","who is bethor","iceshard undercity"},it="identity"},{q="What does the Nether Gem do?",a="Gunther Arcanus gave Bethor Iceshard the Nether Gem, an enchanted artifact. When Bethor channels arcane power into it, the gem manifests a spectral image of Gunther so the spellcasters can speak across great distances.",al={"what is the nether gem","gunther gem"},it="item"},{q="Why does Gunther agree to join the Forsaken?",a="Gunther spent years fearing he was Lordaeron's only free-willed undead. Convinced that Sylvanas's Forsaken are free of the Scourge and fight the Lich King, he willingly pledges allegiance and renews ties with his former peers.",al={"why join forsaken","gunther allegiance"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="Why does the quest call Gunther a 'Lich'?",a="Gunther looks like any Forsaken, rather than a floating, frost-wreathed Scourge lich, yet the Forsaken call him one. A Kirin Tor student and skilled necromancer in life, he was raised by the plague during the Third War and later broke the Lich King's hold by himself.",al={"is gunther a real lich","gunther lich form"},it="name"},{q="What happens when you turn in the Nether Gem?",a="When you deliver the Nether Gem, Bethor activates it and conjures Gunther's Visage in the Magic Quarter. The projection moves toward Bethor to begin their long-awaited reunion, then fades.",al={"nether gem turn in event","what happens at bethor"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gunther Arcanus need you to deliver the Nether Gem?",a="Gunther Arcanus remains isolated on his island in Brightwater Lake, maintaining his cautious seclusion while he re-establishes contact with the world beyond. As an emissary who proved your loyalty by recovering his spellbook and destroying his necromantic enemies, you have earned his trust. Handing you the Nether Gem allows him to reach out to his old comrade Bethor Iceshard and negotiate his allegiance without having to abandon his sanctuary or march straight into the Undercity.",al={"why send player nether gem","why does gunther need me","why deliver the gem"},it="why_me",add="5e5e694d"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Gunther's freedom without the Banshee Queen's help shows the willpower Lordaeron's fallen can muster.",["class:Mage"]="Bethor's communion with Gunther joins traditional Dalaran spellcraft with the dark necromancy practiced in the Undercity's Magic Quarter.",["faction:Horde"]="Recruiting an independent master necromancer like Gunther strengthens the Horde's magical standing in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"arcanus","bethor","brightwater lake","gunther","iceshard","lich","nether gem","prodigal","undercity"},rel={"npc:gunther-arcanus","npc:bethor-iceshard","quest:409","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Gunther Arcanus",["end"]="Bethor Iceshard",level="12",faction="Horde",id=411},src={"The Prodigal Lich Returns"}}
E["quest:441"] = {t="quest",n="Raleigh and the Undercity",z="undercity",s="In Brill and the Undercity, a ring draws Raleigh into an old tragedy. Magistrate Sevren sends you to return Deliah's ring to her widowed husband, found after her stolen corpse was bound for Fenris Isle.",h="In Brill and the Undercity, a ring draws Raleigh into an old tragedy.",sec={{t="A Tragic Heirloom",b="In Brill, Magistrate Sevren has pieced together clues about a stolen corpse and an engraved ring. The ring belonged to Deliah, and Sevren hopes to learn where it came from and return it to her family. He sends you into the Undercity to find Raleigh, Deliah's surviving husband.",sp=0},{t="Cold Hearts, Bitter Vengeance",b="In the Trade Quarter of the Undercity, Raleigh Andrean recognizes his former wife's ring at once. Like many of the Forsaken, undeath has left him unable to grieve Deliah's death or the desecration of her remains. Yet a thirst for retribution still burns in him. Raleigh plots revenge against those who violated her final rest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Magistrate Sevren sends you from Brill in Tirisfal Glades after you return Deliah's Ring to him.",al={"where do i get raleigh and the undercity","quest giver","magistrate sevren quest"},gp=true},{q="Where is Raleigh Andrean located?",a="Raleigh Andrean is in the Undercity's Trade Quarter, among its merchants and craftsmen.",al={"raleigh location","where is raleigh","trade quarter raleigh"},gp=true},{q="Whose ring is being delivered?",a="The ring belonged to Deliah, a woman from Brill who was Raleigh Andrean's wife before Lordaeron fell.",al={"deliah ring","who was deliah","whose ring is this"},it="item"},{q="Why doesn't Raleigh mourn his dead wife?",a="As one of the Forsaken, Raleigh says that grief and love have grown cold within his undead heart. Vengeance is what remains.",al={"raleigh reaction","does raleigh care","why is raleigh cold"}},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="When you hand over the ring, Raleigh sends you to avenge his wife's desecration.",al={"next quest","follow up to raleigh","what comes after"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="How was Deliah's ring found initially?",a="Deliah's ring was taken from her hand among the wrapped corpses on a boat at the Decrepit Ferry in Silverpine Forest.",al={"ring origin","where did the ring come from"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Magistrate Sevren want Deliah's ring brought to Raleigh?",a="When the engraved ring was recovered, Magistrate Sevren recalled that a woman named Deliah once lived in Brill with her husband, Raleigh. Raleigh now resides among the Forsaken in the Undercity. Sevren sends you to deliver the keepsake so Raleigh can confirm whether the heirloom truly belonged to his former wife, bringing closure or clarity to the fate of his lost family.",al={"why send ring to raleigh","magistrate sevren motive","why deliver deliah ring"},it="motive",add="a3ed960c"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, Raleigh's cold response reflects the Forsaken's shared anguish. Their mortal attachments have faded into bitter wrath.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you carry tokens of old Lordaeron through the gates of the Undercity. They show the somber shape of life among your Forsaken allies."},kw={"a husband's revenge","brill","deliah","deliah's ring","raleigh","sevren","trade quarter","undercity"},rel={"quest:440","quest:530","npc:raleigh-andrean","npc:magistrate-sevren","zone:undercity","subzone:trade-quarter","subzone:brill"},m={start="Magistrate Sevren",["end"]="Raleigh Andrean",level="16",faction="Horde",id=441},src={"Raleigh and the Undercity"}}
E["quest:444"] = {t="quest",n="Rot Hide Origins",z="undercity",s="In Silverpine Forest, the Rot Hides carry a magic Renferrel cannot explain by alchemy alone. He sends a sample to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity, where arcane knowledge may reveal its origin.",h="In Silverpine Forest, the Rot Hides carry a magic Renferrel cannot explain by alchemy alone.",sec={{t="A Concoction of Death and Fel",b="Apothecary Renferrel has reduced fluid from the Rot Hides of Silverpine Forest to its basic elements. His first tests show the ichor bears both necromancy and warlock magic. Alchemy cannot explain the sorcery behind it, so he prepares a sample for an expert in the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="Audience with the Mage",b="Bethor Iceshard, a Forsaken mage in the Undercity’s Magic Quarter, studies the sample. He is not part of the Royal Apothecary Society, but knows arcane and dark arts. The vial holds old, potent enchantments he has not seen in years. Bethor begins a divination to learn who wove the magic.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends the player on this quest?",a="Apothecary Renferrel of the Royal Apothecary Society sends you from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He examined ichor taken from nearby Rot Hides.",al={"who starts rot hide origins","where do i get rot hide origins"},gp=true},{q="Why does Renferrel send the sample to Bethor Iceshard?",a="Renferrel finds necromantic and warlock magic in the Rot Hide ichor. Since alchemy cannot explain the enchantments, he sends the sample to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity for arcane study.",al={"why bethor iceshard","why give sample to mage"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Bethor Iceshard located?",a="Bethor Iceshard lives in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, among arcane researchers and trainers.",al={"bethor location","where is bethor iceshard"},gp=true},{q="What are the Rot Hides?",a="Rot Hides are undead gnolls prowling Silverpine Forest. Their rotting condition comes from foul magical experiments.",al={"what are rot hides","rot hide gnolls silverpine"}},{q="What happens when you deliver the sample to Bethor?",a="Bethor recognizes old, potent magic in the fluid, spells he has not encountered in a very long time. He begins a divination to trace its source.",al={"what does bethor do","bethor iceshard reaction"}},{q="What quest comes next?",a="After Bethor's divination, he sends you to investigate the renegade mage corrupting the gnolls in Thule Ravenclaw.",al={"next quest after rot hide origins","follow up to rot hide origins"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you see the Royal Apothecary Society and the arcane masters of the Undercity work together, joining science and sorcery to protect Lordaeron.",["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you know arcane divination and learned spellcraft can uncover dark mysteries beyond ordinary alchemy.",["class:Warlock"]="As a Warlock, you recognize fel and warlock magic mingled with necromancy in the Rot Hide ichor. Such forbidden spellcraft is at work in the Silverpine wilderness."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","bethor iceshard","magic quarter","rot hide ichor","rot hide origins","sample ichor","silverpine forest","undercity"},rel={"npc:bethor-iceshard","npc:apothecary-renferrel","zone:undercity","subzone:magic-quarter"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="Bethor Iceshard",level="17",faction="Horde",id=444},src={"Rot Hide Origins"}}
E["quest:447"] = {t="quest",n="A Recipe For Death",z="undercity",s="In Silverpine, A Recipe For Death gathers reagents for the Forsaken's New Plague. Apothecary Renferrel sends bear hearts and spider blood from the Sepulcher to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",h="In Silverpine, A Recipe For Death gathers reagents for the Forsaken's New Plague.",sec={{t="A Weapon Against Two Foes",b="In Silverpine Forest, Apothecary Renferrel sees the danger facing Sylvanas's people. Arthas's legions press them, and remnants of humanity remain their foes. Conventional warfare offers little hope. The Forsaken seek a New Plague that can rot living humans and undead Scourge alike. Renferrel's field research found that arachnid venom from the Skittering Dark, joined with toxins in the hearts of native bears, makes a virulent foundation.",sp=0},{t="Dispatch to the Apothecarium",b="The collected organs and blood from Silverpine's wilderness go beneath the ruins of Lordaeron, to the Apothecarium in the Undercity. Master Apothecary Faranell oversees the Royal Apothecary Society's design. He takes Renferrel's samples to test their contaminable properties and refine formulas that may secure Forsaken supremacy across the continent.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of collecting bear hearts and spider blood?",a="Renferrel found that spider blood from the Skittering Dark reacts lethally with toxins in grizzly bear hearts. Together, they give the Royal Apothecary Society raw materials to test and develop the New Plague.",al={"why bear hearts","why spider blood","what is this recipe for"},it="item"},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell heads the Royal Apothecary Society in the Apothecarium quarter of the Undercity. He oversees research into the New Plague on behalf of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"faranell lore","who is faranell","master apothecary"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the Forsaken want to create a New Plague?",a="The Forsaken face the Scourge and the hatred of living humans, with too few soldiers for a long conventional war. Their New Plague is meant to kill both living foes and undead Scourge, securing Forsaken survival and autonomy.",al={"why make new plague","forsaken plague motivation","new plague lore"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Apothecary Renferrel located?",a="Apothecary Renferrel conducts his research from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",al={"renferrel location","where is renferrel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where is the Skittering Dark?",a="The Skittering Dark lies northwest of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Giant spiders infest this wilderness, and Renferrel needs their blood.",al={"skittering dark location","where to find spiders silverpine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does this quest continue further?",a="Yes. Master Apothecary Faranell uses the reagents in further experiments, followed by work in the Apothecarium to refine and test the lethal mixture.",al={"recipe for death follow up","is there a part 2"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel want you to gather these reagents?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is dedicated to the Royal Apothecary Society's grand goal of crafting a New Plague. Facing the overwhelming armies of the Scourge and lingering human enclaves, Renferrel believes conventional warfare cannot secure the Forsaken's survival. He seeks to provide Master Apothecary Faranell with viable biological ingredients to brew a blight capable of obliterating both undead and living enemies alike.",al={"why does renferrel need this","renferrel motive","why help apothecary renferrel"},it="motive",add="dca2eeef"},{q="Who are you sent against to collect the ingredients?",a="You are sent into the wilds of Silverpine Forest to hunt grizzled bears and the venomous arachnids infesting the Skittering Dark. These untamed beasts roam the ancient pine woods, thriving amid the creeping blighted decay, and their venom and resilient organs provide the potent natural toxins the Royal Apothecary Society requires.",al={"recipe for death targets","what do i kill recipe for death","who do i fight recipe for death"},it="target",add="922f4213"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you can help the Apothecary Society develop its plague to defend the Forsaken realm against the Scourge and humanity.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see Forsaken apothecaries pursue victory with virulent concoctions, a grim way of war among the Horde's newest allies."},kw={"faranell","new plague","renferrel","royal apothecary society","silverpine","skittering dark","undercity"},rel={"npc:apothecary-renferrel","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","topic:royal-apothecary-society","quest:367","subzone:skittering-dark","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity","topic:scourge"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="Master Apothecary Faranell",level="12",faction="Horde",id=447,ri={"Grizzled Bear Heart","Skittering Blood"}},src={"A Recipe For Death"}}
E["quest:450"] = {t="quest",n="A Recipe For Death",z="undercity",s="From the Undercity, Master Apothecary Faranell sends you to Pyrewood Village in A Recipe For Death. You seek Apothecary Berard's notes on the ancient blight that wiped out Lake Lordamere's aquatic life.",h="From the Undercity, Master Apothecary Faranell sends you to Pyrewood Village in A Recipe For Death.",sec={{t="A Mind Lost to Shadow",b="Apothecary Berard once stood among the Royal Apothecary Society's most promising researchers. He worked in Pyrewood Village, studying past ecological disasters for the Forsaken's alchemical pursuits. Then Archmage Arugal unleashed shadow magic across Silverpine Forest, and Berard fell under its curse. His mind gave way, binding him as a servant to the mage.",sp=0},{t="The Secrets of Lake Lordamere",b="Master Apothecary Faranell considers Apothecary Berard beyond saving, but the Royal Apothecary Society still needs his research. Berard recorded the traits of a forgotten plague that wiped out all aquatic life in Lake Lordamere long ago. His journal lies in the Pyrewood Village Inn. You are to recover it and take it to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher, so the Society can adapt the plague's deadly properties for the Dark Lady's arsenal.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Berard?",a="Apothecary Berard was once one of the Royal Apothecary Society's most promising researchers in Silverpine Forest. Archmage Arugal's shadow curse shattered his mind and bound him as a thrall in Pyrewood Village.",al={"berard lore","who was berard","apothecary berard pyrewood"},it="people"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society want Berard's journal?",a="Berard's journal records an ancient plague that wiped out all aquatic life in Lake Lordamere. It preserves the plague's traits for the Royal Apothecary Society.",al={"why get the journal","berards journal purpose","lake lordamere plague notes"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Berard's journal located?",a="Berard's journal lies in his study on an upper floor of the Pyrewood Village Inn, toward the rear of the village. The afflicted apothecary still guards his former quarters.",al={"where is the journal","find berard journal","pyrewood inn journal"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who receives the recovered journal?",a="Apothecary Renferrel receives the journal at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He oversees the Royal Apothecary Society's field operations there.",al={"who turns in berard journal","who do i bring the journal to","where take journal"},it="next_step"},{q="What happened to Pyrewood Village?",a="Archmage Arugal's shadow magic from nearby Shadowfang Keep corrupted Pyrewood Village. The curse warped the villagers' minds and bodies, binding them to Arugal's will.",al={"pyrewood curse","what is wrong with pyrewood","arugal curse pyrewood"},it="history"},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell heads the Royal Apothecary Society from the Apothecarium in the Undercity. He oversees the creation of blights and venoms to defend the Forsaken and eradicate their enemies.",al={"faranell","who gives recipe for death","apothecary leader undercity"},it="leader"},{q="What is Berard's Journal?",a="Berard's Journal contains the research notes of Apothecary Berard before Archmage Arugal's curse stripped him of his mind. In it, Berard documented an ancient plague that eradicated aquatic life across Lake Lordamere ages ago. The Royal Apothecary Society hopes to study his findings to develop new plagues for the Forsaken.",al={"berards journal","what is in berards journal","berard journal purpose"},it="item",add="5e9e51e7"},{q="Who is guarding Berard's journal in Pyrewood?",a="The journal remains in the Pyrewood Village inn, guarded by Berard himself alongside the cursed villagers. Once a promising alchemist for the Royal Apothecary Society, Berard succumbed to Arugal's shadow magic and now serves the mad mage mindlessly as a feral creature, hostile to any who intrude upon his former study.",al={"who guards berards journal","who is guarding the journal","who do i fight for the journal"},it="target",add="3b951ca3"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you see the Royal Apothecary Society's cold pragmatism. When Berard was lost to madness, the Society set aside his tragedy to salvage his lethal research.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help the Royal Apothecary Society in Silverpine secure the Forsaken's borders against the wild terrors Arugal unleashed."},kw={"arugal","berard","faranell","journal","lordamere","pyrewood","renferrel","sepulcher"},rel={"quest:447","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:pyrewood-village","subzone:sepulcher","npc:arugal","topic:royal-apothecary-society"},m={start="Master Apothecary Faranell",["end"]="Apothecary Renferrel",level="15",faction="Horde",id=450,ri={"Berard's Journal"}},src={"A Recipe For Death (2)"}}
E["quest:451"] = {t="quest",n="A Recipe For Death",z="undercity",s="Apothecary Renferrel sends you to gather rare reagents across Lake Lordamere. Berard's journal names mosses and a strange tumor, which you bring to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity. The Royal Apothecary Society needs them for its work on a New Plague.",h="Apothecary Renferrel sends you to gather rare reagents across Lake Lordamere.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Research",b="Apothecary Berard's death under Arugal's curse cost the Royal Apothecary Society a skilled researcher. His field journal survived, preserving what he learned about blighted life in Silverpine Forest and Lake Lordamere. At the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel studied the recovered notes and found Berard's account of promising properties in local freshwater organisms. Now Renferrel asks you to carry forward the work his colleague began.",sp=0},{t="The Hazards of Lake Lordamere",b="Berard's reagents lie among the Dawning Isles, mist-shrouded islands in the eastern waters of Lake Lordamere. Lake skulkers and lake creepers on the isles carry peculiar moss strains that live in tainted water. Berard also noted a hardened tumor among the fierce Vile Fin murloc tribes that nest along the islets and the lake's southern shoreline near Ambermill.",sp=0},{t="Fueling the Apothecarium",b="Master Apothecary Faranell receives the specimens at the Apothecarium in the Undercity, bypassing the Sepulcher. He considers these strange mutations essential to making a New Plague that can destroy the Scourge and the living. Berard's research now feeds the Society's work in its cauldron vats, bringing the Forsaken closer to their weapon.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society need moss and a tumor?",a="Apothecary Berard's field journal describes unusual properties in the aquatic mosses found on lake beasts and the hardened tumors growing on local Vile Fin murlocs. Master Apothecary Faranell uses these rare, altered materials to brew and refine the Royal Apothecary Society's New Plague.",al={"why moss and tumor","apothecary recipe ingredients","what is the tumor for"},it="item"},{q="Who was Berard?",a="Apothecary Berard researched for the Royal Apothecary Society in Silverpine Forest. Arugal's curse made him a mindless servant, but his recovered field journal gave Apothecary Renferrel and Master Apothecary Faranell the reagent details needed to carry on his work.",al={"apothecary berard","who is berard","berard journal"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Dawning Isles located?",a="The Dawning Isles are small islands in eastern Lake Lordamere, just east of Silverpine Forest. Lake skulkers, lake creepers, and hostile Vile Fin murloc tribes infest them.",al={"where are dawning isles","dawning isles location","lake skulker location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell leads the Royal Apothecary Society from deep within the Apothecarium in the Undercity. He oversees research into chemical warfare and biological concoctions, as well as the creation of the New Plague for Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"faranell","who is faranell","master apothecary faranell"},it="leader"},{q="Why are Vile Fin murlocs growing hardened tumors?",a="Blighted decay and nearby arcane conflicts have warped Lake Lordamere's waters and shores. Hardened tumors on the Vile Fin are rare, abnormal growths from this contaminated environment, and the Forsaken prize them for study.",al={"why murloc tumor","vile fin tumor lore","hardened tumor murlocs"},it="origin"},{q="How does this quest connect to the New Plague?",a="The Recipe for Death chain gathers ingredients for the New Plague. Junior apothecaries such as Renferrel decipher and collect regional materials, then send them to Faranell's plague-brewing work in the Undercity.",al={"new plague connection","a new plague questline","is this the plague"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel want this done?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is dedicated to advancing the Royal Apothecary Society's research into the New Plague. Following the loss of his colleague Berard, Renferrel deciphered Berard's field journal and discovered promising leads on unique biological reagents. By sending you to collect these specimens and deliver them directly to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity, Renferrel ensures that Berard's sacrifice is not wasted and that their work for the Dark Lady continues without delay.",al={"why does renferrel want this","renferrel motive","why does apothecary renferrel send you"},it="motive",add="ba3f7fe6"},{q="What are you hunting on the Dawning Isles?",a="You are dispatched to eastern Lake Lordamere to hunt the lake beasts and local murlocs dwelling around the Dawning Isles. Lake Skulkers and Lake Creepers yield the vital mosses identified in Berard's journal, while the aggressive Vile Fin murloc tribes inhabiting the shores occasionally develop the strange, hardened growths Master Apothecary Faranell needs to experiment on.",al={"who are you sent against","what do you kill in a recipe for death","lake lordamere targets"},it="target",add="98d37a99"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, carrying on Berard's unfinished experiments serves the Dark Lady's vision. Every Forsaken mind helps the nation survive, even in death.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help Forsaken apothecaries gather reagents for their New Plague."},kw={"a recipe for death","apothecarium","berard","dawning isles","faranell","hardened tumor","lake creeper","lake lordamere","lake skulker","new plague","renferrel","vile fin"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","quest:447","quest:367","topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:dawning-isles","zone:undercity","topic:murloc"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="Master Apothecary Faranell",level="18",faction="Horde",id=451,ri={"Hardened Tumor","Lake Creeper Moss","Lake Skulker Moss"}},src={"A Recipe For Death (3)"}}
E["quest:491"] = {t="quest",n="Wand to Bethor",z="undercity",s="At Fenris Keep, the confrontation ends with the Woven Wand bound for Bethor Iceshard. Three apprentice mages made it as a sign of fellowship, but Thule Ravenclaw hid it after choosing the Scourge. Its return brings a piece of Bethor's mortal youth back to the Undercity.",h="At Fenris Keep, the confrontation ends with the Woven Wand bound for Bethor Iceshard.",sec={{t="A Token of Fractured Fellowship",b="Before Lordaeron fell, three young mages joined their training wands into one, the Woven Wand. It marked their friendship and shared hopes in the magical arts. Thule Ravenclaw later gave his loyalty to the Lich King and embraced the Scourge, breaking their fellowship. He came to despise the friendship they had shared, yet could not destroy the wand or leave it with his former companions.",sp=0},{t="Hidden in the Keep",b="Thule Ravenclaw carried the Woven Wand to Fenris Isle and hid it on a dusty shelf inside Fenris Keep. The wand lay untouched for years, its enchantment dormant. Bethor noted that using its magic would have revealed its whereabouts at once. Returning it to the Magic Quarter of the Undercity gives Bethor a keepsake of his mortal youth, recovered from the lair of a traitor who could neither love his friends nor let them go.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Woven Wand?",a="The Woven Wand is a magical tool made long ago by Thule Ravenclaw, Bethor Iceshard, and a third apprentice mage. Each gave an early training wand, and the three were woven together as a sign of their friendship and shared arcane studies.",al={"woven wand","what is the wand","thule wand lore"},it="item"},{q="Why did Thule Ravenclaw steal the wand?",a="When Thule Ravenclaw turned to the Lich King, his bond with the other mages broke. He came to hate what the wand represented, yet would not part with it or let Bethor and their other companion keep it. He hid the wand on Fenris Isle.",al={"why did thule take it","why steal the wand","thule stolen wand"},it="history"},{q="Who is Bethor Iceshard?",a="Bethor Iceshard is a powerful Forsaken mage who lives in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Before Lordaeron fell, he was Thule Ravenclaw's peer and friend. Thule later surrendered his will to the Scourge.",al={"who is bethor","bethor iceshard lore","bethor undercity"},it="identity"},{q="Why didn't Thule use the Woven Wand's magic?",a="Bethor would have sensed the wand's enchantment across the arcane weave if Thule had used it. Thule left its power untouched on a forgotten shelf in Fenris Keep, keeping the wand out of spite and possessiveness.",al={"did thule use wand","wand power","why not use it"},it="power"},{q="Who was the third apprentice who helped make the wand?",a="Gunther Arcanus was the third apprentice who joined his wand with Bethor's and Thule's, long before Thule betrayed them.",al={"third apprentice","three mages wand","third mage"},it="people"},{q="Where did the wand end up before being found?",a="Thule Ravenclaw hid the wand on a dusty shelf in a hidden niche inside Fenris Keep on Fenris Isle. He had established his Scourge operations in that stronghold.",al={"where was wand","hidden niche wand","fenris keep wand"},it="place"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For a mage, the Woven Wand recalls an arcane tradition: apprentice mages joining their foci in fellowship. The Scourge shattered that innocence when it tore Dalaran and Lordaeron apart.",["race:Undead"]="As one of the Forsaken, you may see old artifacts as reminders of mortal hopes and former friends. Bethor's keepsake recalls those who chose the Lich King's tyranny over free will."},kw={"bethor iceshard","fenris isle","fenris keep","magic quarter","silverpine","thule ravenclaw","undercity","woven wand"},rel={"quest:461","quest:460","quest:446","npc:bethor-iceshard","subzone:magic-quarter","subzone:fenris-keep","zone:undercity","topic:lich-king"},m={start="Dusty Shelf",["end"]="Bethor Iceshard",level="18",faction="Horde",id=491},src={"Wand to Bethor"}}
E["quest:513"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Agony",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Lydon's freshly mashed Mudsnout Composite awaits refinement. Apothecary Lydon sends it from Tarren Mill to Master Apothecary Faranell, who must treat it with a colloid of decay as the Royal Apothecary Society develops a new plague for the Forsaken.",h="In the Undercity, Lydon's freshly mashed Mudsnout Composite awaits refinement.",sec={{t="A Courier to the Capital",b="The Royal Apothecary Society sends raw discoveries from its regional researchers to the Undercity for specialized refinement. In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon has mashed local Mudsnout Blossoms into a composite. Only the capital's laboratory holds the advanced reagents needed to bring his work to lethal fruition.",sp=0},{t="The Master's Urgency",b="Master Apothecary Faranell works under pressure in the Apothecarium. The Scourge threatens from the north, while aggressive human populations press from the south. Lady Sylvanas Windrunner has demanded a potent new plague to defend the Forsaken. Lydon's composite could give Faranell the toxic breakthrough the Dark Lady expects.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do I need to take the Mudsnout Composite to the Undercity?",a="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill lacks the reagents to finish this stage of his experiment. Master Apothecary Faranell has a colloid of decay in the Apothecarium, and he must apply it to the Mudsnout Composite before the mixture can progress.",al={"why go to undercity","mudsnout composite destination","why bring to faranell"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell leads the Royal Apothecary Society from his laboratory deep in the Undercity. He oversees the Forsaken's major chemical and alchemical research and answers directly to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"who is faranell","master apothecary faranell lore","apothecarium leader"},it="identity"},{q="What is the new plague the apothecaries keep mentioning?",a="The new plague is an ongoing Forsaken project commanded by Lady Sylvanas. It is engineered to annihilate both the living and the undead Scourge, giving the Forsaken an absolute weapon against their enemies.",al={"what is the new plague","forsaken plague project","why make a new plague"},it="threat"},{q="Where can I find Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Faranell resides in the Apothecarium, the Undercity's southwestern quarter, devoted entirely to alchemy, poison brewing, and surgical experimentation.",al={"where is faranell","faranell location","apothecarium location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Apothecary Lydon trying to create?",a="Lydon is concocting the Elixir of Agony, an intensely virulent toxin brewed from Hillsbrad flora and decay agents. It is designed to prove the effectiveness of new strains in the field.",al={"what is lydon making","elixir of agony purpose","lydon experiment"},it="motive"},{q="Why is the Royal Apothecary Society so rushed?",a="The Forsaken face threats on every side. The Scourge of Northrend threatens to overrun them, while human resistance from the south applies relentless pressure. A decisive biological weapon is urgently needed.",al={"why rush","faranell busy","undercity threat"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon send you instead of going himself?",a="Apothecary Lydon is stationed in the Hillsbrad Foothills running critical field research for the Royal Apothecary Society. Preparing toxic compounds and monitoring local developments requires his constant attention at Tarren Mill, so trusted couriers must carry his raw mixtures to the Undercity for specialized refinement.",al={"why send me","why doesn't Lydon go to Undercity","why can't Lydon deliver it"},it="why_me",add="c9de6b5a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, each batch of raw plant matter delivered to Faranell helps secure the Forsaken's survival and sovereign defense against the living and the Scourge.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you rely on Forsaken territory to hold northern Lordaeron. The Royal Apothecary Society's research helps defend those vulnerable borders."},kw={"apothecarium","apothecary lydon","colloid of decay","elixir of agony","master apothecary faranell","mudsnout composite","new plague","undercity"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","quest:509","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","quest:367","zone:hillsbrad","topic:scourge","topic:horde"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",["end"]="Master Apothecary Faranell",level="28",faction="Horde",id=513},src={"Elixir of Agony (2)"}}
E["quest:515"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Agony",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Faranell prepares Lydon's mixture for a deadly purpose. The Royal Apothecary Society's new plague needs coastal reagents and alchemical draughts before the brew can be used.",h="In the Undercity, Faranell prepares Lydon's mixture for a deadly purpose.",sec={{t="A Colloid of Decay",b="Apothecary Lydon sent his Mudsnout Blossom mixture from gnoll-held Nethander Stead to the Apothecarium in the Undercity. Master Apothecary Faranell, head of the Royal Apothecary Society, saw its grim potential at once. Pleased by its toxic properties, he added his own colloid of decay. Then he named the catalysts needed to make the mixture a weapon.",sp=0},{t="Catalysts from the Coast",b="Lydon must gather precise reagents in Tarren Mill to activate the mixture's contaminating agents. Faranell calls for a restorative draught of Strong Troll's Blood to feed and steady the chemical reaction. He also needs organic parts from Hillsbrad's southern shore: scales from the serpentine Daggerspine naga and eyes from the coastal Torn Fin murlocs.",sp=0},{t="Cruelty in Tarren Mill",b="Back in Tarren Mill, Lydon passes the waiting hours by poisoning, infecting, and reanimating his undead test subject, Umpi. Faranell's enriched mixture and the coastal catalysts bring Lydon closer to perfecting an agonizing new strain of blight for the living settlements of Hillsbrad.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does the plague require a restorative troll's blood elixir?",a="Restorative Strong Troll's Blood helps sustain, fuel, and rapidly mutate aggressive biological agents. Its properties keep the toxic cultures thriving long enough to react with the other tissues.",al={"why troll blood","strong trolls blood purpose","trolls blood elixir plague"},it="item"},{q="Where are the Daggerspine scales found?",a="Daggerspine scales come from the hostile naga on Hillsbrad's eastern beaches, along the shore east of Southshore.",al={"daggerspine scales location","where are naga scales","where to get scales"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where are the Torn Fin eyes obtained?",a="Torn Fin eyes come from murloc tribes on Hillsbrad's western coast, just west of Southshore.",al={"torn fin eye location","where are torn fin murlocs","murloc eyes hillsbrad"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is Umpi?",a="Umpi is the frog Apothecary Lydon keeps as his assistant in Tarren Mill. In his idle hours, Lydon uses her as a test subject, inflicting lethal toxins and diseases before reanimating her.",al={"who is umpi","umpi hillsbrad","lydon assistant umpi"},it="people"},{q="Why is Master Apothecary Faranell involved in this local project?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell leads the Royal Apothecary Society and oversees research into biological agents and plagues. Field apothecaries such as Lydon send promising discoveries to Faranell in the Undercity for refinement and authorization.",al={"why faranell","master apothecary faranell role","royal apothecary society leader"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Mudsnout Mixture?",a="Lydon's Mudsnout Mixture is an unrefined toxic blend made from Mudsnout Blossoms, foul mushrooms gathered at gnoll-infested Nethander Stead in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Seeing its unusual virulence, Lydon sent it to the Undercity, where Faranell added decayed colloids to make a deadlier contagion.",al={"mudsnout mixture","gnoll poison","mudsnout composite"},it="item"},{q="What are the Daggerspine Scales and Torn Fin Eyes for?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell specifies that both the reptilian scales of the Daggerspine naga and the eyes of the Torn Fin murlocs are necessary reagents to activate the contaminating agents dormant within the Mudsnout Mixture. Combined with his own colloid of decay and restorative troll blood, these coastal aquatic harvests provide the reactive catalyst Apothecary Lydon requires to bring his lethal compound to life.",al={"daggerspine scale use","torn fin eye why needed","why daggerspine scales"},it="item",add="45c57bb0"},{q="Who are the Daggerspine and Torn Fin along the coast?",a="The southern shoreline of Hillsbrad Foothills has been overrun by hostile aquatic tribes flanking Southshore. To the east, the Daggerspine naga have encroached onto the beaches from the Great Sea, claiming territory with serpentine ferocity. To the west dwell the Torn Fin murlocs, scavengers clinging to the shallows. Their biology makes them unwitting sources of reagents for Forsaken alchemical warfare.",al={"hillsbrad naga murlocs","who are daggerspine","who are torn fin"},it="target",add="ff4494e7"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Each refined reagent brings the Royal Apothecary Society closer to fulfilling Lady Sylvanas's desire for an ultimate weapon against the living.",["faction:Horde"]="Tarren Mill faces constant border skirmishes with the Alliance of Southshore. Lydon's toxic experiments aim to tip the regional balance of power."},kw={"daggerspine","elixir of agony","faranell","lydon","mudsnout","tarren mill","torn fin","umpi","undercity"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:royal-apothecary-society","npc:umpi","quest:509","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity","subzone:southshore"},m={start="Master Apothecary Faranell",["end"]="Apothecary Lydon",level="30",faction="Horde",id=515,ri={"Daggerspine Scale","Strong Troll's Blood Elixir","Torn Fin Eye"}},src={"Elixir of Agony (3)"}}
E["quest:530"] = {t="quest",n="A Husband's Revenge",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Raleigh Andrean sends you after the friend who murdered his wife.",h="In the Undercity, Raleigh Andrean sends you after the friend who murdered his wife.",sec={{t="A Bitter Memory",b="An engraved ring from Silverpine Forest brings Raleigh Andrean's mortal memories back to him. He remembers his close friend Valdred Moray, who murdered Raleigh's wife, Deliah. The Scourge's chill and undeath have dulled Raleigh's grief and love, but his thirst for revenge remains. You are sent to find Valdred.",sp=0},{t="Justice at the Wall",b="Valdred Moray fled south through Silverpine Forest, seeking refuge beyond the Greymane Wall. The gates to Gilneas stayed shut to refugees and outcasts. Trapped against the wall, Valdred met his end at Raleigh's command. His severed hands were carried back to the Undercity.",sp=1},{t="Cold Keepsakes",b="Raleigh receives his former friend's hands without warmth or relief. With the score settled, he returns Deliah's wedding band, calling it a useless bauble. Valdred Moray's severed hands remain in the Undercity as a lasting reminder of betrayal.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Raleigh want Valdred's hands specifically?",a="Raleigh wants Valdred's hands because they ended his wife's life. He keeps them in the Undercity as a trophy and reminder of his friend's betrayal.",al={"why hands","valdred hands","raleigh wants hands"},it="item"},{q="Where is Valdred Moray hiding?",a="Valdred Moray is in far southern Silverpine Forest, camped against the Greymane Wall after failing to enter Gilneas.",al={"where is valdred","valdred location","valdred moray spot"},gp=true},{q="Why does Raleigh give back the wedding ring?",a="Raleigh's attachment to Deliah has withered in undeath. Her ring means nothing to him; revenge was what mattered.",al={"why give ring away","ring of scorn lore","why discard ring"},sp=1},{q="Can Valdred Moray enter Gilneas?",a="No. King Genn Greymane sealed Gilneas behind a wall after the Second War, and its gates remain closed. Valdred, like many desperate refugees, is stranded there.",al={"greymane wall closed","why is valdred outside wall"}},{q="What quests lead up to this task?",a="The chain begins with The Engraved Ring in Silverpine Forest. It sends you to the Undercity in Raleigh and the Undercity, which opens A Husband's Revenge.",al={"husband revenge chain","prerequisite quest","previous quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Raleigh Andrean want revenge?",a="Valdred Moray was once Raleigh's close friend, but he murdered Raleigh's wife, Deliah. While the cold grasp of undeath has stripped Raleigh of his ability to mourn or grieve his lost love, the burning urge for retribution remains. Avenging her death and punishing his former friend's betrayal is the only desire he has left in his unlife.",al={"why does raleigh want valdred dead","raleigh andrean motive","why kill valdred moray"},it="motive",add="f744ed49"},{q="Who is Valdred Moray and why is he at the Greymane Wall?",a="Valdred Moray is Raleigh Andrean's former friend who murdered Raleigh's wife, Deliah. Having committed the crime, he fled south into Silverpine Forest and holed up by the sealed gates of the Greymane Wall, desperate to escape into the closed kingdom of Gilneas before his past catches up with him.",al={"who is valdred moray","why is valdred moray in silverpine","valdred moray greymane wall"},it="target",add="71a98bea"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you can see how undeath has dulled Raleigh's love for his dead wife while leaving his hatred and hunger for revenge.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure the Undercity's borders by pursuing human outlaws through Silverpine Forest."},kw={"deliah","engraved ring","greymane wall","raleigh andrean","ring of scorn","silverpine forest","undercity","valdred moray"},rel={"npc:raleigh-andrean","quest:441","quest:440","subzone:greymane-wall","zone:undercity"},m={start="Raleigh Andrean",level="20",faction="Horde",id=530,ri={"Valdred's Hands"}},src={"A Husband's Revenge"}}
E["quest:550"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="undercity",s="At Hillsbrad, the Forsaken campaign has broken the human township's defenses. High Executor Darthalia sends you to carry her commendation to Varimathras in the Undercity.",h="At Hillsbrad, the Forsaken campaign has broken the human township's defenses.",sec={{t="A Decisive Campaign",b="The fighting in Hillsbrad Foothills has been a brutal struggle for southern Lordaeron. From Tarren Mill, Horde champions struck at the township's farmers, militia, blacksmiths, and civic leaders. With Alliance forces crippled and the territory secured for the Forsaken, High Executor Darthalia prepares an official commendation so the champion's deeds reach the highest ranks of command.",sp=0},{t="Audience with the Dreadlord",b="Darthalia's sealed commendation takes you to Varimathras in the Undercity's Royal Quarter. The dreadlord oversees military operations across Lordaeron beside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. The Scourge from the northern Plaguelands remains the Dark Lady's greatest threat, while surviving human enclaves still endanger the Forsaken's southern borders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is this quest?",a="High Executor Darthalia sends you to deliver her sealed commendation to Varimathras in the Undercity, after the Forsaken campaign against Hillsbrad has broken the township's defenses.",al={"battle of hillsbrad finale","hillsbrad final quest","quest 550"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do I turn in Darthalia's Sealed Commendation?",a="Take Darthalia's Sealed Commendation to Varimathras in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity, where he stands beside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"where is varimathras","turn in commendation","darthalia letter turn in"},gp=true},{q="Why does Varimathras care about Hillsbrad?",a="Varimathras oversees military operations across Lordaeron. The Scourge in the north is the Undercity's greatest threat, but human settlements in the south harass Forsaken lines, so Hillsbrad's defeat protects the southern frontier.",al={"why varimathras","varimathras role in hillsbrad"},it="ties"},{q="Who is High Executor Darthalia?",a="High Executor Darthalia is the senior Forsaken commander at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. She directs the offensive against the nearby human settlement.",al={"darthalia","who gave the quest"},it="identity"},{q="Does this quest lead to further missions in Hillsbrad?",a="Delivering the commendation to Varimathras concludes the Battle of Hillsbrad storyline. Darthalia commends you for breaking the town's defenses.",al={"next quest after battle of hillsbrad","what comes after quest 550"},it="next_step"},{q="Why were the Forsaken attacking Hillsbrad in the first place?",a="Hillsbrad is one of the last organized human footholds in Lordaeron. Its Alliance militia and its proximity threaten Tarren Mill and the southern approaches to the Undercity.",al={"why attack hillsbrad","hillsbrad lore"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia want this commendation delivered?",a="You have fought with valor and perseverance throughout the brutal campaign across the Hillsbrad Foothills. High Executor Darthalia wants your battlefield heroics formally recognized by the Forsaken high command in the Undercity. By sending you directly to Varimathras with her sealed commendation, she ensures that the leadership acknowledges a capable champion whose decisive strikes broke human resistance on the southern front.",al={"why send commendation","darthalia motive","why send to varimathras"},it="motive",add="8522c300"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you bring word of your victory over Hillsbrad's living to the Royal Quarter, earning praise and affirming your place in the Dark Lady's rising empire.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you drive back Alliance forces in Lordaeron and secure vital ground for the Horde in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","hillsbrad foothills","royal quarter","sealed commendation","tarren mill","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"npc:varimathras","npc:high-executor-darthalia","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:lich-king"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",["end"]="Varimathras",level="32",faction="Horde",id=550},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (7) (Classic)"}}
E["quest:5679"] = {t="quest",n="Devouring Plague",z="undercity",s="Forsaken priests in the Undercity learn Devouring Plague from Priestess Aelthalyste. The rite is for those who have proven their dedication to shadow magic, and teaches a feared curse of the undead priesthood.",h="Forsaken priests in the Undercity learn Devouring Plague from Priestess Aelthalyste.",sec={{t="A Curse of the Shadow",b="In the Undercity’s War Quarter, Priestess Aelthalyste teaches Forsaken priests the grim arts of the Shadow. Priests of other races draw power from the Holy Light or ancestral spirits, but the Forsaken have shaped their own spiritual doctrines. Devouring Plague gives form to that path: it torments foes and drains their stolen vitality to sustain the caster’s decaying body.",sp=0},{t="A Test of Mastery",b="Priestess Aelthalyste shares the plague’s power only with care. The spell is a weapon of potent malice, meant to turn the tide against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade. As she teaches it, she warns her disciples to practice until their command is sure. Greater trials await those who seek mastery of the dark arts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This rite teaches Forsaken priests who have reached seasoned standing to cast Devouring Plague. The shadow affliction drains its victim and heals the caster.",al={"why do devouring plague","what does devouring plague quest do","devouring plague purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Priestess Aelthalyste?",a="Priestess Aelthalyste is a Forsaken priest trainer in the Undercity’s War Quarter. She guides emerging shadow casters and sees that they wield their destructive blessings effectively for the Forsaken.",al={"who is aelthalyste","aelthalyste lore","aelthalyste undercity"},it="identity"},{q="Can priests of other races learn Devouring Plague from Aelthalyste?",a="Devouring Plague isn't hers alone to give: every priest, whatever their race, learns it from a priest trainer at level 20. The Forsaken's own racial teachings are Touch of Weakness and Dark Sacrifice.",al={"can trolls learn devouring plague","is devouring plague undead only","other races devouring plague"},gp=true},{q="Where do I turn in this quest?",a="Priestess Aelthalyste is in the War Quarter of the Undercity, among the Forsaken priest instructors and practitioners.",al={"aelthalyste location","where is devouring plague quest","undercity priest trainer location"},gp=true},{q="Why do Forsaken priests specialize in plague and shadow magic?",a="Forsaken priests feel intense physical pain when they channel the Holy Light because they are undead. Many turn to the Shadow, using afflictions, curses, and stolen life-force to survive and wage war.",al={"why forsaken shadow priests","lore behind undead priests","forsaken priest magic"},it="origin"},{q="What tests is Aelthalyste referring to?",a="As a priest grows in power, Aelthalyste warns, trials across Lordaeron grow harder. Dark magic draws dangerous scrutiny and deadly foes, so an acolyte must command every curse in their repertoire.",al={"tests later meaning","future tests aelthalyste","what tests"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Priestess Aelthalyste want you to learn Devouring Plague?",a="Priestess Aelthalyste sees Devouring Plague as a vital, potent weapon for the Forsaken's survival. She instructs Forsaken priests in this dark art so that you will be properly equipped to defend the Undercity and prevail in the relentless trials and conflicts awaiting the Forsaken across Lordaeron.",al={"aelthalyste motive","why teach devouring plague","why does aelthalyste want this done"},it="motive",rc="Undead",add="7f0f5b4f"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a Forsaken priest, you learn one of your most dreaded spells, tying your survival to the affliction you inflict on your enemies.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you inherit a path of plague-like shadowcraft that reflects the Forsaken’s departure from traditional Lordaeron worship after the Third War.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you bring ruthless, disease-like curses to its arsenal, while other allies rely on ancestral spirits or elemental balance."},kw={"aelthalyste","devouring plague","forsaken","lordaeron","priest","shadow","undercity","war quarter"},rel={"npc:aelthalyste","quest:5644"},m={start="Aelthalyste",level="20",faction="Horde",id=5679},src={"Devouring Plague (Undercity)"}}
E["quest:6322"] = {t="quest",n="Michael Garrett",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, Michael Garrett awaits a crate bound for the Sepulcher. Gordon Wendham packs field supplies in the Trade Quarter, and you bring them to Garrett for the Forsaken bat network to carry toward Silverpine Forest.",h="In the Undercity, Michael Garrett awaits a crate bound for the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="Supplying the Outposts",b="The Forsaken send supplies from the Undercity to outposts such as the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Gordon Wendham packs field supplies in a crate in the Trade Quarter. Moving freight along the ground through blighted forests is slow and leaves it open to ambush by Scourge remnants or wild beasts.",sp=0},{t="Wings of the Forsaken",b="The Forsaken use captive vampire bats, bred and kept by skilled handlers, to avoid dangerous roads. Michael Garrett tends the bats from his roost in the Undercity's Trade Quarter. When you bring him the cargo, it can be strapped to a bat and flown over the hills toward Silverpine, linking the capital with its outposts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Michael Garrett?",a="Michael Garrett handles bats in the Undercity's Trade Quarter. He arranges travel and air deliveries between the Forsaken capital and allied flight masters throughout Lordaeron.",al={"michael garrett","undercity bat master","who is garrett"},it="identity"},{q="What is in Gordon's Crate?",a="Gordon Wendham's crate holds field supplies for Forsaken forces stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",al={"gordon's crate","what supplies","sepulcher crate"},it="item"},{q="Why use bats instead of carts or horses?",a="The roads are hazardous, and trained giant bats fly much faster while bypassing ground ambushes.",al={"why bat flight","why use bats","flying supplies"}},{q="Where does the delivery go after Michael Garrett?",a="After Michael Garrett receives Gordon's Crate, the cargo is prepared for flight to the bat master stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",al={"next step","after michael garrett","where do bats fly"},it="next_step"},{q="Where can Michael Garrett be found in Undercity?",a="Michael Garrett is in the southwestern part of the Trade Quarter, where bats arriving from the Sepulcher land.",al={"where is garrett","find bat handler","undercity flight master location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Do you need to have visited the Sepulcher before doing this?",a="To ride a bat alongside the delivery, you must have spoken with the flight handler at the Sepulcher to open the route. Otherwise, you travel there on foot.",al={"sepulcher flight path required","can i fly immediately"},gp=true},{q="Why does Gordon Wendham want this done?",a="Gordon Wendham is tasked with coordinating vital logistical supplies destined for the Sepulcher, the Forsaken outpost in Silverpine Forest. Since he must remain at his trade post in the Undercity to manage goods, he needs you to transfer the packed crate to Michael Garrett so it can be dispatched swiftly along their aerial courier route.",al={"why send gordon's crate","gordon wendham motive","why bring crate to michael garrett"},it="motive",add="2851daa3"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The aerial supply line run by handlers such as Michael Garrett helps maintain Sylvanas's presence beyond Tirisfal Glades.",["faction:Horde"]="For travelers arriving from Kalimdor, the Forsaken bat network is the primary way to travel quickly across the northern Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"bat master","flight master","gordon wendham","gordon's crate","michael garrett","sepulcher","silverpine","undercity"},rel={"npc:gordon-wendham","zone:undercity","subzone:sepulcher","quest:6324"},m={start="Gordon Wendham",["end"]="Michael Garrett",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6322},src={"Michael Garrett (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6323"] = {t="quest",n="Ride to the Undercity",z="undercity",s="A courier carries Podrig's weapons request from the Sepulcher to the Undercity. A dread bat bears the message over Silverpine Forest to the Forsaken capital.",h="A courier carries Podrig's weapons request from the Sepulcher to the Undercity.",sec={{t="Wings Over Silverpine",b="Karos Razok handles the dread bats at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. They carry messengers and supplies between the Forsaken capital and its frontline outposts. The roads below are dangerous, with hostile beasts, Moonrage worgen, and Scourge remnants. The bats give urgent military requests a swift route to the capital.",sp=0},{t="Arming the Front",b="In the Undercity's Trade Quarter, the courier brings Podrig's equipment request to Gordon Wendham. The weaponsmith prepares arms for the Dark Lady's cause and keeps outposts such as the Sepulcher supplied with battle-ready weapons. Those outposts defend the young Forsaken nation against its surrounding enemies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this flight to the Undercity?",a="The flight carries Deathguard Podrig's weapons request from the Sepulcher to Gordon Wendham in the Undercity's Trade Quarter. It also shows new champions how to use the Forsaken flight network.",al={"why ride to undercity","ride to the undercity objective","podrig's order use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Karos Razok?",a="Karos Razok handles the dread bats at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. The bats carry Forsaken messengers and supplies to and from the Undercity.",al={"karos razok role","who is the sepulcher bat master"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Gordon Wendham?",a="Gordon Wendham is a Forsaken weaponsmith in the Undercity's Trade Quarter, near the bat handler's landing platform. He keeps weapons clean, sharp, and ready for Lady Sylvanas's frontline forces.",al={"gordon wendham","where is gordon wendham"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the Forsaken use bats for transit?",a="The Forsaken use dread bats to travel swiftly above dangerous ground. They cross Lordaeron's blighted skies over threats such as feral worgen, hostile rot hides, and the Scourge.",al={"why bats","forsaken flight mounts"}},{q="What happens after completing the delivery?",a="After receiving the order, Gordon Wendham sends couriers to Michael Garrett, the Undercity bat handler, to establish a return flight toward the Sepulcher.",al={"what comes next","follow up to ride to the undercity"},it="next_step"},{q="Where does the dread bat land in the Undercity?",a="The dread bat lands on the raised bat roost at the center of the Undercity's Trade Quarter, near the city's craftsmen and supply merchants.",al={"undercity bat landing","where does bat land"},it="place"},{q="Why does Karos Razok want this done?",a="As the flight master stationed at the Sepulcher, Karos Razok oversees the aerial courier network binding Silverpine Forest to the capital. Outposts like the Sepulcher depend entirely on steady supply lines and rapid correspondence to survive against surrounding threats. By carrying Deathguard Podrig's equipment requisition directly to the weapon suppliers in the Undercity, you ensure the front-line sentries defending the realm receive the arms and armor they desperately need.",al={"why send podrig order","karos razok motive","why ride to undercity"},it="motive",add="d629dc0f"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you can see how the Dark Lady's network links Silverpine to the capital and keeps isolated garrisons connected to the Undercity's industry.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see how Gordon Wendham helps keep Lordaeron's weapons sharp and ready for war.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you travel quickly across the wilderness through its flight masters, who connect its territories."},kw={"dread bat","flight master","gordon wendham","karos razok","podrig's order","ride to the undercity","sepulcher","trade quarter"},rel={"npc:karos-razok","npc:gordon-wendham","zone:undercity","subzone:trade-quarter","subzone:sepulcher","quest:6321"},m={start="Karos Razok",["end"]="Gordon Wendham",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6323},src={"Ride to the Undercity (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6324"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Podrig",z="undercity",s="At the Undercity, you receive a crate of weapons for the Sepulcher after delivering a dispatch to the capital. Forsaken bats carry you across Lordaeron to Deathguard Podrig.",h="At the Undercity, you receive a crate of weapons for the Sepulcher after delivering a dispatch to the capital.",sec={{t="The Undercity Supply Line",b="Deathguard Podrig's garrison at the Sepulcher needs a steady supply of weapons from the Undercity. In Silverpine Forest, its sentries face worgen, Dalaran remnants, and Scourge stragglers. Fresh armaments help the Forsaken hold the region and keep the outpost ready.",sp=0},{t="Wings of the Forsaken",b="Bat Master Michael Garrett tends the central roost in the Undercity's Trade Quarter. Forsaken bats know the way back to the capital, but you speak with local handlers such as Karos Razok before arranging a flight to a distant outpost. Carrying Gordon's Crate across Lordaeron links the Undercity's supplies with its scattered strongholds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is in Gordon's Crate?",a="Gordon's Crate holds fresh weapons made in the Undercity for the Deathguards at the Sepulcher, who face threats nearby.",al={"gordons crate contents","what am i delivering to podrig"},it="item"},{q="Who is Deathguard Podrig?",a="Deathguard Podrig is a Forsaken soldier stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He oversees the garrison's supplies and defenses.",al={"podrig","who is podrig"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Michael Garrett?",a="Michael Garrett is the Forsaken bat master at the Undercity's Trade Quarter. He coordinates flight paths across Lordaeron.",al={"michael garrett","undercity bat master"},it="identity"},{q="Why do you have to speak to a bat master before flying somewhere?",a="Forsaken bats know the way back to the central roost in the Undercity. For an outward flight, you first establish a route with a regional handler so the bat can reach its destination safely.",al={"flight path rules","how do bat handlers work"}},{q="Why is the Sepulcher so important to supply?",a="The Sepulcher is the Forsaken's main forward base in Silverpine Forest. It anchors their presence against worgen packs, Moonrage threats, and Dalaran forces in the area.",al={"why sepulcher matters","sepulcher importance"},it="place"},{q="Who is Karos Razok?",a="Karos Razok is the bat master at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He manages the roosted bats that connect the outpost to the Undercity.",al={"karos razok","sepulcher bat master"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Michael Garrett want this done?",a="As the Undercity's bat master, Michael Garrett oversees aerial transit and courier routes across Forsaken lands. Deathguard Podrig and the soldiers holding the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest desperately require fresh armaments from the capital. Garrett ensures these vital weapons are dispatched efficiently using the bat network, strengthening the Dark Lady's frontier outposts against nearby threats.",al={"why michael garrett crate","garrett motive return to podrig","why send crate to sepulcher"},it="motive",add="02244cab"},{q="Why does Michael Garrett send you instead of going himself?",a="Garrett must remain stationed at the Undercity's bat roost to tend to the beasts and coordinate flights in and out of the capital. Since you are an able courier already journeying back toward Silverpine Forest, entrusting you with the crate ensures the delivery is made without pulling valuable flight masters or guards away from their essential posts.",al={"why send me","why doesn't garrett deliver it","why me return to podrig"},it="why_me",add="eed737b1"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you help keep forward garrisons armed to defend Lordaeron and secure Queen Sylvanas's fledgling realm.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help sustain the supply routes connecting the Undercity to remote outposts across the northern continent."},kw={"bat master","gordons crate","karos razok","michael garrett","podrig","sepulcher","silverpine","undercity"},rel={"quest:6322","zone:undercity","subzone:sepulcher","npc:karos-razok"},m={start="Michael Garrett",["end"]="Deathguard Podrig",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6324},src={"Return to Podrig"}}
E["quest:8354"] = {t="quest",n="Chicken Clucking for a Mint",z="undercity",s="At Hallow's End, Innkeeper Norman of the Undercity offers a sweet to travelers helping an ailing child. Earn the Undercity Mint by setting dignity aside and flapping like a chicken.",h="At Hallow's End, Innkeeper Norman of the Undercity offers a sweet to travelers helping an ailing child.",sec={{t="A Rare Bit of Mirth",b="Laughter is scarce in the Undercity, built beneath Lordaeron's ruins by the liberated Forsaken. Yet when Hallow's End comes, even the grim folk of the Trade Quarter join the revelry. Innkeeper Norman keeps Undercity Mints for travelers gathering treats for Spoops, a sick orphan who needs holiday cheer.",sp=0},{t="Earning the Treat",b="Innkeeper Norman will not hand a treat to seasoned adventurers without a show. He believes grown warriors and spellcasters should earn their sweets. So the petitioner must mimic a barnyard chicken right before his counter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Innkeeper Norman want me to cluck like a chicken?",a="Innkeeper Norman thinks grown champions should put on a show before they go trick-or-treating. To lift the Hallow's End mood, he asks you to flap and cluck like a chicken before handing over the treat.",al={"why chicken emote","why cluck norman","norman chicken dance"},it="motive"},{q="Who is the treat intended for?",a="The Undercity Mint is for Spoops, a sick orphan resting in Orgrimmar who cannot go trick-or-treating during Hallow's End.",al={"who gets the mint","what is the mint for","why get undercity mint"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Innkeeper Norman located?",a="Innkeeper Norman keeps the central tavern in the Undercity's Trade Quarter, serving Forsaken patrons and visiting Horde travelers.",al={"norman location","where is undercity innkeeper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is this a seasonal festival quest?",a="Yes. It is part of Hallow's End, the annual holiday celebrated across Azeroth by both Horde and Alliance.",al={"is this hallows end","when is this quest available"},gp=true},{q="Do Forsaken normally celebrate Hallow's End?",a="The Forsaken celebrate Hallow's End with great enthusiasm. They burn a massive wicker man outside Lordaeron's ruins to honor their liberation and break with their former mortal lives.",al={"forsaken hallows end","undead holiday"},it="history"},{q="What happens after getting the Undercity Mint?",a="The Undercity Mint joins signature treats gathered from the Horde's racial capitals to make a full holiday gift for young Spoops.",al={"next quest","what do i do with the mint"},it="next_step",gp=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Laughter in the Undercity's rotting halls is rare. Norman's seasonal demand brings a strange break from daily necromantic pragmatism.",["faction:Horde"]="During Hallow's End, Horde travelers visit every capital city and endure foolish indignities to bring joy to an orphaned child."},kw={"chicken","cluck","hallow's end","innkeeper norman","spoops","trade quarter","undercity","undercity mint"},rel={"npc:innkeeper-norman","zone:undercity"},m={start="Innkeeper Norman",faction="Horde",id=8354},src={"Chicken Clucking for a Mint (Horde)"}}
E["quest:8648"] = {t="quest",n="Darkcore the Elder",z="undercity",s="During the Lunar Festival, travelers find Darkcore the Elder in the Undercity and honor Azeroth's ancient spirits. In return, they receive a Coin of Ancestry.",h="During the Lunar Festival, travelers find Darkcore the Elder in the Undercity and honor Azeroth's ancient...",sec={{t="A Spirit in the Undercity",b="During the Lunar Festival, spirits of ancient night elven and earthen ancestors appear across the continents. They offer wisdom and blessings to those who seek them. Elder Darkcore dwells in the Undercity's shadowed halls, watching the world as it is now and remembering those who sought its roots.",sp=0},{t="Honoring the Ancestors",b="Approaching Elder Darkcore honors an ancient custom. It shows respect for the venerable dead and Azeroth's timeless wardens. In return for the pilgrimage, the spirit gives travelers a Coin of Ancestry, a token of goodwill and enduring memory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of visiting Elder Darkcore?",a="Visiting Elder Darkcore during the Lunar Festival honors Azeroth's ancient peoples. Speaking with him earns a Coin of Ancestry.",al={"elder darkcore goal","why visit darkcore","darkcore quest purpose"}},{q="Where can Elder Darkcore be found?",a="Elder Darkcore appears in Lordaeron's ruined throne room, above the Forsaken capital of the Undercity.",al={"elder darkcore location","where is elder darkcore","darkcore undercity spot"}},{q="What is the Lunar Festival?",a="The Lunar Festival is an annual time of remembrance and renewal across Azeroth. It celebrates the triumph over the Burning Legion and honors ancient elders who guided mortal races.",al={"lunar festival lore","why are elders appearing","what are the elders"}},{q="What do the elders represent?",a="Elders are ancient spirits often tied to the night elves or early earthen cultures. During the Lunar Festival, they appear to bless those who remember their deeds and carry their lessons forward.",al={"who are the elders","lunar festival elders lore","ancestor spirits"}},{q="Can Alliance adventurers speak to Elder Darkcore?",a="Elder Darkcore greets any traveler who reaches him. Alliance travelers must brave the heavily defended Forsaken capital to speak with him.",al={"alliance darkcore","can alliance get darkcore","elder darkcore alliance"}},{q="What is a Coin of Ancestry?",a="A Coin of Ancestry is a festive token given by elders during the Lunar Festival. It honors the ancient past and can be traded for festive garb and seasonal keepsakes.",al={"what are coins of ancestry","coin of ancestry use","lunar festival coin"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken who walk the ruins of their former kingdom, Elder Darkcore recalls older times, before the Scourge and Lordaeron's fall.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can take part in the Lunar Festival's rites across the continents within an allied capital."},kw={"ancestor","coin of ancestry","darkcore the elder","elder darkcore","elders","lunar festival","undercity"},rel={"npc:elder-darkcore"},m={start="Elder Darkcore",id=8648},src={"Darkcore the Elder"}}
E["subzone:apothecarium"] = {t="subzone",n="Apothecarium",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity’s southwest quarter, the Apothecarium drives the Royal Apothecary Society’s work. Under Master Apothecary Faranell, Forsaken alchemists pursue plagues, toxins, and engineered horrors for Lady Sylvanas’s campaign against the living and the Scourge.",h="In the Undercity’s southwest quarter, the Apothecarium drives the Royal Apothecary Society’s work.",sec={{t="Chamber of Horrors",b="The Apothecarium fills the Undercity’s southwestern terrace with vats, dissection tables, and chemical fumes. Master Apothecary Faranell leads the Royal Apothecary Society’s work there, studying mortality and rot. Alchemists and surgeons experiment with tissue grafts and vivisection, and assemble mighty abominations. Lady Sylvanas Windrunner has charged them with creating a plague that can eradicate both the Scourge and the lingering human presence across Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="Center of Forsaken Alchemy",b="The quarter draws alchemists and herbalists from across the Horde in the Eastern Kingdoms. Initiates and masters gather beside toxic canals to distill concoctions, study botanical blights, and seek counsel from master practitioners.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Apothecarium used for?",a="The Apothecarium is where the Royal Apothecary Society researches and makes its wares. Forsaken alchemists brew experimental poisons, refine the New Plague, build abominations, and teach alchemy and herbalism there.",al={"apothecarium purpose","what happens here","why does the apothecarium exist"},it="purpose"},{q="Who leads the Apothecarium?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell leads the Apothecarium and its researchers. As chief scientist of the Royal Apothecary Society, he works with Queen Sylvanas Windrunner’s full authority and patronage.",al={"apothecarium leader","who runs the apothecarium","faranell undercity"},it="leader"},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society trying to create?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society seeks to create a lethal New Plague. It is meant to destroy the Lich King’s Scourge forces and the living human resistance contesting Forsaken territory in Lordaeron.",al={"forsaken plague research","new plague undercity","what are they brewing"},it="wants"},{q="Can players learn professions here?",a="Yes. The Apothecarium is the Undercity’s main hub for alchemists and herbalists, with advanced trainers along its walkways and in its chambers.",al={"apothecarium trainers","alchemy in undercity","undercity herbalism trainer"},gp=true},{q="What is the Apothecarium?",a="The Apothecarium is the southwestern quarter of the Undercity, serving as the grim headquarters and laboratory complex of the Royal Apothecary Society. Deep within its cavernous chambers, Forsaken alchemists and researchers brew noxious concoctions, engineer powerful abominations, and conduct grisly experiments to advance the Forsaken cause.",al={"what is the apothecarium","apothecarium undercity","undercity apothecarium"},it="place",add="05b32189"},{q="Is the Apothecarium dangerous?",a="It is safe enough for Horde travelers, but outsiders find it a chamber of horrors. The air is foul with toxic vapors, open vats churn with corrosive chemicals and blighted reagents, and shambling abominations roam its halls. Any living trespasser foolish enough to wander in risks ending up strapped to an apothecary's dissecting table.",al={"is apothecarium safe","apothecarium hazards","danger in apothecarium"},it="danger",add="170a66ad"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the Apothecarium produces the chemical and stitched weapons they need to hold Lordaeron against overwhelming enemies.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you supply the Royal Apothecary Society’s distillers with rare, blighted flora gathered from the northern kingdoms’ ruins."},kw={"abominations","alchemy","apothecarium","faranell","new plague","royal apothecary society","sylvanas","undercity"},rel={"topic:royal-apothecary-society","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","zone:undercity","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","quest:447","topic:forsaken","topic:lordaeron","quest:445"},src={"Apothecarium"}}
E["subzone:canals-undercity"] = {t="subzone",n="Canals (Undercity)",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity, green slime fills the Canals between its quarters. The murky channels carry waste and mark the Forsaken's underground stronghold.",h="In the Undercity, green slime fills the Canals between its quarters.",sec={{t="A Toxic Moat",b="Beneath Lordaeron's ruins, green sludge fills the Canals. The stone channels circle the Undercity and divide its quarters. They carry industrial refuse, chemical runoff, and alchemical waste instead of flowing water. Faint light shines through the liquid, and foul vapors rise from it. Water Walking cannot carry anyone across. Still, desperate anglers sometimes pull strange, tainted curiosities from the muck.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the green liquid in the canals?",a="The green liquid is alchemical sludge made from toxic runoff, plague byproducts, and industrial waste gathered in the Undercity's drains. It is tainted and noxious, unlike clean water.",al={"undercity green water","what is the slime in undercity","green slime river"}},{q="Can you fish in the Undercity canals?",a="Yes. Patient anglers can cast into the sludge and sometimes pull up sickly, contaminated fish or discarded junk. Among it are old human skulls from Lordaeron's fallen past.",al={"fishing undercity","can you fish here","fishing in green slime"},gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Water Walking work on the canals?",a="The thick chemical slurry does not behave like natural water. Its foul, viscous makeup keeps shamans and other spellcasters from using ordinary Water Walking magic on it.",al={"water walking undercity","shaman water walking bug","why cant i walk on water undercity"},gp=true},{q="What are the Canals in the Undercity?",a="The Canals are the sunken waterways that wind between the Undercity's distinct quarters. Flowing in a broad circular loop throughout the subterranean city, these deep stone channels carry a sluggish river of foul green sludge, dividing the districts while tying the cavernous lower city together.",al={"undercity canals","what are the canals","undercity canal system"},it="place",add="dc46e6d3"},{q="Are the Canals dangerous?",a="While the canals pose little immediate physical threat from lurking predators, their murky green depths are far from pristine. The viscous sludge is foul enough to harbor discarded bones, human skulls, and sickly, mutated aquatic life, making an accidental plunge thoroughly unpleasant.",al={"canals danger","is it safe to swim in undercity canals","are undercity canals safe"},it="danger",add="c0800d9e"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the foul canals do no harm to their unliving bodies. They carry chemical runoff through the underground realm and serve as a moat.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you find the elements have little sway over the polluted muck in the Undercity's waterways. Ordinary spells like Water Walking fail there."},kw={"canals","fishing","forsaken","green slime","lordaeron","sludge","toxic","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","subzone:canals-stormwind-city"},src={"Canals (Undercity)"}}
E["subzone:magic-quarter"] = {t="subzone",n="Magic Quarter",z="undercity",s="In the Undercity's northeast, Forsaken spellcasters study arcane and fel arts. The Temple of the Damned anchors their work.",h="In the Undercity's northeast, Forsaken spellcasters study arcane and fel arts.",sec={{t="A Conclave of Dark Arts",b="In the Undercity's northeastern quadrant, Forsaken mages preserve arcane learning and explore darker arts. The Temple of the Damned dominates the district, a Scourge-built structure now used by the free-willed undead. Beneath its vaulted ceilings, mages shape magical energies while warlocks commune with demons. Their work makes the quarter a center of study and occult research in Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="Scholars, Weavers, and Summoners",b="Spellcasters also come here for training and craft. Portal trainers maintain routes across Horde territories, and master tailors shape magically infused fabrics into robes and shrouds. In Dalaran, academic wizardry and forbidden magic are kept apart; Forsaken practitioners study arcane and fel power openly in the same halls, seeking strength against their many enemies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Magic Quarter?",a="The Magic Quarter is the Forsaken center for arcane and demonic studies. Mages and warlocks train there, portal masters connect it to other cities, and tailors weave enchanted cloth.",al={"what is magic quarter","magic quarter purpose","undercity magic district"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is there a Temple of the Damned in the Undercity?",a="The Scourge raised the Temple of the Damned when they carved the Undercity beneath the ruins of Capital City. Sylvanas and her free-willed Forsaken seized the subterranean complex and repurposed its existing buildings for their spellcasters.",al={"temple of the damned undercity","why temple of the damned here","scourge building undercity"}},{q="Who can be trained in the Magic Quarter?",a="Mages, warlocks, and demon trainers teach in the Magic Quarter. Portal specialists and tailors also train practitioners in transport and craft.",al={"trainers in magic quarter","who trains here","magic quarter classes"},gp=true},{q="Where is the Magic Quarter located?",a="The Magic Quarter occupies the Undercity's northeastern quadrant, across the central ring from the Apothecarium.",al={"where is magic quarter","magic quarter location","find magic quarter"},gp=true},{q="What is the Magic Quarter?",a="The Magic Quarter is the northeastern district of the Undercity, serving as the heart of the Forsaken's arcane and occult research. Towering over the quadrant sits an ominous Temple of the Damned, repurposed from Scourge architecture to serve the dark spellcasters, scholars, and weavers who pledge their craft to the Banshee Queen.",al={"what is magic quarter","magic quarter undercity","undercity magic quarter"},it="place",add="f984761d"},{q="Why is it called the Magic Quarter?",a="The district takes its name directly from its primary function within the Undercity: it is the realm of Forsaken spellcraft. Here, practitioners of the arcane, summoners of demonic power, and weavers of enchanted cloth gather to hone their dark arts and conduct arcane experiments in service of Lady Sylvanas.",al={"why is it called magic quarter","magic quarter name origin","magic quarter name meaning"},it="name",add="cec11eb0"},{q="Is the Magic Quarter dangerous?",a="For loyal subjects of the Forsaken and their Horde allies, the Magic Quarter is secure. However, it is thick with volatile arcane energies, summoned fel entities, and grim rituals. Reckless outsiders or enemies of the Dark Lady who trespass beneath the Temple of the Damned will quickly find themselves overwhelmed by its resident warlocks and mages.",al={"is magic quarter dangerous","magic quarter danger","is undercity magic quarter safe"},it="danger",add="8725bde7"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can study arcane arts in the Magic Quarter and learn teleportation routes linking the Undercity with the wider Horde.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can summon demonic minions and hone shadow magic in the Temple of the Damned, away from the Alliance's judgment."},kw={"forsaken","mage","magic quarter","portal trainer","tailoring","temple of the damned","undercity","warlock"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},src={"Magic Quarter"}}
E["subzone:rogues-quarter"] = {t="subzone",n="Rogues' Quarter",z="undercity",s="Scouts, assassins, and underworld operatives gather in the Rogues' Quarter, in the Undercity's southeastern wing. Craftsmen there support their covert work.",h="Scouts, assassins, and underworld operatives gather in the Rogues' Quarter, in the Undercity's southeastern...",sec={{t="Shadows of the Undercity",b="Survivors skilled in stealth gather in the Rogues' Quarter, deep in the Undercity's southeastern wing. Many served the Kingdom of Lordaeron in life as thieves, cutpurses, or silent blades. In death, they use their skills with stealth, poisons, and misdirection to defend the fledgling nation from the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade. Operatives sharpen daggers, brew toxins, and hone clandestine skills in this covert haven.",sp=0},{t="Tools of the Trade",b="Specialized trades in the Rogues' Quarter support undercover survival. Artisans teach travelers leatherworking and skinning, turning raw hides into light, silent armor. Tinkers work at engineering benches, while field medics and apothecaries teach first aid. Poison vendors stationed nearby supply lethal reagents for covert work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Rogues' Quarter located?",a="The Rogues' Quarter lies in the southeastern section of the Undercity's outer ring, past the Trade Quarter.",al={"rogues quarter location","where is rogues quarter","undercity rogues quarter map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What trainers can be found here?",a="The quarter has rogue trainers and instructors for leatherworking, skinning, engineering, and first aid. Poison vendors are stationed nearby to supply reagents.",al={"rogues quarter trainers","undercity rogue trainer","who trains in rogues quarter"},it="residents",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken maintain a dedicated district for rogues?",a="The Forsaken rely on espionage, assassination, and hit-and-run tactics to defend their territory from the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade, so covert operatives are vital to their survival.",al={"why do forsaken need rogues","forsaken assassins","undercity rogue lore"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Rogues' Quarter?",a="The Rogues' Quarter is the southeastern district of the Undercity, carved into the subterranean ruins beneath Lordaeron. It serves as the domain for the Forsaken's rogues' guild and their network of shadowy operatives. Beyond espionage and stealth, the quarter hosts specialized craftsmen, poisoners, leatherworkers, skinners, and engineers who support the clandestine efforts of the Forsaken.",al={"what is rogues quarter","rogues quarter undercity","about rogues quarter"},it="place",add="4d735fe6"},{q="Is the Rogues' Quarter dangerous?",a="If you walk here as an ally of the Forsaken and the Horde, the Rogues' Quarter poses no outward physical threat. However, it is populated by assassins, thieves, and covert agents who thrive on deception and secrecy. Lingering too long or prying into the business of the guild's poisoners and spies is never wise, as the district's residents are trained to eliminate threats without leaving a trace.",al={"is rogues quarter safe","danger rogues quarter","rogues quarter hostiles"},it="danger",add="8086d959"},{q="Why is it called the Rogues' Quarter?",a="The district takes its name from the rogues' guild that established its base within these dim halls. It gathers the Forsaken's scouts, infiltrators, and cutthroats under one roof, housing the instructors, poison vendors, and craftsmen who supply their lethal craft.",al={"why is it called rogues quarter","rogues quarter name origin","name rogues quarter"},it="name",add="e71830ac"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="For Forsaken and Horde assassins, the Rogues' Quarter is the premier hub for mastering stealth, learning combat techniques, and stocking up on lethal poison reagents.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can visit the Rogues' Quarter to learn schematics and craft bombs, gadgets, and mechanical tools favored by undercover agents."},kw={"engineering","forsaken","leatherworking","poison vendor","rogue trainer","rogues quarter","rogues' quarter","skinning","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},src={"Rogues' Quarter"}}
E["subzone:royal-quarter"] = {t="subzone",n="Royal Quarter",z="undercity",s="In the Royal Quarter, Sylvanas Windrunner directs the Forsaken from her throne. Varimathras stands at her side, while Royal Dreadguards protect the seat of power beneath the Undercity.",h="In the Royal Quarter, Sylvanas Windrunner directs the Forsaken from her throne.",sec={{t="The Seat of the Dark Lady",b="The Royal Quarter, also called the Hall of the Dark Lady, is where the Forsaken make their military and political decisions. Sylvanas Windrunner holds court in its vast chamber beneath the Undercity, working for the survival of her free-willed undead and the destruction of the Scourge. Royal Dreadguards keep watch along the dais, protecting their queen from uninvited visitors and would-be assassins.",sp=0},{t="A Dangerous Alliance",b="Varimathras, a nathrezim, stands beside Sylvanas in the heart of the Undercity. During the civil war in the ruins of Lordaeron, he sided with her to save his own life and pledged loyalty to her cause. From the Royal Quarter, he commands deathstalkers and coordinates defenses across the realm. His tactical skill serves the Forsaken, but his demonic nature makes many Horde allies wary of his true allegiance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who rules from the Royal Quarter?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen, rules the Forsaken from the Royal Quarter. The nathrezim Varimathras stands beside her, having pledged loyalty during the reconquest of Lordaeron.",al={"who is in the royal quarter","undercity throne room leader","who leads undercity"},it="residents"},{q="Why is there a dreadlord standing in the throne room?",a="Varimathras surrendered to Sylvanas Windrunner during the reconquest of Capital City, then betrayed his brothers Detheroc and Balnazzar. He saved his own life by swearing loyalty to Sylvanas, and now acts as her enforcer and master of scouts.",al={"why is varimathras here","dreadlord in undercity","why is demon in royal quarter"}},{q="What are the Royal Dreadguards?",a="The Royal Dreadguards are elite Forsaken chosen to protect Lady Sylvanas and the Royal Quarter. They are among the Undercity's most disciplined and lethal defenders.",al={"dreadguards","undercity throne room guards","royal quarter guards"}},{q="What other function does this chamber serve?",a="The Royal Quarter is also an audience chamber for the Dark Lady and Varimathras, and houses battlemasters. They coordinate Horde combatants for foreign campaigns and strategic skirmishes across Azeroth.",al={"what else is in royal quarter","royal quarter purpose","battlemasters royal quarter"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Royal Quarter?",a="The Royal Quarter, also known as the Hall of the Dark Lady, is the grand seat of power within the Undercity. Found deep beneath the ruins of Lordaeron, this cavernous throne room serves as the command center where Lady Sylvanas Windrunner guides the Forsaken, surrounded by her most trusted protectors and advisors.",al={"what is royal quarter","royal quarter undercity","hall of the dark lady"},it="place",add="8b23b6f3"},{q="Is the Royal Quarter dangerous?",a="For champions of the Horde, the chamber is a secure sanctuary, heavily defended by towering Royal Dreadguards. However, any trespassing Alliance intruders will find it exceptionally deadly, as both the Banshee Queen herself and the Nathrezim Varimathras stand ready to obliterate any who dare threaten the heart of the Forsaken realm.",al={"is royal quarter safe","danger in royal quarter","royal quarter hostile"},it="danger",add="698c5316"},{q="Why is it called the Royal Quarter?",a="The district takes its name from its role as the seat of royalty and supreme command in the subterranean capital. Here, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner rules her kingdom as the sovereign of the free undead, styling the chamber as her personal royal court.",al={"why is it called royal quarter","royal quarter name meaning","why royal quarter"},it="name",add="199248c7"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the Royal Quarter is the heart of their independence. Sylvanas Windrunner and her dreadlord lieutenant chart the future of their liberated people there.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde envoys visiting the Royal Quarter often regard the Dark Lady's nathrezim councilor with deep suspicion. They question the wisdom of trusting a demon in the heart of a Horde capital."},kw={"banshee queen","hall of the dark lady","royal dreadguard","royal quarter","sylvanas windrunner","throne room","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"zone:undercity","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","npc:varimathras","quest:1886","topic:horde","topic:burning-legion"},src={"Royal Quarter"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-lordaeron"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Lordaeron",z="undercity",s="At the Ruins of Lordaeron, the hollowed surface of Capital City guards the way into the Undercity. Once the heart of humanity’s northern empire, the city fell when Prince Arthas murdered his father and unleashed the Scourge.",h="At the Ruins of Lordaeron, the hollowed surface of Capital City guards the way into the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Fallen Empire's Gateway",b="Capital City once united the northern realms under King Terenas Menethil II. Its splendor ended when Prince Arthas returned from Northrend with Frostmourne, the cursed runeblade. Celebration gave way to slaughter. Arthas slew his father on the throne, and the Scourge ruled the city as it rotted.\n\nAfter civil war tore the Scourge apart, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner claimed the devastated palace. She secured the surface and expanded the crypts and dungeons below into the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of Betrayal",b="The palace still bears the psychic wound of its violent fall. In the entryway and courtyards, travelers hear celebration bells, the murmurs of adoring crowds, and the chilling exchange between Arthas and his father before the regicide.\n\nBlood still stains the grand throne room floor. Those with magical detection can glimpse spectral citizens reliving the afternoon their prince doomed them all.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do I hear bells and whispers when walking through the entrance?",a="The slaughter of King Terenas and his city left a psychic imprint on the stone. At the outer gate and shattered throne room, you can hear phantom bells, spectral cheers, and Terenas and Arthas's final conversation echoing across time.",al={"creepy sounds lordaeron","throne room whispers","haunted castle sounds"}},{q="Who rules the ruins today?",a="The Forsaken hold and patrol the surface ruins under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Sylvanas and her court dwell in the Undercity below, and the ruins guard the entrance to her subterranean realm.",al={"who owns lordaeron ruins","who controls ruins of lordaeron"},it="in_charge"},{q="What happened to the people who used to live here?",a="Most inhabitants were slaughtered when Arthas unleashed the Scourge upon the city. Many were raised as mindless undead, then broke free and joined Sylvanas as the Forsaken. Others remain unseen spirits drifting through the palace courtyards.",al={"where did lordaeron people go","what happened to capital city humans"},it="people"},{q="What is the dark stain in the throne room?",a="The dark stain on the royal dais is King Terenas Menethil II's dried blood. His son Arthas spilled it when he drove Frostmourne through the king's heart.",al={"blood on throne room floor","stain in lordaeron throne room"},it="history"},{q="What is the Ruins of Lordaeron?",a="These shattered ramparts and grand halls are all that remain of Capital City, the magnificent seat of the fallen human kingdom of Lordaeron. Once the heart of the Alliance during the Second War, the city collapsed when Prince Arthas Menethil betrayed his realm and unleashed the Scourge. Today, the surface palace sits crumbling and haunted, serving as the gateway to the sprawling Forsaken subterranean metropolis known as the Undercity.",al={"what are the ruins of lordaeron","ruins of lordaeron overview","capital city ruins lore"},it="place",add="d8b1c653"},{q="Why is Lordaeron in ruins?",a="Lordaeron fell to treachery from within. Crown Prince Arthas Menethil, corrupted by the cursed blade Frostmourne, returned from Northrend under the banner of the Lich King. After slaying his father, King Terenas, Arthas and his undead Scourge slaughtered the populace and shattered the city's defenses. Subsequent clashes involving dreadlords, surviving Alliance resistance forces, and Sylvanas Windrunner's Forsaken completed the ruin of the surface city.",al={"why is lordaeron destroyed","how was lordaeron destroyed","why is lordaeron ruined"},it="ruin",add="b22541a4"},{q="Is the Ruins of Lordaeron dangerous?",a="For champions of the Horde, the surface ruins are secure, as Forsaken guards patrol the courtyards and passages leading into the Undercity. However, Alliance travelers will find it fiercely hostile territory crawling with Forsaken sentries. The area is also spiritually unsettled, echoing with tragic phantom whispers and invisible ghosts of slaughtered citizens, while vile Scourge and beasts prowl the surrounding Tirisfal countryside.",al={"ruins of lordaeron danger","is ruins of lordaeron safe","are ruins of lordaeron hostile"},it="danger",add="e6ebc4a5"},{q="Why is it called the Ruins of Lordaeron?",a="The site was originally Capital City, the majestic center of the Kingdom of Lordaeron. Following the utter annihilation of the realm and the slaughter of its people by the Scourge, only the cracked marble walls, shattered throne room, and crumbling courtyards remain. It is named to mark the fallen majesty and tragic devastation of humanity's greatest northern kingdom.",al={"ruins of lordaeron name origin","why ruins of lordaeron","where does ruins of lordaeron get its name"},it="name",add="39a2d118"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, these ruined ramparts are your ancestral home. The living kingdom that birthed you once ruled here; now its halls guard the Undercity and the Banshee Queen.",["race:Human"]="As a human, these halls recall the greatest betrayal in your history. Prince Arthas shattered the Alliance of Lordaeron and left humanity's jewel in the hands of the dead."},kw={"arthas","capital city","haunted","lordaeron","palace","scourge","sylvanas","terenas","throne room","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:lordaeron","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:forsaken","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand"},src={"Ruins of Lordaeron"}}
E["subzone:sewers"] = {t="subzone",n="Sewers",z="undercity",s="Beneath the hills west of Lordaeron's ruined palace, the Sewers offer a second way into the Undercity. Their stone passage carries bat handlers and travelers past the elevators descending from the throne room.",h="Beneath the hills west of Lordaeron's ruined palace, the Sewers offer a second way into the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Backdoor into the Catacombs",b="The Sewers once drained Lordaeron's royal capital. Now Sylvanas Windrunner's Forsaken fold those old stone channels into the Undercity's defenses. The passage opens west of the surface ruins, near a Scarlet Watchtower in Tirisfal Glades, then slopes directly inside. Forsaken bat handlers fly riders through the cavernous conduit into the Undercity's subterranean rings, avoiding the slow cage lifts. The route also skirts the fortified courtyards, leaving a dangerous weakness that hostile infiltrators seek to exploit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the sewer tunnel lead outside?",a="The sewer passage opens in the hills of Tirisfal Glades, west of the main gates to the Ruins of Lordaeron. The Scarlet Watchtower overlooking the lake is nearby.",al={"undercity sewer exit","where do sewers go","sewer back entrance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why would anyone use the sewers instead of the main entrance?",a="The main entrance descends from the palace ruins by iron cage elevators, which can be slow and dangerous during an attack. The Sewers provide a direct, sloped route for Forsaken bat traffic and a quick way out without waiting for the lifts.",al={"why use sewers","sewers vs elevators","undercity backdoor"},it="purpose"},{q="Is the sewer safe from Alliance raiders?",a="No. The Sewers bypass Lordaeron's fortified gatehouse and throne room, making them a breach point for Alliance scouts and strike teams trying to enter the Forsaken capital unseen.",al={"alliance attack sewers","is sewer guarded","undercity sewer defense"},it="danger"},{q="What are the Sewers of the Undercity?",a="The Sewers serve as a sprawling drainage system beneath the Ruins of Lordaeron that empties out into Tirisfal Glades, just west of the palace gates. Rather than relying on the precarious palace elevators, many Forsaken travelers and bat handlers utilize these foul tunnels as an alternate conduit directly into the subterranean heart of the Undercity.",al={"what are the sewers","undercity sewers","sewers undercity"},it="place",add="833a18e0"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the Sewers are an essential lifeline and flight corridor, keeping the Undercity connected to the rest of Lordaeron without crowding the courtyard elevators.",["faction:Alliance"]="If you assault the Forsaken capital, the Sewers offer a covert route past the heavily defended surface ruins."},kw={"backdoor","bat handler","drainage","flight path","lordaeron","sewers","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","zone:tirisfal","topic:lordaeron","topic:alliance"},src={"Sewers"}}
E["subzone:trade-quarter"] = {t="subzone",n="Trade Quarter",z="undercity",s="Trade Quarter draws the Undercity’s commerce and civic life beneath the Ruins of Lordaeron. Its bank, auction house, and other services serve the Forsaken capital, while corridors link it to the surrounding districts.",h="Trade Quarter draws the Undercity’s commerce and civic life beneath the Ruins of Lordaeron.",sec={{t="Heart of the Crypts",b="You step from the lifts beneath the Ruins of Lordaeron into the Trade Quarter’s broad, circular halls. Canals of noxious runoff circle the central platform, crossed by bridges. The city’s coffers and bank rest there, while vendors, guild registrars, and auctioneers work along the terraces. At the inn, wooden caskets replace soft beds. Stone archways lead into the other districts, drawing the Undercity’s business through its center.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Trade Quarter located?",a="The Trade Quarter lies at the center of the Undercity. Lifts beneath the Ruins of Lordaeron carry you from the surface into its upper ring.",al={"trade quarter location","how to find trade quarter","where is trade quarter"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services are found in the Trade Quarter?",a="The Trade Quarter holds the Undercity’s central bank, an auction house along the outer ring, and the primary inn. You can also find a bat handler for air travel, guild registrars, and trade trainers, including the city’s cooking mentor.",al={"trade quarter services","what is in trade quarter","undercity bank location"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why are there coffins in the inn?",a="The Forsaken need no true sleep, and many keep habits suited to their undead condition. The inn offers plain, unlined wooden caskets for comfort, though they can unsettle living visitors.",al={"undercity inn coffins","why caskets in inn","undercity beds"}},{q="Who is the vendor lurking beneath the bridges?",a="Jeremiah Payson sells live pet cockroaches beneath one of the central bridges leading to the bank. Other merchants above sell weapons and trade goods.",al={"jeremiah payson","cockroach guy undercity","who sells cockroaches"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Trade Quarter?",a="The Trade Quarter serves as the central hub and beating heart of the Undercity. Positioned immediately beyond the elevators descending from the ruins of Capital City above, this tiered circular chamber connects directly to all other quarters via winding canals. It functions as the realm's bustling center of commerce, housing the grand bank vault, general vendors, guild services, and the city's primary gathering spaces.",al={"what is the trade quarter","trade quarter undercity","undercity center"},it="place",add="d7706923"},{q="What happened to create the Trade Quarter?",a="Originally carved beneath the royal palace and capital of Lordaeron, these subterranean halls once held dungeons, crypts, and sewers. Following the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge and Prince Arthas, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner led the Forsaken in reclaiming the territory. They expanded and refashioned the central subterranean chambers into a fortified city center to conduct trade and govern their new sovereign realm.",al={"trade quarter history","how was trade quarter made","history of trade quarter"},it="history",add="b95b8a75"},{q="Is the Trade Quarter dangerous?",a="For members of the Horde and allies of the Dark Lady, the Trade Quarter is one of the safest places in the realm, heavily guarded by towering Abominations and royal sentries. However, it is utterly lethal to members of the Alliance or uninvited trespassers, who will be slain on sight the moment they descend from the ruins above.",al={"is trade quarter safe","is trade quarter dangerous","threats trade quarter"},it="danger",add="5eb4f186"},{q="Why is it called the Trade Quarter?",a="It earns its name as the foremost commercial district of the Forsaken capital. The central vault houses the city coffer and bank, while surrounding rings and tiers host merchant stalls, auctioneers, craft suppliers, and guild liaisons, facilitating all major business transactions throughout the kingdom.",al={"why is it called trade quarter","trade quarter name","why trade quarter"},it="name",add="49015933"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you see the Forsaken restore civilized order in the Trade Quarter. Their underground market helps fund their survival.",["faction:Horde"]="As an Orc, Tauren, or Troll emissary arriving in Tirisfal Glades, you find a foreign, shadowy market at the heart of your northern allies’ capital."},kw={"auction house","bank","bat handler","caskets","inn","jeremiah payson","trade quarter","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:lordaeron","topic:horde"},src={"Trade Quarter"}}
E["subzone:war-quarter"] = {t="subzone",n="War Quarter",z="undercity",s="In the War Quarter, Lordaeron's Forsaken hone weapons and shadow magic for their fledgling kingdom. Training halls, weapon masters, and heavy industry fill the Undercity's northwest.",h="In the War Quarter, Lordaeron's Forsaken hone weapons and shadow magic for their fledgling kingdom.",sec={{t="The Forsaken Garrison",b="Rank-and-file guards and elite champions drill beneath the War Quarter's gloomy stone arches. There, ruthless iron warfare meets the chilling rites of shadow. The Altar of Darkness stands at its heart.",sp=0},{t="Forge and Steel",b="Warrior and priest guilds make the War Quarter the heart of Undercity's wartime production. Blacksmiths and smelters ring the stone with their labor as weapon masters prepare blades and armor. Iron forged deep underground arms the forces defending Lordaeron's ruins from the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the War Quarter?",a="The War Quarter is the Undercity's military headquarters. Its training grounds serve warriors and priests, while blacksmithing and mining centers keep the Forsaken army armed and armored.",al={"what is war quarter","war quarter purpose","why visit war quarter"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are priests located in the War Quarter?",a="Forsaken priests largely practice the discipline of the Shadow, wielding it beside warriors rather than tending pastoral sanctuaries. Their place near the martial forces and the Altar of Darkness binds faith closely to the Forsaken's defense.",al={"undead priest location","why are priests in war quarter","priest trainers undercity"},it="people"},{q="What is the Altar of Darkness?",a="The Altar of Darkness is a focal point of dark spiritual power in the War Quarter. It is tied to the Forsaken's dark rites and training, and anchors the shadow magic their priests and champions wield.",al={"altar of darkness undercity","altar in war quarter"},it="place"},{q="Where is the War Quarter located in the Undercity?",a="The War Quarter occupies the northwest of the Undercity's circular layout, northwest of the central Trade Quarter. It lies between the Magic Quarter to the east and the Apothecarium to the south.",al={"where is war quarter","war quarter location","war quarter directions"},gp=true},{q="What is the War Quarter?",a="The War Quarter is the northwestern district of the Undercity, serving as the primary bastion and training ground for the Forsaken military. Deep beneath the ruins of Lordaeron, its cavernous halls ring with the clash of steel and dark chants, housing warrior barracks, martial instructors, and the Forsaken priests who practice the arts of shadow.",al={"what is war quarter","war quarter undercity","undercity war quarter"},it="place",add="89f17781"},{q="Why is it called the War Quarter?",a="It earned its name by serving as the martial heart of Lady Sylvanas's domain. Here, the Forsaken organize their standing army, drill soldiers, sharpen blades, and prepare the tactics necessary to wage war against the Scourge, the Scarlet Crusade, and any other threats to their sovereignty.",al={"why called war quarter","war quarter name","why war quarter"},it="name",add="e554fcad"},{q="Is the War Quarter dangerous?",a="For champions of the Horde, the district is safe and heavily guarded by elite Forsaken forces and Deathguard sentries. To outsiders, the Alliance, or agents of the Scourge, however, stepping into the War Quarter means facing an armed garrison ready to strike down intruders without hesitation.",al={"is war quarter dangerous","danger war quarter","is the war quarter safe"},it="danger",add="d58a257c"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, the War Quarter is your primary haven in the Undercity. Weapon masters, advanced combat instructors, and heavy armories prepare you for Lordaeron's brutal frontline battles.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you find training masters and high-heat anvils in the War Quarter. It is the central hub for smiths forging munitions and plate for the Forsaken war effort."},kw={"altar of darkness","barracks","blacksmithing","forsaken","priest trainer","undercity","war quarter","warrior trainer"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},src={"War Quarter"}}
E["zone:undercity"] = {t="city",n="Undercity",z="undercity",s="Beneath the shattered ruins of Lordaeron's capital lies the Undercity, the dark stronghold of the Forsaken. Lady Sylvanas Windrunner took it from the Scourge, and made it a sanctuary no enemy can breach. Today it is the seat of Forsaken power. And it is the Horde's great bastion, in the north of the Eastern Kingdoms.",h="Beneath the shattered ruins of Lordaeron's capital lies the Undercity, the dark stronghold of the Forsaken.",sec={{t="From Royal Crypts to Scourge Redoubt",b="Long before the plague, the catacombs and sewers beneath the palace were already called the Undercity. Nobles lay entombed there, beside the poorest people of the realm. And there lay the kingdom's deepest prisons. Even Orgrim Doomhammer, the former Warchief, was held in them before he escaped.\n\nIn the Third War, Arthas Menethil murdered King Terenas, and laid waste to the capital. Then the prince set his undead servants to dig. They widened the old passages into a fortified seat of Scourge rule. But the Scourge never saw their dark capital finished.",sp=0},{t="Rise of the Forsaken",b="When the Lich King's power waned, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner broke free of his will, and took thousands of undead with her. She ambushed Arthas, and he fled back to Northrend. A vicious civil war followed, against the Scourge remnants, the dreadlords and the human resistance. Out of it, Sylvanas claimed the half-finished catacombs. She named her people the Forsaken, and oversaw years of labor on the sprawling city.",sp=0},{t="Architecture of the Damned",b="The city spreads in rings around the Trade Quarter, and great lifts join it to the palace ruins above. Around it lie the other quarters, and among them is the toxic Apothecarium. There the Royal Apothecary Society brews virulent plagues, beside canals of green slime. Deeper still, the Banshee Queen holds court in the Royal Quarter, with her dreadlord commander Varimathras. Legions of towering abominations stand guard.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Undercity before the undead took it over?",a="Beneath the palace of Lordaeron lay the ancient crypts of human royalty, along with the city's dungeon complex and vast sewer network. It housed prisoners of war, including Orgrim Doomhammer, as well as destitute citizens living in the subterranean shadows. The dungeons beneath the palace were already called the Undercity. After sacking the capital, Prince Arthas began turning these catacombs into a Scourge fortress before Sylvanas captured them.",al={"undercity origins","what was undercity originally","lordaeron sewers history"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the city built underground instead of on the surface?",a="The surface city of Lordaeron was utterly ruined during the Third War, making it difficult to defend against the Scarlet Crusade, Scourge forces, and Alliance survivors. The subterranean tunnels offered natural fortification, choke points, and secrecy, allowing the Forsaken to complete the Scourge's initial construction and thrive unseen.",al={"why live underground","why not rebuild lordaeron","why undercity beneath ruins"},it="why_here"},{q="Who rules the Undercity?",a="The city is ruled by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen and Queen of the Forsaken. She governs from the Royal Quarter, guarded by Forsaken royal sentries and her subjugated dreadlord lieutenant, Varimathras. Sylvanas broke free of the Lich King's will after the battle of Mount Hyjal. The city also has a War Quarter, Rogues' Quarter, and Magic Quarter.",al={"who is leader of undercity","undercity ruler","who runs undercity"},it="leader"},{q="What is King Terenas's memorial in the ruins above?",a="Above the city's main lifts sits a stone memorial for the slain King Terenas Menethil II. It does not contain his body, as his corpse was cremated and his ashes discarded during Kel'Thuzad's resurrection. Surviving Alliance humans bravely carved the monument amidst the ruins so the memory of Lordaeron's last true king would endure.",al={"king terenas tomb","lordaeron throne room grave","who built the tomb above undercity"}},{q="What are the strange noises in the Lordaeron throne room?",a="In the ruined throne room above the Undercity lifts, spectral echoes of the past still linger. Visitors standing in the center can hear faint phantom sounds: the celebratory bells and rose petals of Arthas's return, the warning words of the prophet Medivh, and the final conversation between King Terenas and his patricidal son.",al={"ghost sounds throne room","throne room whispering","voices in lordaeron throne room"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken allow other Horde members here?",a="The Forsaken formed an alliance of convenience with Warchief Thrall's Horde for survival, surrounded as they are by hostile Scarlet zealots and Scourge legions. While living Horde races find the toxic fumes and alchemical rivers stifling, emissaries and travelers are allowed access to foster diplomatic and military ties.",al={"why are orcs in undercity","horde in undercity","why is undercity part of horde"},it="allies"},{q="What is the Undercity?",a="The Undercity is the subterranean capital of the Forsaken, built directly beneath the shattered ruins of Capital City in Tirisfal Glades. Carved out of ancient royal crypts, sewers, and catacombs, it was expanded by Prince Arthas as a Scourge stronghold before Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and her renegade undead seized it during the civil war. Today, it stands as a fortified sanctuary for free-willed undead, crisscrossed by toxic sludge and guarded vigilantly against all living intruders.",al={"what is undercity","tell me about undercity","undercity lore"},it="place",add="a590d153"},{q="What happened to the old king of Lordaeron?",a="King Terenas Menethil II was murdered in the throne room directly above this city by his own son, Prince Arthas. After returning from Northrend corrupted by the runeblade Frostmourne, Arthas struck down his father and unleashed the Scourge upon the kingdom. Terenas's ashes were later stolen by the death knight to resurrect Kel'Thuzad, leaving behind only the memorial stone and the dried trail of blood you can still see near the ruined throne.",al={"king terenas fate","what happened to king terenas","who killed king terenas"},it="history",add="c51b16b2"},{q="Who was Arthas?",a="Arthas Menethil was the Crown Prince of Lordaeron and a celebrated paladin of the Silver Hand. Desperate to stop the Plague of Undeath sweeping his homeland, his crusade turned ruthless and fanatical. In Northrend, he claimed the cursed runeblade Frostmourne, which devoured his soul and made him the dread champion of the Lich King. He returned home only to butcher his father, raze Lordaeron, and eventually travel back north to merge with the Frozen Throne.",al={"who is arthas","prince arthas lore","arthas menethil"},it="history",add="c11144c7"},{q="Who is Sylvanas Windrunner?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner was once the valiant Ranger-General of Silvermoon, defending Quel'Thalas against the Scourge during the Third War. When she fell, Arthas tore her soul from her corpse and twisted her into a banshee to torment her. When the Lich King's grip weakened, she broke free, reclaimed her physical form, and rallied other independent undead into the Forsaken. Now she reigns as their Banshee Queen from the Royal Quarter.",al={"who is the banshee queen","sylvanas lore","who is sylvanas"},it="leader",add="7f6bbd49",nx={11}},{q="Why is Sylvanas called the Dark Lady?",a="The Forsaken honor Sylvanas as the Dark Lady because she liberated them from the mindless thrall of the Lich King and gave them shelter when the rest of Azeroth sought their total extermination. Revered alongside her title as the Banshee Queen, the moniker reflects both her shadowy mastery over death and the fierce, unyielding devotion of her undead subjects.",al={"why dark lady","dark lady title sylvanas","dark lady meaning"},it="identity",add="2a8de90f"},{q="Why are the Forsaken part of the Horde?",a="Surrounded by hostile Scarlet Crusaders, relentless Scourge, and vengeful Alliance remnants, the Forsaken could not survive alone in Lordaeron. Lady Sylvanas reached out across the sea to Warchief Thrall, forging a pragmatic alliance of convenience. The Horde gained a crucial military foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms, while the Forsaken secured essential reinforcements and political legitimacy in their war for survival.",al={"why forsaken horde","undead join horde","forsaken horde alliance"},it="arrival",add="84f18f47"},{q="What is the Scourge and are they still nearby?",a="The Scourge is the vast, ravenous army of mindless undead created by the Burning Legion and ruled by the Lich King from Northrend. Though the Forsaken wrested the Undercity and Tirisfal from their grasp, the Scourge remains an immediate, lethal danger. Their legions still choke the nearby Plaguelands under Kel'Thuzad's command and infest abandoned farmsteads and crypts across the glades.",al={"is the scourge nearby","what is the scourge","scourge in lordaeron"},it="threat",add="71200045",nx={14,15}},{q="Where is the Lich King now?",a="The Lich King resides atop the Frozen Throne in the distant, icy wastes of Northrend. Following the civil war in the Plaguelands, Prince Arthas fled Lordaeron to protect his weakening master, ascending the glacier and merging their essences into a single terrifying entity. From that arctic bastion, his chilling gaze still watches over Azeroth.",al={"where is lich king","lich king location","where is arthas now"},it="threat",add="501548ab"},{q="Who are the Scarlet Crusade?",a="The Scarlet Crusade is a fanatical order of human zealots born from the ruins of Lordaeron's defense. Blinded by their righteous hatred of the undead, they make no distinction between mindless Scourge and free-willed Forsaken, viewing anyone tainted by undeath—and any living outsider who tolerates them—as vile abominations fit only for the pyre. Their primary bastion in Tirisfal is the Scarlet Monastery.",al={"who is scarlet crusade","scarlet crusaders","scarlet crusade lore"},it="threat",add="4cc7f971"},{q="Is the Undercity dangerous?",a="It is extraordinarily dangerous, especially for the living. Channels of raw alchemical waste and poisonous sludge run through the city streets, filling the cavernous halls with toxic fumes that make breathing hazardous for flesh-and-blood visitors. Beneath the paved quarters lie infested sewers, and deeper still are secretive experiments where dark alchemy and ruthless assassinations are plotted daily.",al={"is undercity safe","danger in undercity","undercity dangers"},it="danger",add="271820ed"},{q="How did I end up in Undercity?",a="As a Forsaken, your path naturally led here after awakening from death in Deathknell and proving your loyalty through Tirisfal Glades, following the roads past Brill to descend beneath the shattered ruins of Capital City. If you hail from Kalimdor or distant lands, you likely arrived aboard a Horde zeppelin docking at the towers just outside the capital, or trekked across the blighted countryside. The Undercity stands as the Horde's primary stronghold in northern Lordaeron, offering shelter and purpose beneath the ancient palace catacombs.",al={"how did i get here","how did i reach undercity","how do you get to undercity"},it="arrival",add="2539a3c3"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Undercity?",a="You are here to aid the Forsaken and muster the strength of the Horde against the perils surrounding Lordaeron. Within the city's concentric quarters, you can consult class trainers, acquire supplies, and consult the dark researchers of the Royal Apothecary Society. Beyond tending to your trade, your duty is to take up assignments for Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and her lieutenants. The Forsaken fight a war on multiple fronts: scouring the remnants of the mindless Scourge, driving back the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, and securing safe ground for the free-willed undead to endure.",al={"what am i doing here","what should i do in undercity","why am i here"},it="purpose",add="b63c4cf2"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Undercity is your sovereign sanctuary and homeland, carved out by your own hands after breaking the Lich King's iron grip on your mind.",["faction:Horde"]="As the Horde's primary foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms, the Undercity secures zeppelin links directly back to Durotar and Grom'gol Base Camp.",["race:Human"]="Beneath the soil of your fallen ancestral kingdom lies a grim perversion of Lordaeron's royal crypts, occupied by the walking corpses of your former brethren.",["race:Orc"]="Deep within these very dungeons, the legendary Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer was once imprisoned by the Alliance of Lordaeron before making his historic escape."},kw={"apothecarium","arthas","forsaken","lordaeron","scourge","sylvanas","terenas","tirisfal","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"npc:sylvanas-windrunner","topic:forsaken","zone:tirisfal","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge","topic:arthas-menethil","subzone:apothecarium"},src={"Undercity"}}
